In addition, Senior Minister Kun Kim also urged the search and identification of homeless veterans to provide housing for them as well as provide land, which is the policy of the Royal Government.
Mr. Kun Kim also instructed the association officials throughout the province to work together to promote and prevent the encroachment on social land provided by the Royal Government to the association to be distributed to Cambodian veterans.
In addition to the above-mentioned priorities, Senior Minister Kun Kim also instructed the association's leading officials at both the central and provincial levels to work together to address the plight of veterans. In particular, be able to move to help each other when a family member of a veteran is suffering from illness and death.
In this meeting, Senior Minister Kun Kim expressed his strong expectation that all the leaders of the association and all relevant authorities will work hard in this new mandate to achieve the best results for the veterans. As a benefactor for the motherland. Minister of Cult announces to stop wearing pagoda license plates on cars contrary to the law
The announcement of the Minister of Cult, which was received by Fresh News on July 18, 2020, after it was observed that there was a case of using a license plate with the name of the pagoda on the car, contrary to the spirit of the sub-decree on registration Provide vehicle identification card and equip vehicle license plate.
It should be informed that in relation to the use of the license plate with the name of the pagoda on the car, in the past, the police also stopped the car and confiscated the modified license plate. Most of these cars are known to be duty-free cars that Buddhists buy for monks to make it easier to get around.
The National Union Congress of Cambodia and the Sen Sok District Administration sprayed disinfectants on more than 200 rooms in workers' houses and in Khan Sangkat administrative buildings.
(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly of the National Trade Union of Cambodia, in cooperation with the administration of Khan Sen Sok, conducted a campaign to educate and spray disinfectants to prevent and prevent Kovid-19 infectious diseases at Khan / Sangkat Administration Building, Administration Building, Khan Party, Sangkat, and more than 200 rented rooms. Rooms for civil servants, people, workers in some villages, Sangkat Kork Khleang, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh.
Taking this opportunity, Mr. Tima Sophea, on behalf of the district authority, requested the people and workers to continue to fight against Kovid-19 by following the hygiene rules as instructed by the Ministry of Health.
Mr. Som Oun said that Kovid-19 is still a serious threat to human life in the world and there is no vaccine yet.
(Takeo): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Mr. Ouch Phea, Governor of Takeo Province, this morning, July 18, 2020, inspected the location where the reception of Samdech Techo Hun Sen will be held. The Prime Minister of Cambodia, who will visit and evaluate the activities of the people in Prey Kabas district, Takeo province on July 21.
The visit to the venue for the reception of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was also accompanied by Mr. Ngin Chhay, Delegate of the Royal Government of Cambodia in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Agriculture, Director of the Department of Agriculture and Forestry of Takeo Province. Leaders of the Department of Rice Crops, Department of Agricultural Engineering and many colleagues.
(Prey Veng): Mr. Prum Sokha, Minister of Public Works, Representative of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, presided over the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of a school building with 5 classrooms, which is a precious gift from Samdech. Pong Puos Primary School is located in Pong Puos Village, Rong Damrey Commune, Ba Phnom District.
The ceremony took place on the morning of July 18, 2020, with the participation of all officials of the Ministry of Public Works, commune, district, authorities and local people, a total of 250 people.
Addressing the ceremony, Mr. Prum Sokha reminded the working group and local authorities to pay attention to follow the high recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister to continue to help the people, especially the poor. And vulnerable to overcoming all difficulties and shortcomings caused by the Kovid 19 crisis.
These include: Continuing vigilance, preventing the spread of coronavirus, distributing equity cards, receiving cash donations from the Royal Government properly, encouraging the cultivation of agriculture, aquaculture, animal husbandry and other local businesses. Etc.
After the traditional Buddhist celebration, donations of food, materials and budget were distributed to 60 poor families.
The National Health Commission said in its daily report that the latest outbreaks were found in Xinjiang, but no new cases were reported as of Friday. On the same day, 21 more patients were released from the hospital.
On this issue, the Prime Minister of the United Kingdom, Boris Johnson, said: "It is my sincere hope that we can reconsider the austerity measures and allow change to take place. "Normal returns gradually from next November, possibly before Christmas."
It should be noted that although the UK wants to remove additional restrictive measures, such as easing measures to keep the security gap in society, caution is still advised because models from some countries already exist, especially when they COVID-19 was thought to have been defeated, but the re-emergence of the most alarming.
Another 143 students and military students studying in Egypt and Russia are facilitated to return to Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): A total of 143 Cambodian military students and trainees studying in Egypt and Russia were facilitated by the Cambodian Embassy and arranged for their return to Cambodia.
Koy Kuong, spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, said that the 143 military students and trainees will fly on flight MH754 through Malaysia and arrive in Cambodia at 13:00 on the 19th. July 2020, tomorrow.
Please note that according to the principles and rules of the Ministry of Health, all passengers, both Cambodians and foreigners who come to Cambodia will be screened for Kovid 19. On board the plane, if anyone is diagnosed with Kovid 19, all passengers will be quarantined for 14 days at locations designated by the Ministry of Health.
However, if no one is found to be infected with Kovid 19, passengers will be allowed to return home, but they will also be required to perform self-medication at home.
The Ministry of Health has called on all foreign travelers to adhere to these rules and regulations to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in the country.
King orders appointment of National Anti-Corruption Council
(Phnom Penh): The King of Cambodia, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, has ordered the appointment of 11 members of the National Anti-Corruption Council for a new term.
Please note that the National Anti-Corruption Council is an anti-corruption body established by Royal Decree with the role of consulting and recommending anti-corruption work.
The Royal Decree stipulates that each member of the National Council Against Corruption must be a Cambodian by birth, have good morals and a clean reputation, have never been convicted of a felony or a crime, or have not gone bankrupt. Study and above, have at least 10 years of social work experience, at least 45 years old.
All members of the National Council Against Corruption are appointed by Royal Decree for a term of five years. The members of the National Anti-Corruption Council are defined as the chairperson with the rank of deputy prime minister, the deputy chairperson with the rank of senior minister and members with the rank of minister.
