Kratie Provincial Police: News on social media that a Prey Lang activist was shot dead, but the victim was drunk and fell on a motorcycle and died on his own
(Kratie): The Kratie Provincial Police on July 18, 2020, came out to confirm the information on the social network Facebook, which fabricated that a Prey Lang activist was shot dead in Sambo district, Kratie province, in a traffic accident that caused his death. .
Sen Sothea, a motorbike taxi driver named Heng Sros, left Man Thol Roratou's house at Ka Phluk point, Achen village, Kampong Cham commune, Sambo district, Kratie province. Suddenly, the motorbike fell into a ditch, seriously injuring Sen Sothea.
Heng Sros saw an unknown person walking down the frog, and he asked the frog reflector to take Sen Sothea to Nam Nak's house so that Nam Nak could contact him to rent a car to transport the victim to the hospital. Sambo Commune Health Center.
At the same time, the medical team also confirmed that the victim really died in a traffic accident, not because he was shot.
For this, the competent authorities are searching for more information. Director of Sre Ambel District Referral Hospital: Kovid-19 is still a concern, so do not neglect it
(Koh Kong): Dr. Hour Sok Hourn, Director of Sre Ambel District Referral Hospital, said that Kovid-19 disease is still a constant concern for the health of people living in remote areas or remote areas, so do not neglect Not at all.
Dr. Hour Sok Hourn However, the important thing is that the doctors have cooperated with the local authorities to disseminate the guidelines of the Royal Government, the Ministry of Health on health care, environmental sanitation to prevent Kovid-19 and other diseases. Well.
Dr. Hour Sok Hourn said that Kovid 19 is a vicious and widespread disease in the world and can be life-threatening very quickly. Therefore, we need to make people very careful because Kovid-19 has not disappeared from the world yet.
Dr. Hour Sok Hourn added that the follow-up of Dr. Chattalysak in Sre Ambel district did not have any symptoms of Kovid 19 because Dr. Chattalysak, the local authorities and the people cooperated well, especially the doctors. Local authorities play microphones every day and in practice ask him to wash his hands often with alcohol, soap and clean water and to stay healthy.
The doctor added: "People who come to see him in Sre Ambel District Referral Hospital, Koh Kong Province, every day, Dr. Chattalysak's team checks the temperature one by one to wash his hands, gel, soap, massage and let him sit. At a distance of 1.50 meters, patients who come to the hospital for medical treatment should follow the same procedure to prevent the spread of the disease in the case of Kovid 19.
(Prey Veng): A case of aggravated theft committed by a suspect named Pros Det, male, 22 years old, Sdao Kong village, Sdao Kong commune, Ba Phnom district, Prey Veng province, rented a motorbike for the victim, Sar Loeung, male, 48 years old, Kraing Kok village Kampong Soeng Commune, Preah Sdach District, Prey Veng Province.
This incident happened on July 18, 2020 at 08:40 in the morning at Prey Samlanh village, Samrong commune, Svay Antor district, Prey Veng province.
According to the authorities, the suspect rented a motorbike for the victim to drive in front of Sdao Kong commune, Ba Phnom district, to the Svay Antor roundabout.
Seeing a good opportunity, the suspect made an excuse to stop urinating and hit the victim with a stick on the victim, and the victim escaped and jumped off the motorcycle, then the suspect picked up the motorcycle and ran away.
After receiving the information, the district police force, under the direct command and direction of the inspector, chased and ambushed until 10:50 AM, then arrested the suspect at the Chinese canal in Prey Chhlong village, Pean Rong commune.
The suspect is currently being held at the Svay Antor District Police Inspectorate to be sent to the Office of Procedural Management. Thank you
(Prey Veng): Prey Veng is still the number one rice producer in the country, with about 78.6% of the population being farmers, and the farmers in this province have increased the harvest during the rainy season in 2020. More than 80% is equivalent to more than 200,000 hectares.
Mr. Ouk Samnang, Director of Prey Veng Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that the situation of rain-fed rice cultivation of the people in Prey Veng Province has been achieved by July 16, 2020, plowing speed 200,162 hectares, sowing a total of 200 rice. 162 hectares, of which light rice 57., 431 hectares, medium rice 111,081 hectares, heavy rice 31,647 hectares, accounting for 80.06%.
Factors that cause Prey Veng to get such a high yield in relation to the good geographical location and favorable climate, which allows farmers to grow rice in all seasons and is also the province with the highest rice yield in the country. Until now, in 2020, while in the past, only Battambang province.
It should be noted that the government considers agriculture as a priority sector that contributes to the development of the national economy and increase the income of the people.
At the same time, the Royal Government has ambitions to modernize the agricultural sector to make it more environmentally resilient, sustainable, and especially to transform the sector from subsistence agriculture to intensive agriculture, increase productivity, and diversify crops. Potential and market demand, including agro-commercial animal husbandry and aquaculture.
