(Phnom Penh): A brutal woman who brutally stabbed a 5-year-old girl in Borey Phop Thmey Chhouk Va 2 in Tek Panhna village, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh, could face at least 10 years in prison while the court Decided to charge her with torture and aggravated assault.
Kuch Kimlong, Spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, told Fresh News that Sok Keo Bandith, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, on the morning of July 18, 2020, decided to charge the woman with a raw heart. Liu Bunthoeun, 43, who stabbed a 5-year-old girl in the face with a knife for aggravated assault and torture, is aggravated under Article 211 of the Penal Code.
Article 211 of the Penal Code stipulates that torture and aggravated assault involving a victim is punishable by 10 to 20 years in prison if the act is committed on: * 1: A particularly vulnerable person Age of the person. * 2: Pregnant woman when the pregnancy is obvious or when the perpetrator knows. * 3: A person who is particularly weak due to illness or disability when this person's condition is obvious. Or when the perpetrator knew.
Following the prosecution's indictment, the case was referred to an investigating judge for further proceedings. This is according to the spokesman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, Mr. Kuch Kimlong.
The suspect, 43-year-old Liu Bunthoeun, was arrested by police and taken for questioning on July 16, 2020, and sent to court on the afternoon of July 17, 2020, after carrying a knife. Slash the face, including some other places of a 5-year-old girl named Las Mavilia.
Por Senchey District Police Inspector Mr. Morn Vuthy said that the woman was at No. 6, Street 26, Borey Phop Thmey, Chhouk Va 2, in the village of Tek Panho, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Sen Chey. The victim, a 5-year-old girl named Las Mavilia, lives at No. 18, Street 20, Borey Phop Thmey, Chhouk Va 2, Tek Panha Village, Sangkat Samrong Krom.
The girl is still being treated at the National Children's Hospital.
