The Minister stated that after Ratanakkiri Province was connected to the National Transmission System on July 2, Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) on July 17, 2020, launched a 150-kilometer sub-transmission line with a voltage of 35 kilovolts. Provides temporary supply in Mondulkiri before the 230 kV transmission line from Kratie to Mondulkiri is completed and operational by the end of this year.
Currently, the supply in Mondulkiri province is sourced from Vietnam, along with a small hydropower source with the help of the Japanese government in the province, he said.
According to Minister Keo Rattanak, the leaders of the Ministry of Mines and Energy joined forces with Electricite du Cambodge (EDC), Mr. Ith Prang, Secretary of State, and Mr. Victor Zona, Director General of the General Department of Energy, inspected and commissioned the 35 kV transmission line. Successfully, it is hoped that this temporary supply will be enough to replace imports from Vietnam until next year, as new sub-transmission lines begin to supply better street electricity.
