Among those cards, China may call on all Chinese companies or investors to reconsider or withdraw from the UK, citing London's lack of transparency and discrimination against Chinese companies. The British in China may also find it more difficult to do business, as the profitability of their business depends entirely on Sino-British bilateral relations.
In addition, China may cancel the UK as a special trading partner or trade preferences, which will reduce bilateral trade, but China can still solve this problem by increasing demand in Domestic.
In terms of the financial sector, China is a huge market for British financial services. So if China starts diverting financial cooperation with British companies to British rivals in Europe, London could see more of the big losses as it decides to divorce the EU.
