(Phnom Penh): A brutal woman who used a knife to operate on a 5-year-old girl because of a child quarrel was sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on the afternoon of July 17, 2020 for legal action. The woman confessed that she had used a knife to cut the victim's face because she was angry and threw stones at her, causing her to break her two-year-old son's head.
This incident happened at 3:15 pm on July 16, 2020 in Borey Phop Thmey Chhouk Va 2 in the village of Tek Panha, Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Sen Chey, Phnom Penh.
Por Senchey District Police Inspector Morn Vuthy said that the woman, 43-year-old Liv Bunthoeun, lived at No. 6, Street 26, Borey Phop Thmey, Chhouk Va 2, in the village of Tek Panha, Sangkat Samrong Krom. After the arrest, the woman said that she was very angry and could not sleep for two nights because the girl made her child bleed and knew that her child had grown up to be a star, so she only asked for the girl Bleeding just like his child.
The victim, a 5-year-old girl named Las Mavilia, suffered injuries to her face, nose, neck and arms.
Villagers said that the incident started from holding the child's legs too hard and lacking long-term consideration. On July 14, 2020, the son of the woman who was the perpetrator picked up stones and threw stones at the girl. The girl was also hit by the victim, causing her to break her head and break two stitches. At that time, the girl's mother also helped to send her to the hospital.
After that, the girl did not dare to walk for 2 days until the day of the incident, then she dared to go for a walk and walked in front of the woman's house. Kill. But then the girl cried out in shock, then the woman touched her face, nose, hands and neck, causing serious injuries and then ran to hide in the house.
Last night, Por Sen Chey District Governor Mr. Hem Darith and District Inspector visited and donated some money to the girl victim who is being treated at the National Children's Hospital.
