Speaking to the media after the meeting to review the semi-annual results of the General Department of Immigration on the morning of July 17, 2020, General Kiet Chantharith confirmed that using the foreign presence control system (FPCS) from the beginning. Last year, it was found that there are more than 160,000 non-immigrant foreigners in Cambodia, but the actual number is about 110,000.
In Cambodia, there are three different types of foreigners: non-immigrants, immigrants and foreigners as investors.
Non-immigrant foreigners refer to agents working at foreign embassies or consulates or foreign missions, international experts and others who enter Cambodia on an equal footing or by agreement with the Royal Government of Cambodia. Both their families and their staff during their stay.
General Kiet Chantharith stated, "By using the Foreign Presence Management System (FPCS) to date, we have received more than 160,000 people registered in our system, but the system confirms that the actual presence is "More than 110,000 people and the system is still being monitored or may increase."
According to the General, the General Department of Immigration in the first half of this year has made efforts to organize rallies in order to promote the management of non-immigrants more effectively by requesting to fill in the correct address in the letter upon arrival. Strengthen the documents and procedures when applying for a temporary residence visa and assign the implementation of the instructions of the Ministry of Interior.
General Kiet Chantharith strongly expressed his belief that from now on, using the Foreigner Presence Management System (FPCS), the General Department of Immigration will manage the presence of foreigners in Cambodia well and clearly, as is now the first step in using the system. Technology to manage.
Please be informed that according to the report presented at the meeting so far, 50,974 homeowners have connected to the Foreigner Presence Management System (FPCS) and reported the presence of foreigners to the General Department of Immigration.
