Cracked down on 2 drug trafficking cases, confiscated 2 kg of drugs and arrested 2 suspects in Khan Toul Kork and Khan Russey Keo
(Phnom Penh): Police from the Anti-Drug Bureau of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police launched an operation to crack down on two different drug trafficking cases, confiscating two drug exhibits, a large bag weighing about 2 kilograms, and detaining drug suspects. Two Khmer-Vietnamese nationals in Khan Toul Kork and Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh.
The operation took place on July 16, 2020, under the coordination of the procedure by the Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, Mr. Long Cheab and Mr. Soeur Lundy.
Phnom Penh Deputy Police Chief Major General Huot Chanyaran told Fresh News on the afternoon of July 17, 2020 that the large-scale drug crackdown operation in Phnom Penh was carried out under the direct orders of Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy General Commissioner of the National Police and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner.
In meetings at the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, the General Commissioner has always put in place measures to encourage the Phnom Penh Municipal Police in all divisions and areas to work together to effectively crack down on drugs, including the use, sale, distribution and trafficking of drugs in order to reduce crime. Drug offenses in Phnom Penh.
The commissioner also warned to take legal action against subordinate police officers if found to be involved in drug offenses.
According to the report of the Anti-Drug Police Office, the crackdown on the two drug trafficking suspects was led by Lt. Gen. Huot Chanyaran, Deputy Commissioner for Anti-Drug Planning. After the specialized forces identified the suspects and proceeded to arrest the two drug suspects in a row.
The first drug crackdown operation at 5:00 pm on July 16, 2020, the Anti-Drug Police arrested a 21-year-old unidentified suspect, Nhim Kimleang, in front of the university. Asia-Europe, Street 257, Sangkat Toek Laak 01, Khan Toul Kork, while the suspect was traveling by bus.
During the search, the police found and confiscated 1 large bag of methamphetamine and ice, weighing 1,000.74 grams, and 1 truck.
On the same day, the Anti-Drug Police Force continued to search and arrest another Vietnamese drug trafficking suspect, Sok Chantha, a 57-year-old male, who was engaged in running a pickup business at the intersection of National Road 5, Sangkat Kilometer. No. 6, Khan Russey Keo.
During the inspection, the police found and confiscated 1 large bag of methamphetamine, ice, 929.84 grams and 1 package of luggage.
Currently, drug suspects and drug paraphernalia are being questioned by the specialized office and a case is being prepared for legal action.
