(Stung Treng): Stung Treng Fisheries Administration District, on July 17, 2020, in cooperation with Borey O'Svay Sen Chey and Siem Bok districts, organized a forum on cooperation to eliminate fishery crimes in Stung Treng province with the participation of all actors. All stakeholders in each district, including district authorities, communes, administrative posts, police, military, river guards, environmentalists, community fisheries and fisheries experts.
Through this forum, all stakeholders are more committed to volunteering to protect the fishery resources by increasing the education of local people to volunteer to hand over illegal equipment to the authorities. .
It should be noted that in the last few years, Stung Treng Fisheries has made great efforts to reduce fishing offenses, especially the use of fishing gear and explosives, and has been widely disseminated to the public and fishermen everywhere. Basic. Under this effort, many illegal devices were confiscated and confiscated, stored and destroyed.
Mr. Tum Niro, Director of Stung Treng Fisheries Administration, said that after tightening the implementation of legal measures since 2018, all kinds of fishery crimes in Stung Treng province have decreased by not less than 90% by now. The crime is extremely secretive.
Local authorities and fishing communities have also said that fishing offenses are actually significantly lower than they were a few decades ago. Please note that the geography of Stung Treng is the most important breeding ground for fish in Cambodia, which has large fish such as king fish, trout, cucumber, prawns, giant prawns and freshwater dolphins and other fish. .
Finally, the fisheries community and local communities strongly urge all fishermen to immediately stop fishing that leads to the destruction of fishery resources and jointly protect these rare resources to ensure Sustainability for future generations as well.
