(Kandal): Senior Minister Kun Kim was appointed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association, as the Secretary General of the Veterans Association in the new term to serve as Samdech's staff. Cambodian Veterans.
The appointment ceremony of the new leadership of the Veterans Association was held this morning, July 16, 2020, presided over by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, as the High Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
During the appointment ceremony of the leadership of the Cambodian Veterans Association in the new mandate, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh praised and appreciated the achievements as well as the efforts of the leaders of the Cambodian Veterans Association achieved in the old mandate for 5 years. Ago.
Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh also urged the leaders who were elected to take charge of the association in the new mandate to work more actively and effectively to serve the interests and improve the lives of Cambodian veterans who are all rich. Great merit for the motherland.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, in his capacity as Vice-President of the Association and Secretary-General of the Association, as the Executive Director, is seen to have been active in resolving issues as well as efforts to improve the lives of veterans. The better.
With the trust from Samdech Techo Hun Sen to serve as a veteran in the new mandate, Senior Minister Kun Kim expressed his commitment and commitment to help the families of veterans.
"This is a great honor for me to receive the trust and great opportunity from Samdech Techo Hun Sen to serve the veterans. I would like to declare my commitment to work hard without fear of fatigue to solve the problems of the veterans as well as help the lives of the veterans better. This is the declaration of commitment of Senior Minister Kun Kim.
The senior minister added, "The wish of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit is to see you live happily and have a better life, so I must try not to disappoint the two Samdech."
Mr. Kun Kim said that for the past five years, from 2015 to 2020, in response to the great merits of Cambodian veterans Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen have considered construction. Homes for 2,460 veterans. According to the senior minister, there are still about 3,654 families of veterans who need to continue to build and resolve social land concessions.
According to the Senior Minister, as of May 2020, the Cambodian Veterans Association has 76,923 members, with a total of 108,871 members, receiving policy support from the state every month, including 26 retirees. 892 people, 1,444 people with disabilities and 26,449 people with disabilities.
The senior minister called on ministries, institutions, civil servants, and the armed forces to buy water to support veterans, as well as to contribute to the development of Cambodian veterans. In addition, the Senior Minister praised and appreciated the efforts made to achieve the achievements and progress of the Cambodian Veterans Association over the past five years.
