According to the demarcation of the borders of the French Empire during the Napoleonic period, the above confirms that the French Empire of that period covered some countries today, such as France itself, Spain, Switzerland, Italy, Belgium, Germany, the Netherlands, Poland (Warsaw), Czech Republic, Slovakia, Austria-Hong. Croatia, Bosnia, Montenegro, Belarus, Lithuania and parts of Russia.
Napoleon Bonaparte became French emperor in 1804 after overthrowing the old government in 1798, and he has been pursuing a policy of territorial expansion ever since. The French army grew stronger, especially when he began to form the "Great Army". Forming the first imperial army, he mobilized about 100,000 troops and gradually increased with the expansion of conquests throughout Europe.
This war father led the army to battle more than 70 times, winning almost every battle, but seven times the French army was defeated by the majority, mostly by the end of his reign.
Seeing the defeat of Napoleon, the great empires of Britain, Sweden, Austria and Russia joined forces to invade France until the invasion of Paris and forced Napoleon to step down from the throne. In 1813 they were forced into exile to live on the island of Elba, in the Mediterranean Sea of present-day western Italy.
Napoleon was again deposed by his allies and exiled to Saint Helena, a remote island in the middle of the Atlantic Ocean nearly 2,000 kilometers west of Africa. On March 5, 1821, the former most famous king in world history died at the age of 52 due to gastritis.
Foreign documents state that Napoleon Bonaparte had a total of 2.5 million troops under him, all of whom were close to him in the expansion of the French Empire, almost all over Europe. Round. Some of his strategies have been quoted and trained in many modern international military academies.
Napoleon presented many famous philosophies, but one of them was a delicious philosophy: "If you want the work to get the best results, you have to do it yourself." Summary of important news events for July 16, 2020
