(Stung Treng): Mr. Sik Bun Hok, Chairman of the National Election Committee (NEC), met with officials of the Stung Treng Provincial Election Secretariat on the morning of July 16, 2020. Located in Kaing Memay Village, Sangkat Preah Bat, Stung Treng City, Stung Treng Province.
Stung Treng Provincial Chairman Mr. HONG Kong briefed the NEC delegation that Stung Treng Province has a total population of 37,131 families, equivalent to 158,567 people, including a total of 18 people over the age of 18. There are 86,139 people, and the total number of people who have not yet registered and estimated for the 2020 voter registration is 3,630, but according to the 2020 voter registration plan, there are 2,760.
According to Hang Kong, Stung Treng province has 34 main offices for voter registration and voter registration, and 133 mobile offices, of which 40 are located in difficult locations, using boats and bulldozers to transport goods. Hold those polling station locations due to geographical factors.
He added that all officials cooperated and had good relations with the provincial, municipal, district, commune, 34 communes and all relevant parties in the province. Stung Treng Corps also conducted a training course on population statistics estimates for stakeholders, especially local authorities, to participate in the implementation of the voter list and voter registration 2020 in October.
After listening to the report of the Provincial Police, the Chairman of the NEC praised and highly appreciated the Stung Treng Provincial Police for taking care to maintain the equipment properly, especially with good cooperation. With stakeholders.
At the same time, the President will continue to work at the national level to address the difficulties that the LRC faced, because the election was held in the capital and provinces, and the LRC did the work directly on the spot. Strengthen the lower voting cells.
The President of the NEC also expressed his willingness to continue the electoral reform to the old and new officials that this election is very important to participate in maintaining the stability and peace of the country as we have. Already going through the past, post-election crises, whether in Cambodia or in other countries.
"Whatever you do, follow the law," he said. "Election officials need to learn and know the code of conduct for voters, which is the compass of our work."
The NEC's vision is that not only in 2016, the NEC will change from manual registration to computer registration, so that the election will be more acceptable to the NEC public. Plans to follow the electronic system:
* Registration of political parties and candidates * Announcement of election results, including: Receipt and transmission of election results, announcement of preliminary election results, distribution of seats, selection of elected candidates.
In addition, the NEC Chairman advised all election officials to adhere to the code of conduct for election officials and to abide by the law in order to eliminate protests and ensure that there is no crisis after the election. Vote.
He said that for new officials, which is a short-term contract, must strive to understand the law related to the election clearly, because the technique of voting is not taught in any school.
In June, the Ministry of Public Works seized 228 overweight vehicles and fined more than 400 million Riels (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): In June 2020, the Secretariat of the Standing Coordinating Committee of the Steering Committee for Overweight Vehicle Inspection Seized 228 overweight trucks and fined a total of 404,840,000 Riels.
(Phnom Penh): Mondulkiri provincial governor Svay Sam Eang presented plans to build a new airport in the northeastern province as the province prepared about 600 hectares of state land when the government needed to build one. The location of the new airport project is about 20 km from Sen Monorom.
In a press conference held by the Royal Government Spokesperson on the morning of July 16, 2020, Mr. Svay Sam Eang confirmed that the new airport project could not be built on the old site with about 19 hectares of land in the old place. At present, it seems crowded because people live around a lot.
According to the provincial governor, when the Royal Government built the new airport, the old airport was not abandoned or sold to any private sector, the provincial administration in cooperation with the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction will turn the site into a park. Garden or place for people to relax.
Mr. Svay Sam Eang said, "We leave the old airport site as a garden and we find a new location, this new location we have about 600 hectares, more than 20 kilometers away from Sen Monorom. "The new location could expand the large-scale domestic airport or international losses, depending on the study of civil aviation and relevant ministries."
The Mondulkiri provincial governor claimed that the provincial authorities were currently preparing to protect the prepared land from encroachment by the people, and whenever the government needed it, the provincial administration would be located in accordance with the requirements for investing in the new airport.
Regarding the preservation of the old airport, the provincial administration will organize it into a park, but this park will be done in stages, not once, while currently preparing the infrastructure gradually, with the planting of trees. Original.
According to the Secretariat of Civil Aviation, the new airport in Mondulkiri could be built on 300 hectares and is estimated to cost more than $ 60 million. The project has been studied and submitted to the Economic Policy Development Council.
Please be informed that today Cambodia has 3 international airports in operation: Phnom Penh International Airport, Siem Reap International Airport, Sihanoukville International Airport, which is managed and modernized by the French company SCA. Ministry of Agriculture and Ministry of Commerce Hold Meeting to Discuss Pig Trade
(Phnom Penh): Following the instructions of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister, on July 14 at the Freshwater Aquaculture Research and Development Center in Prey Veng Province, Samdech urged farmers to continue their efforts to raise more animals (pigs, chickens, ducks). And fish) to meet the needs of households, domestic markets and exports, and especially restrict the import of animals.
Please be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, on July 14, 2020 stated that he rejected a request from a company to import 1 million pigs to Cambodia, which was claimed by Samdech Techo to Protect local farmers.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if Samdech agrees to import 1 million pigs, this is equivalent to Samdech killing his farmers who are actively trying to raise pigs.
Please be informed that Cambodia needs about 10,000 pigs per day, of which domestic breeding is up to 5800 pigs per day, allowing the import of 6,000-7,000 pigs. Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang Leads a Delegation to Honor the Late Brigadier General Ouk Samon
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of July 16, 2020, Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang, Deputy Commander of the National Gendarmerie and Commander of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie, led a delegation to pay tribute to the late Brigadier General Ouk Samon. Pursat Provincial Gendarmerie, who died of a disease at 8:49 on July 14, 2020.
On the occasion of paying his respects, Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang brought 2 million Riels to share the deepest condolences with all the family, relatives and friends of the deceased and to dedicate to the soul of Brigadier General Ouk Samon. In death, do not be lazy.
All state property in Kandal province, especially Boeung Boor land, the provincial administration urges all units to expedite the preparation of inventory
(Central): All state property, especially state lands and lakes that have not yet been registered in the inventory, must be registered in accordance with financial procedures in order to avoid illegal possession or eventual loss. Therefore, all units must be prepared and must prepare their inventory for the base year (2019) as soon as possible to submit to the inspection committee.
He said that all departments, units and authorities that occupy state property must strive to protect, manage and maintain those state property with high responsibility by recording the state property accurately and comprehensively in accordance with the procedures of Inventory of state assets in accordance with the procedures and guidelines of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to make the management of state assets more efficient and accountable.
On this occasion, Ms. Khon Leakena, Director of the Department of Economy and Finance of Kandal Province, stated that the preparation of the inventory of state assets is carried out in two forms: the first form is an inventory record of all state assets to be done. Every five years, and the second form is the rising and falling stars of the state, which occur once a year during the five-year period of the base year.
She also informed that there are 1,162 plots of land of departments, units, halls, districts, communes, sangkats in Kandal province, of which 618 are land titles and 544 are land titles. .
Ms. Khon Leakena also requested all units to prepare the inventory for 2019 as soon as possible to submit to the review committee as scheduled. Poipet Municipality Authority opens the construction site of a road more than 1,000 meters in Sangkat Phsar Kandal, Poipet City
(Banteay Meanchey): Seeing the hardships of the people during the rainy season, which was continuously flooded, Mr. Keat Hul, Governor of Poipet City, on July 15, 2020, led the professional officers of the local authority to open the construction site of a road. It is 8 meters wide and 1,306 meters long in Mondul 1 Village, Mondul 2, Sangkat Phsar Kandal, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province. It is planned to use more than 200,000 USD from the Commune / Sangkat Fund.
Mr. Hul said that this road has been difficult for a long time and now the authorities have rebuilt it to facilitate commuters and transport patients from National Road 5 to the health center. Poipet City.
Mr. Hul also instructed the people to take care to maintain this road for a long time to leave it to the next generation and not to throw garbage on the road, causing congestion in the sewer. Drainage does not cause water on the road to damage the road is to be packed in the right bin.
The mayor of Poipet also instructed the people to know how to clean according to the instructions of the Ministry of Health to prevent Kovid 19 virus, even if no one dies in Cambodia, must be constantly vigilant.
17 Water Wells Donated by Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to Inaugurate 275 Families in Preah Vihear Province
(Preah Vihear): 17 Aphrates water wells donated by the President of the Cambodian Red Cross, His Excellency Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen, were inaugurated on July 16, 2020 in the presence of Ms. Chak Heng, Governor Deputy Preah Vihear Province and Permanent Vice President of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch and the working group together with many local authorities.
On that occasion, Ms. Chak Heng brought a message of greetings from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who always pays attention to the well-being and living of the people, especially the people. Poor, elderly, helpless, widows, orphans, people living with HIV and others vulnerable to natural disasters.
Ms. Chak Heng also called on people to take good care of their health, drink boiled water and wash their hands thoroughly with soap and alcohol to prevent various diseases, especially Kovid-19 disease.
She encouraged people to use water sparingly according to the Royal Government's circular because climate change can cause problems such as drought, forest fires, floods, etc. Please participate in the maintenance and use of water wells. This is good and accurate, useful so that these wells can be used for a long time.
It should be noted that 17 Aphrates water wells have been provided to 275 families (1,058 people) in 14 villages in 4 communes, including 5 Rong Roeung communes and 4 liberated communes. 3 wells in Rom Tom commune, 5 wells in Romney commune, Rovieng district, Rovieng district, Preah Vihear province.
On that occasion, the Cambodian Red Cross donated to the most vulnerable 36 families from 4 villages in Rong Roeung commune, Rovieng district, Preah Vihear province, each family received 25 kg of rice, 1 box of fish, 1 stick of soy sauce. Also.
