(Kampong Thom): Mr. Say Veasna, Deputy Prosecutor of Kampong Thom Provincial Court, led the Provincial Gendarmerie to crack down on illegal gambling under the direct command of Mr. Sin Virak, Prosecutor of Kampong Thom Provincial Court at 15:30. Minutes, July 15, 2020.
Operation to crack down on gambling: 15 military police forces, 3 vehicles cracked down on gambling at the point of Leap Tong Krao village, Trea commune, Leap Tong village, Kampong Chen Tbong commune and Sandan village, Chamnar Krom commune, Stong district, Kampong Thom province.
As a result of the crackdown, the police arrested 5 gambling addicts:
It should be noted that the gambling house, Siam Lottery, Vietnam Lottery, including apong cards, gambling activities in Stong district for a long time, but no crackdown, which raises suspicions that there is a conspiracy by the local authorities. Including some relevant officials who closed their eyes and closed their noses to allow gambling in Stong district.
In particular, in Stong market, there are always two consecutive incidents of breaking car windows and thefts, but it is not possible to catch a thief. The exhibits confiscated by the police were: 5 mobile phones, 20 notebooks, 4 pens, 1 calculator.
The general public, including the public, expressed their support for the crackdown on gambling by Mr. Sin Virak, the Prosecutor of Kampong Thom Provincial Court, who cracked down on gambling like a downpour, significantly reducing the number of criminal activities. .
700 peacock trees planted on National Road 6A, Kandal provincial governor inspires people to love the environment, love trees and plant as many as possible
(Kandal): The Governor of Kandal Province, Mr. Kong Sophoan, encouraged all people to love the environment, love trees and plant as many as possible, while the Kandal Provincial Administration brought 1,500 saplings to plant. Each house and planted 700 peacock seedlings on National Road 6A, Muk Kampul district to enhance the green beauty of the road.
This activity was led by Mr. Kong Sophoan, which took place on July 15, 2020 with the participation of officials and Mr. Tong Sivmey, Governor of Muk Kampul District.
The governor said that forests play an important role in maintaining the ecosystem and reducing the negative effects of climate change, such as floods, hurricanes and the absorption of carbon dioxide from the atmosphere. The most precious is the life of human beings, animals that have provided unimaginable multidimensional value to humanity, economic and social value.
He added that especially to help maintain the balance of the natural environment, improve the climate, maintain the stability of water resources, protect the slopes and biodiversity, more importantly, the forest has a lot to do with agriculture.
At the same time, the provincial governor called on local authorities, the armed forces, government officials, students and all citizens to take care of the seedlings planted now, because in the next 4 to 5 years. On the other hand, it is hoped that the national roads of Muk Kampul district, full of trees, will be green, so-called streets, accompanied by colorful plants.
Mr. Kong Sophoan also called on people to remain vigilant against the Covid-19 virus, not to be negligent, and all people must know how to clean their hands, wash their hands with alcohol or soap regularly when traveling. On the streets and in the city, wear a mask properly.
