Spokesman for the General Commission: On July 16, another 1594 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, for 77 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to July 16, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected And fined a total of 106498 vehicles, including 78469 motorcycles and 288029 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorcycles are mostly helmet, offense, overweight, unlicensed, no license plate and cell phone use. In particular, the offenses for cars are mostly speeding, overcrowding, no belts, offenses, no license plates, overweight, using mobile phones and so on.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 77 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
