(Kep): Ms. Mon Manvy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, stated that the Royal Government is paying close attention to the promotion of women's rights by increasing the composition of women in the leadership from the grassroots level. For example, in the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, there are four women with the rank of Secretary of State and the Governor of Koh Kong Province.
This morning, on July 16, 2020, she presided over the opening ceremony of the Dissemination Workshop on the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination against Women (CEDAW) and 11 recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, as well as some relevant laws.
The event was attended by about 100 senior officials from relevant ministries, units of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Kep, Koh Kong, Kampot, Takeo, Prey Veng, Svay Rieng and Kandal provinces.
Ms. Men Manvy continued that the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has a long-term vision to promote women leaders in districts / provinces throughout Cambodia, at least to have a governor. Deputy District / Khan / Municipality and Deputy Governor of the province or capital as well.
Ms. Men Manvy called on all citizens to strictly adhere to the traffic law in a spirit of high responsibility and adhere to the principle of safety in order to avoid traffic accidents and to remember the noble words of Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Today, tomorrow, avoid traffic accidents. The Governor of Mondulkiri Province hopes that the first drop of gold ore will be able to do business in 2021 by two companies (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): After using the study time for many years, the first drop of gold ore in Mondulkiri province will appear during the end of 2020 or 2021 by two companies from Australia and China. Who has obtained a legal license from the Royal Government as a business operator.
Mondulkiri provincial governor Svay Sam Eang said at a press conference on the morning of July 16, 2020 that the two foreign companies had graduated and would claim to be in the gold business. In Mondulkiri province during 2020 or 2021, when the company has completed the production line.
Mr. Svay Sam Eang added that the two companies include Australia's Renisen and China's Rong Chheng.
"There are two companies that have studied the amount of gold that the company can do business with: Australia's Renisen and China's Rongcheng," said the Mondulkiri governor. "According to the latest report, he (the gold mining company) will be in business in 2020 or 2021 when he completes the production line."
When the company does mining, it will bring economic income to the nation as well as contribute to the development of Mondulkiri even better, while now both companies have already helped solve the shortage in some localities, such as wells. Hospital water, roads, bridges, etc. This is what the provincial governor highlighted.
According to Mr. Svay Sam Eang, in Mondulkiri province, there is potential for many kinds of minerals, such as gold, lead, bauxite, etc. To date, there are 10 mining companies with 11 licenses.
He added that apart from the mining sector, the energy sector also has the same potential, and the potential sites for dam construction include the 235-megawatt Srepok River, the 20-megawatt O'Plai basin, the 17-megawatt Prek Po and Prek Dak Doe has a power of 200-500 MW. All these locations have already been studied by the Ministry, but there are no investment partners yet.
At present, the province has two small hydropower stations, O'Remis and O'Mleng, to supply power to the people of Sen Monorom, with a power supply of 370 MW and connected to two networks from Vietnam.
