These days, community members, especially patrols, are actively working to wire the canals, use boats and manpower to push the canisters around the lake every day to prevent boats, the community leader said. The ferry driver came to steal fish in this conservation lake because during the rainy season, the wind blows and breaks the wire and cans scattered all over the lake almost every day.
He said, however, that the challenge was that the community did not have the funds to buy wire to buy fuel for these works, which in the past some members had spent their own money to do all this work as far as possible.
Mr. Nhanh, the patrol leader who is leading the patrol team to build the lake to protect the lake, said that the community has 3 patrol teams with a total force of 15 people, taking turns patrolling the protected area day and night. One group of three people during the day and one group of three people at night, but we can only protect 80% because we have less patrol force and no fuel to patrol the boat.
Therefore, the community leader and the patrol team leader requested the partner organizations that help in the field of agriculture, relevant institutions, please support the above shortcomings to the fishing community in Kampong Os for the common benefit.
