The announcement of customs revenue figures for the first half of this year was made at the meeting to review the work of Customs and Excise for the first half of 2020, chaired by Dr. Kun Nhim, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise. With the participation of many customs and excise officials as leaders on July 14, 2020.
In particular, the provisional figures of international trade volume in the first half of 2020 compared to the first half of 2019 have changed as follows: Total import value decreased by 9.4% and total export value decreased by 0.7%. The value of garment exports decreased by 7.5%, but the total price of rice, rubber and other agricultural products increased by 14.5%.
He said that the decline in international trade and customs revenue in the first half of 2020 was due to a number of factors, the most important of which was the outbreak of Kovid 19, which affected the domestic market as well as Cambodia's export markets and international trade flows have been severely affected.
For the direction of implementation in the second half of 2020, the Director General recalled the instructions of the Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance, mentioned at the meeting to review the work of Customs and Excise 2019 in February. In the past, we will continue to implement the four rounds of measures of the Royal Government related to customs to support the national economy in difficult circumstances caused by Kovid 19.
