Mr. Kong Kimny takes over as Deputy Governor of Kratie Province, replacing Mr. Khan Chamnan
(Kratie): Mr. Kong Kimny officially assumed the position of Deputy Governor of Kratie Province on July 15, 2020, replacing Mr. Khan Chamnan, who was transferred to work at the Ministry of Interior.
The Kratie Provincial Administration was presided over by Mr. Bun Hon, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, representing Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, with the participation of Mr. Vathon, Governor of Kratie Province.
During the inauguration ceremony, the Governor of Kratie Province mentioned the geographical situation, management, security and public order in the province to be good and achievements.
Mr. Bun Hon commended the Provincial Unity Command for its efforts to maintain security, public order and safety for the people, and better management of the situation in the whole province, contributing to the strengthening of peace, political stability and socio-economic development.
He also urged the Unity Command at all levels to continue to strengthen the work of safe villages and communes in order to crack down on all forms of insecurity at the local level. He urged to increase the responsibility of law enforcement forces, promote awareness to people to respect traffic laws, stay away from drugs and to participate in measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 as directed by the Ministry. Health.
Mr. Bun Hon stated that the change of role and assignment in leadership is due to Mr. Khan Chamnan reaching the term of office for 8 years as Deputy Governor in accordance with the law. The principle is to ensure that all local leaders work hard, effectively, transparently, and learn from the experience of sub-national leaders from one base to another.
