China announces retaliation for US interference in China's internal affairs (Video inside) (Beijing): Beijing on Wednesday warned that it would retaliate against the United States after US President Donald Trump Signed a law authorizing the imposition of sanctions on Chinese banks over the passage of a new security law for Hong Kong. This was released by CNA on Wednesday afternoon, July 15, 2020.
In a statement, the Chinese Foreign Ministry said, "China will respond as necessary to protect its legitimate interests and impose sanctions on US personnel and all relevant entities."
The Chinese Foreign Ministry also stressed that Beijing strongly opposes the latest US actions and urged Washington to immediately stop interfering in its internal affairs. "Hong Kong affairs are purely China's internal affairs and no foreigner has the right to interfere." This is the statement of the Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
The warning comes after US President Donald Trump signed a law allowing sanctions on banks that do business with Chinese officials and are involved in passing a new national security law. Hong Kong territory recently.
