(Foreign): Missile is a type of weapon used for long-range attacks, it can fly by itself. Today, there are many types, from conventional missiles to ballistic missiles capable of carrying nuclear warheads and intercontinental ballistic missiles.
The earliest missiles used in the operation were missiles developed by the German military during World War II. Among them, the most well-known missiles are the V-1 and V-2 missiles. However, the first missiles used in that era were produced in small quantities and were not very effective.
Missiles now have key components such as guidance systems, flight systems, engines and warheads. Navigation systems are very important for missiles. Some missiles can be equipped with an infrared probe to track the heat emitted from the aircraft engine, while others are guided to their attack targets by laser pointing by infantry near the target. Live and so on.
Tbong Khmum provincial officials cooperated to inspect the quality of goods at the border checkpoint, found and confiscated 6 kinds of vegetables imported from Vietnam containing chemicals
(Tbong Khmum): Six samples of vegetables such as onion, red onion, garlic, kale, lemon and carrot were found by Tbong Khmum Provincial Police, including a mobile laboratory vehicle in cooperation with provincial customs officials and officials at Tbong Khmum Provincial Border Gate. Load chemicals and take immediate action.
Mr. Meas Mora stated that as a measure, the professional officers of the Provincial Branch of the DPRK have provided measures to the Customs and Excise Office to send the vegetables containing pesticide residues back to the country of origin, in case of importing 6 kinds of vegetables. The above requires the importers to show a certificate stating that there is no residue of pesticides from the competent officials of the exporting country, if not, absolutely not to import.
At the same time, officials called on traders importing vegetables, fruits and food through the border gates from neighboring countries into Cambodia to be careful and pay attention, that is, to import, distribute and sell only food products. Good quality, especially strictly prohibited, contains banned and out-of-date chemicals that cause harm to the well-being of consumers and are subject to legal penalties.
(Phnom Penh): Again and again, Prime Minister Hun Sen has shown his special ability to manage and lead the country in any difficult circumstances that have arisen. In fact, during the Kovid-19 phase, this experienced Cambodian leader unleashed a series of talented talents.
In addition to avoiding the spread of Kovid-19 in the community and preventing anyone from dying of Kovid-19, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also showed his special talent in solving national and people's economic problems so as not to be affected. Stronger from this one global crisis.
After being guided by the Cambodian leader, many Cambodians turned to animal husbandry, aquaculture and all kinds of vegetable crops. Realizing that the people are becoming more and more interested, the Prime Minister also promoted agriculture directly with farmers, starting with the promotion of aquaculture in Prey Veng province on the morning of July 14.
To promote this sector, Samdech Techo Hun Sen met directly with farmers, fish farmers and frog farmers to find out about their problems before launching a targeted solution. This is the intelligence of the leaders who do not just wait to hear the report, but have to meet with the people to understand their problems clearly, so that the solution is as effective as Samdech has been doing for a long time.
On July 21, the Prime Minister also plans to visit Prey Kabbas district of Takeo province to harvest light rice and especially to promote the cultivation of rice and other agricultural crops. The presence of the top leader with the farmers now really shows that the campaign to promote agriculture in the context of Kovid 19 has begun. This campaign will be a powerful impetus for both immediate and long-term problems for all Cambodians.
What is noteworthy before the campaign, the Prime Minister has already pointed out the direction to the people to be interested in agriculture, as well as to send a message to lower-level officials to be ready to solve the problems ahead by focusing On agriculture. Leadership that is always planned and has the right strategic plan, direction and situation, and this is the strength of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, especially to turn problems into opportunities.
In fact, since the Kovid 19 crisis erupted, the Prime Minister seems to have grasped the situation in his hands and resolved it step by step without panic, in line with Kovid 19's smooth evolution. It is this wisdom that so far Cambodia has been able to avoid epidemics, deaths and serious economic losses.
How many world leaders can resist this? The answer to this question is an argument that confirms "the special talents and abilities of Samdech Techo Hun Sen."
After receiving this package, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, this morning, July 15, 2020, chaired a high-level meeting between relevant institutions of the Royal Government and the United Nations in Cambodia on the joint program. Together to support migrants returning from the Kovid-19 epidemic and its aftermath.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized that the meeting focused on the distribution of how to use the budget properly and transparently to the targets of migrant workers after returning home and experiencing livelihood problems during the outbreak. The epidemic of Kovid-19 is universal.
According to Prince Sar Kheng, only three provinces are a priority in using this budget to support migrant workers, including Banteay Meanchey, Battambang and Siem Reap. In these three provinces, the Royal Government will select some other target districts according to practical possibilities.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng expressed his belief that if this program is implemented well during the six-month pilot period, Cambodia will receive additional funding from the United Nations. However, in the meeting, Samdech stressed that all working groups must pay attention to implement this work, that is, to be used in a targeted and transparent manner.
In addition, Prince Sar Kheng thanked the United Nations for approving this important project proposal with a US $ 1 million package to implement a joint program to be implemented by a group of UN agencies. The nation and the government aim to protect repatriated migrant workers and communities.
In order to implement this project effectively, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng has set out some recommendations, including:
* Sub-national administrations must properly manage the security, order, movement of migrants and provide public services in a responsive and timely manner, as well as facilitate the participation of partners in promoting and improving the lives of the people.
* Request the UN agency in Cambodia to coordinate with the UN agency with other countries in the region to find a solution to control the cross-border flow of migrant workers between sending and receiving countries.
* The Ministry of Planning and Sub-National Administration should strive to update the real poor, especially migrants who have returned from neighboring countries to benefit from the Royal Government's cash subsidies to poor families and other economic protections of the Royal Government.
