Cambodian Red Cross receives over $ 10 million in donations on May 8, 2020
(Phnom Penh): The First Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, Ms. Men Neary Sopheak, stated that the Cambodian Red Cross Headquarters received $ 10,669,262 in donations from national and international philanthropists on the occasion of the anniversary. The 157th World Red Cross, Red Crescent Day, May 8, 2020, held under the theme "I love peace and the Cambodian Red Cross".
She made this statement in an interview with journalists on "CRC progress 2019-2020 and work direction" which took place at the CRC headquarters on July 14, 2020.
The First Deputy Secretary-General said that the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day is celebrated every year with the aim of promoting achievements and raising funds to continue humanitarian operations to help the most vulnerable people across the country. Cambodia, regardless of political affiliation, race, religion, caste, color at all.
Although no celebrations are being held to celebrate the 157th anniversary of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, as is the case every year, the Cambodian Red Cross continues to raise funds and welcome donations from philanthropists in both the public and private sectors. Private as it did last year at both the national and sub-national levels.
Ms. Men Neary Sopheak continued, "As of July 14, 2020, the Cambodian Red Cross has received a total of $ 10,669,262 in donations from philanthropists." We would also like to thank all the philanthropists who continue to support the Cambodian Red Cross, even in the context of Kovid 19.
On that occasion, she thanked the philanthropists who support the Cambodian Red Cross to continue its activities in managing the use of funds to continue to help people, especially in continuing the campaign with the Royal Government to prevent and prevent measles 19. To have a second wave or spread in the community.
