(Oddar Meanchey): Officers of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud Branch (PDP) in Oddar Meanchey Province, led by Mr. Linh Sovathana, Branch Manager, this morning, July 14, 2020, in cooperation with the Provincial Department of Commerce, disseminated the quality. Food Safety and Inspection of Food Goods at Chong Kal Market is located in Chong Kal Village, Chong Kal Commune, Chong Kal District, Oddar Meanchey Province.
Mr. Linh Sovathana, Head of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud Branch (PDP) in Oddar Meanchey Province, said that the purpose of the inspection is to investigate and prevent the traffic of defective goods, counterfeit signs, expiration dates and substances. Prohibited chemicals that harm people's health.
He said that in this activity, the team conducted a preliminary test on 9 products, including: 2 samples of salt, 1 sample of prawns, 1 sample of prahok, 1 sample of yellow noodles, 1 sample of dried fish, 1 sample of sausage, 1 sample of soy bubbles. One sample and grapefruit to detect iodine and banned chemicals.
He added that as a result, our officers confiscated 3 kilograms of banned chemicals (borax) on the bubble and destroyed them.
At the same time, his team posted and posted 45 posters and explained to the traders to understand and follow the law on quality control, safety of products and services to avoid impact. The health of the people who may face the law.
Mr. Linh Sovathana said that during the operation on July 14, his team conducted a campaign to spread and put up flyers on the content of finding out about fraud in the business related to fuel at gas stations. The two fuel districts are in Chong Kal and Samrong districts of Oddar Meanchey province.
Mr. Linh Sovathana thanked the Provincial Department of Commerce as a partner as well as local authorities at all levels and the smooth participation of all station and depot owners for providing the opportunity and conditions for his branch to carry out this campaign. Smoothly.
