(Svay Rieng): Mr. Men Vibol, Governor of Svay Rieng Province, stated that the OWSO is a collection of administrative services in one place to make it very convenient for people to come and receive services without having to Find services in many places that lead to a waste of time and resources.
Mr. Men Vibol said this morning, July 14, 2020, as he presided over the inauguration ceremony of the OWSO and Romeas Hek District People's Office. The ceremony was attended by Mr. and Mrs. Deputy Provincial Governor, District Governor, Deputy Director of District Administration, Heads of Offices-Units and Civil Servants under the District Hall, Commune / Sangkat Clerks and Chiefs of 16 Administrative Police Stations, Forces and Citizens. A total of 144 people were present.
He also stated that the establishment of the OWSO and the Citizens' Office is aimed at promoting the provision of some services that people need and on a regular basis, and that those services can be effectively implemented by the administration. The district aims to make it easier, faster and more transparent for people to receive services.
The provincial governor also instructed the officers and staff at the OWSO to have a gentle, simple, friendly attitude, to adhere to the principles of professional ethics, be suitable as a service provider to the people and perform their duties. To ensure that the provision of services is transparent and accountable in accordance with established policies, procedures and procedures.
He also called on all residents in Romeas Hek district from now on to come and receive services at the OWSO to contribute to the collection of revenue into the national budget as well as eliminate Overdue fees as well.
