General Knowledge: Is the sea generally blue because of the blue sky or something?
(Foreign): True, the sea is normal white, but most people conclude that the ocean looks blue is probably because it shines the color of the sky, which is blue, but in fact there is a main reason that Interacts with water and sunlight molecules.
At that time, the red, orange, yellow, and green rays of the sun are strongly absorbed by water molecules, while the blue, dark blue, and purple rays are water molecules that are not absorbed at all. Scattered all over the water, making us see the blue ocean. However, the surface of the sea can also look like other colors, such as green, because the light is reflected from other particles in the water.
It should be noted that the deepest part of the ocean is completely dark because there is no more light to penetrate. Generally, from a depth of 1 km or almost 1 km, the sun can no longer penetrate, no matter which ray of light it is.
