Ponhea Leu District Police Arrested a Drunk Man Who Stoned a Commune Clerk on a Motorbike
Victim name: Sam Saveth, Male, Age: 64, Nationality: Khmer, Occupation: Assistant Clerk, Residence: Phum Thom Tray, Khum Phsar Dek, Ponhea Leu District, Kandal Province. The suspect, Soeun Sin, male, 37 years old, Khmer, unspecified occupation, resides in Phsar Dek Krom village, Phsar Dek commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province.
Police recounted the story of the victim riding his 2013 brand motorcycle from the commune hall to his home. Si nearby threw a stone at the victim, who was riding a motorcycle, hitting his left side of the head, causing him to bleed profusely.
At that time, the suspect also picked up a piece of stone and threw it at the next victim, but it was not right because the victim was riding a motorbike and ran to Ponhea Leu District Referral Hospital to be treated for his injuries.
Police confirmed that the suspect had previously been imprisoned in Kampong Chhnang province for six years for armed robbery.
The suspect is currently being detained by the Phsar Dek Administrative Police Station and sent to the Ponhea Leu District Police Inspectorate for questioning and processing.
