General Knowledge: 2644 years ago, no one understood the words of the prophet who predicted that Buddha would become a Buddha.
(India): Our teacher Buddha, originally named "Preah Seth", was born in the year 80 BC and 624 BC in a park in the northeastern part of the ancient Indian Empire (now in the country). Nepal) with a father named King Sothotanak and a mother named Sirim Mahamaya.
Five days after the baby was born, King Sothotanak selected eight mighty Brahmins to name and predict the fate of his son. The boy's name was also given "Seth", which means "one who accomplishes everything."
However, it is claimed that people at that time also understood some of the words of the Buddha, especially King Sothotanak, the father of Preah Sitha Komar, because he used all means to make his son the next king. He meant that he wanted his son Seth to be more of an emperor.
Please be informed that the current Buddhist era is 2564 years, and if you add to the life of the Buddha 80 years, that is 2644 years, which means that 2644 years ago, probably no one understood the prophecy of The Brahmin astrologer that Gotama or Preah Settha will attain enlightenment becomes a Buddha.
