The United States, Britain and some European countries have strongly condemned Beijing's decision to impose a new national security law on Hong Kong, which could undermine the Chinese Special Administrative Region's status as an international financial center.
In fact, China also wants to see Hong Kong have a bright, successful and prosperous future. But the economy and national security must go hand in hand, as protests in Hong Kong for most of 2019 forced Beijing to introduce new national security laws to regulate the situation, prevent separatist movements or demand independence, demonstrations. Create unrest so that Taiwan and other Chinese autonomous regions do not follow suit.
1. Political and economic stability Political stability in Hong Kong is very important for China because Hong Kong is an international financial center that acts as a bridge between mainland China and the global market.
So for China, Hong Kong's growth and success is important because it contributes to China's economic growth, but at the same time, China is developing Shanghai and Shenzhen into international financial centers like Hong Kong. To prevent the West, especially the United States, from using Hong Kong as an excuse to put pressure on China.
2. The new standard of state intervention The new national security law should not only be interpreted or understood in the context of China's economic policy, but it may also change and pave the way for the state to intervene or intervene. Any trade that affects national security, especially related to key infrastructure and technology.
All in all, many countries in the world have national security laws, including countries such as Australia, the United States, the European Union and Canada, which have the strictest national security laws to monitor foreign investment.
