Remarks by Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion of visiting fish breeding center and meeting with farmers in Prey Veng province
(Phnom Penh): On Tuesday morning, July 14, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, paid a visit to the Fish Breeding Research and Development Center as well as meeting with farmers in Peam Ro District, Prey Veng Province.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen had a talk with farmers with the following important contents:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the meeting with farmers this morning is a normal situation of life in a new way.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that since the outbreak of Kovid 19, Cambodia has never closed its economy, only with some restrictions.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that when there was no Kovid 19 disease, when Samdech met the people, they were close, but now the security gap must be maintained.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this morning's visit was to replace the interruption of the celebration of the National Plant and Fish Day, which was not celebrated because of Kovid 19 disease.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Kovid 19 disease has changed the living attitude of the people not only in Cambodia but also in the world.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Kovid 19 disease affects all countries, both rich and poor.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the problem of Kovid 19 industry in the world is more serious than Cambodia. Like the aircraft manufacturing industry, it no longer exists because you do not know who to sell it to?
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia will join the regional food supply chain.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asks foreign friends and foreign journalists to publish Samdech's proclamation to participate in the local food supply.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that during the time of Kovid 19, they can reduce the production of aircraft, cars, reduce the purchase of clothes and other consumables, but can not reduce the food in the stomach.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia still has high potential in the agricultural sector, in which more than 4 million hectares of land, both rice and crops are still in demand.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the crisis caused by Kovid 19 must be turned into an opportunity to increase agricultural potential.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the labor force in the service sector who lost their jobs could return to agriculture.
* Samdech Techo stated that each year, Cambodia needs about 290,000 tons of meat per year, but Cambodia can only supply more than 230,000 tons. Samdech urges to increase additional feeding.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that yesterday a company requested to import pigs from Thailand, but Samdech did not support the import.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that importing pigs from abroad is killing local farmers and raising Thai people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that this is an opportunity for people to raise fish. But be careful not to overlap between farmed fish and fishing lot fish to affect the price.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs the Ministry of Agriculture to prepare a calendar for raising fish and dividing it into regions.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech will increase the technical staff in aquaculture, but will take the contracted staff and put them into the framework next year.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that it is time for Cambodia to attack aquaculture. The Royal Government has dropped $ 500,000 to the Rural Development Bank to support aquaculture.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that providing agricultural knowledge is more important than giving other gifts.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Kovid 19 can destroy the Cambodian people but can not make the Cambodian people starve.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that agriculture is the lifeblood of the Cambodian people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Thailand and Vietnam have a high level of breeding and processing techniques.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces that the Royal Government will allow a five-day New Year holiday from August 17 to 21, 2020
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to call on people to behave to prevent Kovid 19 by wearing masks when going to necessary places, especially meeting places.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen warns that karaoke that is not converted into a restaurant will not open.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government is providing cash to about 170,000 workers in the garment and tourism sector $ 40 per month. At the same time, as of yesterday, it has provided cash to about 520,000 poor families in the amount of 92 billion riels, equivalent to 23 million dollars.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on garment and tourism workers who have lost their jobs to turn to fish farming and the Royal Government provides capital.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government is not afraid to invest in encouraging people to raise fish because it provides employment and improves people's lives.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen questioned who sought justice for Samdech when his brother-in-law was shot dead in 1996 in Phnom Penh and bombed in 1998 in Siem Reap?
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructs the Ministry of Agriculture to discuss with relevant parties to examine the possibility of assisting investors in the processing of fish and animal feed.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if Cambodia could set up a factory to process animal feed and fish feed and the price would be similar, then people would buy local food.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has not collapsed due to Kovid 19 and still has the budget to pay the salaries of civil servants in the Armed Forces as usual.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reacted to a citizen in Banteay Meanchey province named "Rath Sothy" who said that the poor people's allowance is an EU grant.
