General Vong Pisen Receives New Philippine Military Attach
On that occasion, General Vong Pisen welcomed the diplomatic mission of Colonel Sally Mar Imperial in Cambodia and hoped that we would have a good cooperation.
The Commander-in-Chief recalled the cooperative relationship between Cambodia and the Philippines, which dates back to 1957 and was severed in 1975 when Cambodia fell under the Pol Pot genocidal regime and only in 1992 did the two countries begin to exist. Reconnect and mark the 60th anniversary of Cambodia-Philippines diplomatic ties.
Regarding the defense sector, General Vong Pisen emphasized that in 2017, the Defense Ministers of the two countries signed a memorandum of understanding to strengthen the defense sector. The general hopes that after the situation in Kovid 19 calms down, the two countries' armies will continue to cooperate with each other.
In response, Colonel Salimar Imperial thanked the Commander-in-Chief for allowing him to pay a courtesy call on the occasion. The military attaché expressed his appreciation to the Royal Government of Cambodia for its good control and prevention of the spread of Kovid-19, and he wished to study the issue.
Colonel Salimar Imperial was also impressed by Cambodia's strategy for resolving past conflicts, and this is an important area for the Philippines to study. He hopes that in the near future, the Philippines will be as peaceful as Cambodia is today.
