(Phnom Penh): Cambodia-Laos is studying to open another international border gate in Ratanakkiri province, but this project has not been officially announced yet because it is still in the study stage. This is according to Mr. Thong Savun, Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, speaking on the morning of July 13, 2020.
At a press conference on "Progress and Continuation of Ratanakkiri Provincial Administration" organized by the Royal Government Spokesperson, Mr. Thong Savun claimed that so far Ratanakkiri has no roads or border crossings with Laos. And the province is asking the Royal Government to open this gate.
As for the exact location of the bilateral border gate in Ratanakkiri province, Mr. Thong Savun has not yet clarified, but he only revealed that it is open in the areas that are of great importance to Ratanakkiri and Attapeu provinces. Laos) as well as people near the border between the two countries.
