As Northern Macedonia, with a total population of more than 2 million on a total area of 25,713 square kilometers, is preparing for parliamentary elections, here are five key points to keep in mind for a Balkan state. This is what separated from the former Yugoslav Union for almost 30 years:
1: Change the country name
As a result, the West welcomed and welcomed the agreement, and NATO welcomed Northern Macedonia as a member, while the European Union gave the green light for the country to begin negotiations for membership, which will take years to negotiate.
2: Confusion
Northern Macedonia clashed with Albanian ethnic rebels in 2001. In the conflict, 200 people died in the six-month conflict. The conflict ended after the Ohrid Agreement in August 2001, which gave the Albanian indigenous peoples great rights, including the separation of powers, public participation, and status. Official for Albanian and so on.
3: Immigration
Northern Macedonia is one of the poorest countries in Europe, with an average salary of $ 475, 16 percent of the population is unemployed and most of them are young people. Such a weak economy has forced some northern Macedonians to migrate abroad in search of work, according to the World Bank, half a million people, or a quarter of the population. Living abroad.
4: Ancient Capital
The Cardamom Mountains, from the battle of deforestation and wildlife hunting, has become a rich tourist attraction.
(Koh Kong): After the prevention and introduction of the importance of natural resources of wildlife of the Ministry of Environment, Wildlife Alliance and related institutions, people who have been engaged in deforestation and hunting in the southern Phnom Penh area in Koh Kong province. In Kampong Speu and Pursat provinces, people stopped this activity and turned to conserving natural resources until this area became a strong momentum for tourism.
Ms. Koy Lay said that her family has been living in this community since 1994, if you look back, it has not been established as a community, and most of the people here are engaged in logging, hunting, wildlife and business. Others to earn a living.
For Mr. Touch Sophanny, Project Director of Ecotourism Community Project of Wildlife Alliance, the purpose of establishing this ecotourism community is to reduce deforestation, hunting, especially to protect the natural environment in this natural forest area. Efficiency.
Mr. Touch Sophanny added that after the establishment of this community, the people are very aware of the protection of the natural environment, protection of biodiversity, and committed to join the relevant authorities to preserve the natural resources in this area. Loss like in the past.
On Sovann, president of the Wildlife Alliance's ecotourism community, said: "In 1998, there was a lot of anarchy in Giphat, including deforestation, wildlife hunting and land grabbing. "Personally, but with the help of the Wildlife Alliance, he has eliminated a lot of this problem, and he has compiled some documents with the relevant ministries, local authorities and the people of the four villages in Jiphat to form a community."
Mr. On Sovann continued that since 2007, the Giphat ecotourism community has changed its face from a remote area to a tourist destination, reducing the migration of people in Giphat commune. Turn to growing crops, taking tourists for sightseeing and other occupations to meet the needs of tourists.
According to the head of the community, there are now more than 600 families in Jiphat commune, of which 362 families are members of the community, so they can take advantage of the community, such as village chefs, forest chefs, guides and visitors. In the Jiphat Ecotourism Area.
The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment stated that the purpose of the Royal Government of Cambodia is to turn the natural resource protection area with tourism potential into a natural tourism destination.
