(Phnom Penh): Mr. Thong Savun, Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, this morning, July 13, 2020, presented the progress and progress of the province under the shadow of peace through a press conference organized by the Government Spokesperson Unit under the theme "Progress and direction of the work of the administration of Ratanakkiri."
* Agriculture: Ratanakkiri province has favorable potential for crop cultivation, especially agro-industrial crops and animal husbandry. Significant achievements in the agricultural sector in 2019 include:
In 2019, the country exported 87,604 tons of agricultural products worth nearly 37 million US dollars. At the same time, in the province, there are 7 rubber processing factories and 9 rubber handicraft factories, and the average amount of crumb rubber is about 30,479 tons / year, and 1 cassava processing factory is processing semi-finished products for export. Exit.
A total of 230 investment companies, factories, handicrafts, businesses and private establishments in the province have played a key role in creating job opportunities and are employing about 11,136 workers and 39 NGOs operating in the province. Currently, there is a need for more than 2,000 workers in the agricultural and agro-industrial sectors.
In the first half of 2020, Ratanakkiri province also had a positive impact on the economy of the people in the province, in which the tourism sector has affected 19 businesses, karaoke massage services that have been suspended and affected the work of workers who Work on this service and other services about 20%.
* Education, Youth and Sports: There are a total of 427 schools in the province compared to 2018, an increase of 11 schools with a total of 58,488 students, including: 178 kindergartens, 222 primary schools, There are 27 secondary schools and 2 private universities training students in the province.
At the same time, in 2019, 2 new secondary schools were established and upgraded from secondary school to 2 more high schools to meet and reduce the maximum dropout rate at the lower secondary level.
* Provision of public health services: In the province, there are 2 referral hospitals with 192 beds, 27 health centers with a total staff of 433 people, including 3 specialist doctors and 32 doctors. Health services provided a total of 178,231 outpatient examinations and consultations compared to 2018, an increase of 4.24%, of which a total of 20,741 pregnancy examinations, a decrease compared to 2018 equal to 2.12 A total of 4,899 women gave birth.
* Mining and energy, rural water and sanitation: Currently, 2 companies are conducting metal exploration studies in Ratanakkiri province, requesting 5 licenses, Canada and Vietnam, and mining industry licenses for gold mining business. 01 License of India.
For the electricity sector, the province currently has 3 sources and generating power, including: generated by its own hydropower with a capacity of 1.26 MW (Ochum hydropower), purchasing power from Vietnam with a capacity of 12 MW and Sesan hydropower source 02 12 megawatts of power.
For clean water in the province, there are 4 private investment companies and service providers in 3 districts with a production capacity of 1,292,190 cubic meters per year, with an average production capacity of 3,540 cubic meters / day. Connect water to a total of 6,205 houses.
In particular, in rural areas in the province, there is a coverage rate of more than 60%, where people get clean water from various sources, such as wells, pumps, community water distribution systems, ponds, rainwater filters, water bottles, which are safe sources and Ensure the use of some irrigation supplies.
* Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs: Systematic Land Registration: The Department of Land has divided its working groups into 3 groups to survey and identify plots for registration and has issued certificates to 6 villages, equal to 3; 572 declarations of 9 villages, 1,930 certificates were distributed, 6,332 plots were demarcated, 8 villages were publicly posted and 5,878 plots were collected.
19 state-owned private investment companies have been registered, 17 indigenous community lands have been registered, and the province has now built a land use master plan for 1 city. Last year, there were 46 cases related to land issues and 30 cases were settled.
* Environment: Ratanakkiri Province has 7 protected areas and 1 biodiversity corridor, including Virachey National Park, O'Yadao National Park, Vern Sai-Siem Pang National Park, Lumphat Wildlife Sanctuary, Boeung Yaklom Conservation Area Boeung Yak Om and Yakara with a total area of 704,906 hectares.
All of these areas are rich in natural resources, biodiversity of all kinds, especially endangered species, wildlife and listed as vulnerable. At the same time, the department has encouraged the establishment of 10 nature protection communities in order to participate in the management, care, protection and conservation of natural resources.
Separately, the work of administration, security, public order and political security, Mr. Thong Savun affirmed that on behalf of the provincial authorities, the most important task is to maintain security, order and social security within the jurisdiction of the province to ensure harmony, both physically and mentally to the people. Citizens in the daily diet.
Mr. Net Pheaktra said that during the same 18 months, rangers of the Ministry of Environment and officials of the Wildlife Alliance and related institutions rescued 747 live animals and 206 dead wild animals and confiscated 169 vehicles. 43 bulldozers and tractors, 173 motorcycles, 271 bulldozers.
According to Mr. Net Pheaktra, during the same period, rangers of the Ministry of Environment and officials of the Wildlife Alliance and related institutions patrolled 7654 times day and night for a distance of 245,535 kilometers. Of these, 983 illegal huts were demolished, 2,179 cubic meters of timber were confiscated, 1,954 chainsaws were confiscated, and 32,322 traps were removed.
He added that the Ministry of Environment would like to express its gratitude and appreciation for the past cooperation and law enforcement of local authorities and stakeholders in Cambodia's natural areas, with the Wildlife Alliance focusing on protecting the potential of the environment. And natural resources in the Cardamom Mountains, especially in Koh Kong, Pursat and Kampong Speu provinces.
The spokesman confirmed that the Ministry of Environment and the Wildlife Alliance have signed a memorandum of understanding on cooperation in the protection and conservation of the Cardamom Mountains, which covers 1.4 million hectares, including the Tatai Wildlife Sanctuary. Peam Krasop Wildlife Sanctuary, South Cardamom Mountain National Park, Central Cardamom Mountain National Park, Central Botum Sakor National Park, etc.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra further stated that we currently have 69 protected areas on an area of 7.3 million hectares, which is an obligation that the Ministry of Environment requires good cooperation from all parties involved in Ensuring sustainability, protecting the potential of the environment and conserving our natural resources for the benefit of future generations.
(Phnom Penh): At the end of July 2020, the people living under the temporary Stung Meanchey flyover will move back to live on the legally owned land along the Stung Meanchey canal. Ready this July.
Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, presided over the workshop on Dissemination of Community Database Study Report on Stung Meanchey Canal and Strategic Support for Urban Planning, Urbanization and Land Management. This morning, July 13, 2020 at Phnom Penh Capital Hall.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said that in the last two decades, Phnom Penh has developed in all areas, with economic growth, vehicle growth, population growth as well. At the same time, people also migrated to live in Phnom Penh by mistake, as Cambodia has integrated, causing some people to build houses on public land of the state.
He added that the Stung Meanchey canal was also inhabited by hundreds of families, which blocked the flow of water and caused flooding in the western part of Phnom Penh.
So far, the construction of Stung Meanchey canal is nearing completion, that is, at the end of July 2020, the people who were evacuated to stay under the Stung Meanchey bridge temporarily, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will let them come. They live on their legally owned land, which the Prime Minister has given them on a plot of land along the Stung Meanchey canal.
Mr. Khuong Sreng also stated that in relation to the development of poor communities, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has settled with more than 100 families, equivalent to 87 houses in Banteay Sleuk community, where they live on Public Road 434, Village 4, Sangkat Boeung Keng Kang Dam more than 20 years ago.
