England invades Wales, but loses to Scotland
* Britain and Scotland form an alliance to become the "United Kingdom"
Even though Scotland and Britain had one king at the time, the two countries were still two kingdoms with separate politics and parliaments. For about a century there were some attempts to unite the two kingdoms into one nation, but without success. It was not until 1707 that Britain and Scotland formed an alliance to become the United Kingdom under Queen Anne.
Britain makes sister alliance with Ireland, but South Ireland secedes
According to Professor Whatley, Britain used the 1707 alliance with Scotland as a model for the 1801 alliance with Ireland. However, the sisterhood did not last long. Between 1919 and 1921, the army of the Republic of Ireland rose up to fight for independence from Britain. The war ended with Ireland being divided into the North and the South in 1922.
Northern Ireland remained part of the United Kingdom, while Southern Ireland became a separate liberal state. In 1937, Southern Ireland also became a fully sovereign country, or Republic of Ireland, and in 1973 joined the European Union and continues to this day. The United Kingdom has just left the European Union.
