(Kampong Speu): Lieutenant General Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the Land Forces, said:
A strong nation is based on a strong defense sector and a strong defense sector due to a strong army.
He said this during a meeting with trainees of the second generation of military training to complete the framework for the Military School under the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces 2020, Royal Cambodian Armed Forces Techo Sen Phnom Thom, Preah Preav, Kampong Speu province on July 11, 2020.
"A strong nation is based on strong defense, and strong defense is due to our strong army," said Hun Manet. "The previous generation of officers left a legacy of national defense for our national cause today, so we must continue to preserve this legacy on the basis of spirit, will, experience and combined with practical ability."
He added that training soldiers to have a clear foundation is the most important factor that makes our army strong and can defend our homeland in the long run. Training must be based on two factors: first, patriotism, religion, monarchy, and second, the ability to be self-reliant. This is the spirit of nationalism to increase self-confidence in assuring ownership of our future.
Mr. Hun Manet continued that the military has a very important role and the military career has two features, including:
1: We have been directly involved in national service by educating our soldiers on the basis of self-defense, as well as defending the unit, ensuring success in carrying out its duties, which is the pride of contributing to national defense through Training of outstanding heroes.
2: The military receives the honor that is engraved in the heart of every student as a benefactor who has given them knowledge.
On that occasion, he also thanked the leadership of the Army of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, relevant units-institutions, the course management, the military, as well as officers, deputies and all soldiers of the 70th Brigade for their cooperation. Organize and make this training run well and thank all the military candidates who volunteered and actively participated in this training as well.
