(Banteay Meanchey): A group of four people left their hometown in Pursat province to cross the border to work in Thailand, but when they arrived at the border, they were robbed of 8,000 baht. Samnang escaped and the border police helped him to get food, water and money just to return home.
According to the Poipet Police Station, the incident happened on July 11, 2020, under the Cambodia-Thailand Friendship Bridge in Kbal Spean 1 Village, Sangkat Poipet, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
According to the victims, before the incident, they traveled from Pursat province in order to find work in Thailand. At the Poipet roundabout, they met an unidentified man, about 30 years old, who asked them to cross the border by a short charge of 3,000 baht per person, and they agreed to go with him. When they reached the mouth of a stream on the Thai side, the man left them and took 8,000 baht to escape.
After the incident, the mobile inspection force intervened and brought the victims to the unit to educate and provide them with food and donated 1,000 baht to them to return home to the province. Pursat.
As for the suspect who escaped, the police force is looking for him to take legal action.
