According to a press release from the European Parliament (EP), the new law will temporarily exempt certain methods of vaccine testing with 505 votes in favor, 67 against and 109 abstentions after the debate. An emergency was made last week.
The European Commission last June outlined a new strategy for vaccine production, calling for a moratorium on certain bans on clinical trials or treatment of COVID-19 patients through genetic modification. Organisms by engineering techniques (GMOs).
It should be noted that due to the fact that each member state in the European Union always requires risk assessment of drug trials and vaccines by GMOs, this has led to delays in previous vaccination tests. Therefore, the new European law is expected to facilitate as well as cut down on the development of vaccines to save lives in a timely manner.
