This morning, the Royal Academy of Cambodia organized a scientific forum on "Cambodia-US relations"
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Saturday, July 11, 2020, the Royal Academy of Cambodia organized a scientific forum on "Cambodia-US relations" to celebrate the 70th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between the two countries.
This forum aims to reflect on the relationship between the past 70 years and the expectations for the next 70 years. The forum was also attended by Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, Patrick Muffy, US Ambassador to Cambodia, and Dr. Hing Thoraksy, Permanent Secretary of the Office of the Council of Ministers.
Today's forum also features a panel discussion by expert speakers on Cambodia-US relations. The speakers included both government and US embassy officials.
The US Representative Office opened in Phnom Penh on November 14. The prestigious Le Royal Hotel was the first office of the US Embassy until an embassy and a US Information Library were established in a new location.
The Embassy was upgraded to an Embassy on June 25, 1952, at which time Heath became the first US Ambassador to Cambodia. After the connection in the 1950s, relations between Cambodia and the United States were seen to be much better.
But by the end of the 1960s, relations seemed to be strained and murky, and the two countries severed ties in 1965. The secession was due to the US involvement in the Vietnam War, and Cambodia accused the United States of invading and bombing Cambodian territory.
The United States, on the other hand, accuses Cambodia of providing ports and allowing Vietnamese communist troops to transport military equipment through Cambodian territory. But that relationship was restored in 1969, with the United States reopening its embassy in Phnom Penh. By 1970, relations between Cambodia and the United States were much better after a coup d'état overthrew Norodom Sihanouk by Lon Nol.
By 1975, when Cambodia was occupied by the Khmer Rouge, relations between Cambodia and the United States were severed again. After the fall of the Khmer Rouge regime, a new government was formed with Vietnamese support. A government that the United States does not like and has imposed more economic sanctions.
In 1990, relations between Cambodia and the United States were restored, with the United States lifting economic sanctions and providing development assistance to Cambodia. It was then that the American flag was hoisted again in Phnom Penh.
In 1997, relations between Cambodia and the United States deteriorated again. This situation is due to the bombing of the protesters led by Sam Rainsy and the brief fighting between the army of Samdech Krom Preah Norodom Ranariddh and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the first and second prime ministers.
Between 2000 and 2010, relations between Cambodia and the United States improved. The United States has provided a lot of assistance to Cambodia, and in 2006 the United States inaugurated a new embassy building in Phnom Penh. Since then, leaders as well as senior US officials have visited Cambodia remarkably.
In response to the US action, Cambodia responded strongly, "What Cambodia is doing internally and following Cambodian law." However, relations between Cambodia seem to have improved slightly after Patrick Muffy took over as ambassador to Cambodia in late 2019, until a correspondence between US President Donald Trump and Samdech Techo Hun Sen revealed. From enhancing relationships to improving.
* In 2016, the Cambodian-US trade volume appeared to decrease slightly to US $ 2.320 million, but Cambodian-US exports continued to increase to US $ 2.147 billion, while US imports to Cambodia were only 173 million. Million dollars only.
* In 2018, the trade volume between Cambodia and the United States was 3.438 million US dollars, of which Cambodia exported 3,051 million US dollars, while the United States imported only 386 million US dollars.
In the first half of 2019, the trade volume between Cambodia and the United States was $ 2.195 million, of which Cambodia exported $ 1.89 billion, while the United States imported only $ 304 million.
