He added that the rural sanitation situation is a major challenge in the public health sector of the people in the community on regular sanitation practices to lead to change from unhygienic to hygienic living. To improve public health and improve their livelihoods in rural communities.
Changes in access to clean water and regular use of toilets have really contributed to improving community hygiene and preventing the spread of diseases when people turn to clean drinking water and regular use of toilets. It has also contributed to reducing poverty and boosting the national economy.
