Medtecs is one of the suppliers selected through a competitive procurement process conducted by PPFD and has been awarded a $ 5 million contract to manufacture shoe covers and protective clothing for distribution. Frontline health workers in 11 developing countries.
The company has been operating in Cambodia since 1999 and has 5,500 employees in a factory in Kampong Cham province. About 82% of the company's employees are women. The plant provides stable employment for Cambodians living there and contributes to the local economy, which is particularly important as Cambodia is being affected by the COVID-19 impact.
The company spent about a month expanding its operations to meet global PPE demand for a total of nearly 1.2 million textile production. The company currently has a monthly production capacity of 8 million protective clothing, 2.5 million protective suits and 4 million shoe covers. The goods passed the inspection by an independent third party and began shipping out of Cambodia in late June for shipment to various destination countries.
