The report of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Police also claimed that on the day of the incident, the Lumphat District Council organized a forum to disseminate and consult with the people, and there were 94 participants. Separately, Chhorn Phalla was not invited to participate.
At the beginning of the ceremony, Chhorn Phalla came to disrupt the work of the public administration of the government by grabbing the microphone without the permission of the chairman of the ceremony, talking about the subject of defamation, accusing the people and the authorities in various ways, causing the people Anger erupted in protest with this person, causing chaos in the ceremony.
Authorities immediately detained residents to restore order, but Chhorn Phalla continued to defame, videotap and take photographs of people and authorities during the ceremony. Authorities then confiscated the person's phone to maintain order, then reported to the prosecutor for guidelines.
Prosecutors also ordered the man to be summoned for questioning in connection with the incident, but he refused to cooperate with authorities and ran upstairs and locked the door.
