The Minister explained to the public the main points related to the situation of Kovid-19 disease in Cambodia as follows:
* From the point of view of public health, the "first wave" refers to the curve of the spread of infectious diseases, which increased due to the large-scale transmission of the disease in the community and then decreased to near zero. Implementation of public health measures.
* Cambodia does not have a positive increase in the number of positive cases of Kovid-19 virus causing waves, as occurs in other countries in the world. On the contrary, we are in the early stages with positive cases of Kovid-19, most of which are imported cases.
Kovid-19 is a deadly fire and we must prevent it from spreading.
There are currently more than 11 million positive cases of Kovid-19 virus worldwide and more than half a million deaths reported to the World Health Organization as of today. The virus is spreading like wildfire around the world, so Cambodia remains at risk as long as the virus continues to spread around the world.
* This is why strict tests are being carried out at the border as people enter the country. Border control measures and 14-day screening are essential to prevent an increase in the number of positive cases of Kovid-19 virus in Cambodia.
* We all need to be very careful that among the people who are susceptible to this virus, like a single spark, it can ignite and spread.
But if we are all very careful, avoid congregations, avoid close relationships and cramped spaces, we must reduce the risk of transmitting the disease from one person to another. If we wash our hands regularly and wear a mask when necessary, as well as maintain individual safety gaps, we can prevent infection and reduce the chances of it spreading in the event of a spark.
3: We must all work in unity
* Cambodia cannot completely cut itself off from the world, and it is even more important that the Cambodian economy be considered strong.
* We know that the effects of this epidemic are huge on families, society and the economy, and people are anxious and tired. But in this circumstance, it is very difficult to satisfy or please everyone as long as the virus continues to spread somewhere that no country and no one is safe if we do not work together. Preventive measures.
* In addition to government measures, individuals, communities and businesses must continue to make healthy choices and take preventative measures - including good hand hygiene and respiratory hygiene practices at least 1.5 meters from Others will stay home if suspicious symptoms are necessary.
* We must all work together to ensure that each case does not become a flame and does not develop into a fire the next time. If we act in solidarity, we can prevent Cambodia from spreading the disease on a large scale in the community, as we have seen in some countries around the world.
Together to prevent the transmission of Kovid-19 virus, it is the duty of every individual to keep the community free of this deadly disease. The Cambodian Cement Industry Association claims that the cement plant remains sustainable and maintains normal employment for workers despite the Kovid 19 crisis.
