(Phnom Penh): From September 2020 onwards, vehicle transfer owners will no longer be as difficult as they are now. The Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) has partnered with the General Department of Taxation to connect the transfer system to the tax payment system, which allows the transfer of ownership and taxation to take place in one place without the need to carry documents.
Currently, the transfer of ownership of a vehicle is more complicated than the procedures and filing. Vehicle owners have to carry documents running up and down many institutions ready. At least after completing the required documents at the Ministry of Public Works, the vehicle owner must run to the General Department of Taxation.
Due to these complexities, the purchase of vehicles in the past is less likely to transfer ownership between the old and new owners. This non-transfer of ownership leads to many complications when traffic problems or other crimes.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol and Mr. Kong Vibol, Royal Government Delegate, strongly hope that the technology of providing services through the workflow, the process of transferring ownership of vehicles through this technology system will run smoothly and contribute significantly to the strengthening of management. Provide public services, transportation management and national security data management, as well as strengthen fiscal revenue collection.
The joint procedure for the transfer of ownership of the vehicle will be determined by an inter-ministerial prakas between the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and the Ministry of Economy and Finance, which is scheduled to be validated and put into use in September 2020. Ministry of Foreign Affairs announces the results of the 13th Mekong-Japan Foreign Ministers' Meeting via Video
