Senior official of the Ministry of Public Works: The construction of the third ring road has reached about 40%!
(Phnom Penh): On the occasion of leading the working group to inspect the progress of the construction of the third ring road on July 9, 2020, Mr. Lim Sidenin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, on behalf of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport. As of now, the construction of the third ring road has been completed by about 40%, the transport said.
Mr. Lim Sidenin said that through the quality inspection without letting the company know in advance, it was seen that the quality at the bridge site is still a little lacking, but not a problem by the company. Promise to make strong and accurate technical specifications, and for the foundation of the construction of this road is in accordance with the technical standards set by the Ministry.
Mr. Lim Sidenin said that the construction project of the third ring road (National Road No. 4-National Road No. 1) is located in Phnom Penh and Kandal provinces with a total length of nearly 53 kilometers, including through more than 15 Phnom Penh. Km and passing through Kandal province, almost 38 km long, starting from km 14 + 105 of National Road No. 4 and ending point at km 24 + 840 of National Road No. 1.
He said that the third ring road is up to 27 meters wide for downtown and 25 meters wide for out-of-town. The road will have street lights for city streets and ornamental trees for suburban roads. The Third Ring Road is an important road to reduce congestion and accidents in the past and facilitate travel and traffic in the capital.
Please note that this third ring road will have 4 flyovers (crossing National Roads 4, 3, 2 and 21) with a total length of 1,000 meters. Construction of 2 bridges across the Bassac River at Anlong Chen Island with a total length of 996 meters (including the 630-meter-long East Bassac Bridge and the 366-meter-long West Bassac Bridge). Construction of 6 medium and short bridges and 113 sewers of all kinds.
The construction of the third ring road is expected to cost a total of 273 million US dollars, a concessional financing from the Chinese government, and the Royal Government of Cambodia contributes to the impact of demining and unexploded ordnance, taxes and royalties.
