Earth is the third largest planet in the solar system, and the average distance from Earth to the Sun is 150 million kilometers. The longest distance is 152 million kilometers and the nearest distance is 147 million kilometers.
The diameter of the sun is about 1.39 million kilometers, 109 times the size of the earth, and its mass is about 330,000 times that of our earth. This means that if you put the sun on the scales, you would need 333,000 objects weighing the earth in order for it to be in proportion.
Without the sun, the earth would not be able to survive, since the sun emits the light and heat that the earth needs to survive. The sun rotates once every 27 days. Our Earth orbits the Sun for 365 days in space.
It should be noted that the sun is a star that shines in a single space, and even the moon does not shine on its own, in general, it receives light from the sun and, in other words, God The moon is like a mirror that reflects light from the sun to the earth at night. Residents of 3 Sangkats in Khemarak Phoumin City Congratulate and Praise the Municipal Authority for Solving Their Problems
