Chinese State Councilor Wang Yi points out three key points to restore Sino-US relations
BEIJING: Chinese State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi outlined three key points that could improve Sino-US relations and get back on track. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Thursday evening, July 9, 2020.
At a video conference in Beijing on video conferencing with the China-US Research Institute on Thursday, Wang Yi highlighted three key points that could restore ties between the two economic giants. Yes.
The first is cooperation in various fields, with a clear definition of bilateral relations and global issues on which China and the United States can work together. Second, dialogue on all issues should be resolved by the United States and China through peaceful dialogue. The third is the resolution and management of issues that both sides can find common ground and reach.
