Mr. Khuong Sreng claimed that the Phnom Penh Capital Administration has implemented the process of providing cash to the poor and vulnerable people in the Kovid-19 crisis with the utmost care, that is, not to allow any relevant work to commit any irregularities. It does not happen, as there is no selection of one's own relatives or no embezzlement of the poor.
The Governor of Phnom Penh confirmed that through this effort, the process of providing cash flow went smoothly and received support from the people. At this point, we have banned the review of the families of the authorities, you have the right to judge that this person is poor, that person is poor, and if his family is placed, it is very investigative, so we have met with the authorities of the 105 districts To have feelings for one's relatives.
Ms. Mom Chandani, Director of the Department of Social Affairs, Former Youth and Youth Rehabilitation of Phnom Penh, said that as of this morning, July 9, Phnom Penh has achieved 93 percent on the process of providing cash to more than 18,000 poor people. There are only over 600 cards left that have not yet been received.
The above statement by Mr. Khuong Sreng and Ms. Mom Chandany was made at the 14th Ordinary Meeting of Phnom Penh Capital Council on the morning of July 9, 2020 at Phnom Penh Capital Hall.
