(Svay Rieng): Mr. Men Vibol, Governor of Svay Rieng Province, said that in all criminal cases being handled by the prosecution and the court, it should be implemented as soon as possible in order to punish the perpetrators as soon as possible and provide justice to the victims.
This was stated by the provincial governor at a meeting on law enforcement cooperation between the court, prosecutors and judicial police officers on strengthening public security, preventing and suppressing criminal offenses on the morning of July 9, 2020.
The ceremony was attended by Mr. Leav Piseth, Deputy Secretary General of the Ministry of Justice, Mr. Kham Sophary, Prosecutor of the Provincial Court, Mr. Din Sivuthy, President of the Provincial Court, General Commissioner of the Provincial Gendarmerie and Deputy Prosecutor. Judges, civil servants, forces and judicial police officers as well.
He called on all relevant units, including the judiciary, the prosecution and the judiciary, to double their cooperation in law enforcement in the operation to crack down on criminals and bring the perpetrators to justice. There are crimes, one of which is aimed at maintaining security and social stability, and the other is to increase people's trust in the authorities and the judiciary.
Mr. Men Vibol also requested to participate and cooperate to help each other on the procedure to perform their duties and responsibilities, when the competent officials, judicial police officers to send the case there is any shortage. Court officials help to make sure that the perpetrators carry out their sentences.
In performing their duties, all judicial police officers are required to perform their duties and responsibilities properly and strictly in accordance with the provisions set out in the Code of Criminal Procedure, without having to go beyond the jurisdiction of the law. Both the investigation of actual crimes, the initial investigation work, including arrests, referrals, arrests, searches related to actual crimes, searches of non-specific crimes, and so on.
All operations of judicial police officers are to be reported and coordinated with the prosecutor.
