(Koh Kong): On July 9, 2020, the Ministry of Environment and Wildlife Alliance organized a two-day visit for journalists to the Cardamom Mountain Forest to visit the Mountain Forest Protection Program. Cardamom is a joint project of the Ministry of Environment and the Wildlife Alliance to protect the 1.4 million-hectare Cardamom Forest and to improve the livelihoods of communities.
During the visit, reporters were invited to review the achievements of the Cardamom Mountains Forest Protection Program to better understand the challenges that rangers of the Ministry of Environment - Wildlife Alliance in the field are facing. During the performance of his duties.
In the last 18 months alone, rangers from the Cardamom Forest Protection Program have patrolled 6,545 times, covering 245,000 kilometers.
Officials' efforts paid off, removing 32,322 traps, seizing 1,954 chainsaws, seizing 2,178 cubic meters of illegal timber, arresting 87 suspects and sending them to court. Delivered 1,019 units and prevented 172 cases of encroachment on state land.
During the visit, the participants also visited the Jiphat Ecotourism Community, an international winning project that opened in 2008.
