Wastewater from Khmer Breweries 8-stage cleaning with modern waste cleaning system
(Phnom Penh): Khmer Breweries has a liquid waste cleaning system imported from France and has the ability to clean liquid waste in accordance with national and international standards, making the production of this company's products with high responsibility for the environment and society.
This liquid waste cleaning system operates in 8 stages, which makes the wastewater treatment almost 100% clean. The eight stages include:
First, liquid waste from all parts of the factory is discharged into wastewater storage tanks.
Third, the water is filtered one step at a time to remove solids larger than 3 mm.
Fifth, the water is cleaned using a system that does not need air.
Sixth: Water is sent to be cleaned by a system that needs air.
Eighth: Finally, it is cleaned with phosphate according to the standard set by the Ministry of Environment and then discharged into the environment.
It should be noted that Khmer Breweries pays great attention to the environment of the community around the factory to ensure that its investment is sustainable.
