(Phnom Penh): Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, on July 9, 2020, issued a notification on the weather conditions (dry season), stating that the dry season will occur in mid-July. Reduces rainfall.
An announcement from the Ministry of Water Resources, obtained by Fresh News on the morning of July 9, states that after monitoring a series of global and regional climate developments, it appears that this July ( From the middle of the month to the end of the month) high pressure has been increasing its impact on the western Pacific Ocean.
As a result, countries in the region such as Thailand, Cambodia, Vietnam, Laos, Myanmar and the Philippines have reduced their rainfall levels.
The Ministry of Water Resources emphasizes, "We would like to inform the public, especially the farmers, to be informed and take care to maintain and use water well for daily life as well as crop production."
