On April 29, 2011, US President Barack Obama authorized the SEAL Team Six to launch an operation to invade Osama bin Laden's hideout. They immediately began rehearsing for the actual operation, which included practicing in a location built to resemble bin Laden's hideout.
12:30 a.m. - Both helicopters landed at bin Laden's hideout in Abbottabad. At that time, a helicopter crashed but did not cause any injuries and the mission continued as usual without any obstruction.
00:53 AM - Obama receives initial reports that bin Laden has been found dead.
04:01 a.m. - Obama receives further information that the body is likely to be bin Laden.
