(Phnom Penh): A spokesman for the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training said that at least 10 factories have applied to transform some parts of their production line into mass production.
This statement was made on the morning of July 8, 2020 on the occasion of the Economic and Financial Policy Committee held a press conference at the Ministry of Economy.
Heng Sour stated: "So far, we have more than 10 factories have proposed to change parts of its production line to mass production. "Mass production requires a short production line and does not require much labor, but it is cost-effective and the volume of exports is large."
