As is my custom, when cycling, I always listen to foreign radio broadcast in Khmer to listen to the news and want to know what they say about Cambodia. Last month, I heard on a foreign radio station in Khmer covering the 19 cases of Kovid in Vietnam. The broadcast praised the Vietnamese government's response to measures and measures to prevent Kovid 19.
According to the radio station, the Vietnamese authorities' measures to close the country, close schools, canteens, entertainment venues and other government responses have made Vietnam successful in combating 19 cases of smallpox. .
On the night of July 7, the radio also broadcast a small case of 19 cases of Kovid in Cambodia. But in this broadcast, they did not praise the actions of the Royal Government of Cambodia as praising the Vietnamese government. The small number of infections in Cambodia is considered to be due to luck, fearful people, and on the other hand, from neighboring countries, Cambodia has taken good action, so Cambodia is influenced by those actions.
VOA Khmer's Men Kimseng, who co-authored the article, quoted an expert on American social analysts and pro-government dissidents as expressing their views.
US experts say they do not believe that Cambodia can prevent 19 cases of Kovid, because the country's health system is weak, while his country (the United States), which is strong in almost everything, has Infected with this global disease, more than any other country in the world.
In this broadcast, they did not meet with professional officials or government officials, and they did not mention even the slightest action of the Royal Government of Cambodia from the beginning of the year until now to fight against Kovid 19 disease.
To combat Kovid 19, since a case was discovered in Sihanoukville in January, the head of the Royal Government immediately held a press conference on the disease, then measures were taken in schools to prevent Kovid 19. By cleaning, washing hands and so on.
Subsequently, when a series of cases were discovered as cases of infection from abroad, the Royal Government introduced other measures, such as closing the country, closing the New Year, closing schools, closing karaoke, closing clubs, closing cinemas, and banning gatherings. The closure of flights from high-traffic countries in Europe, the United States and Iran, as well as measures to install heaters and sanitation measures at the entrances to the country, followed.
National and inter-ministerial commissions have been set up to prepare for the timely response, prevention and control of Kovid 19. Educational videos and songs on the implementation of Kovid 19 hygiene measures have been produced in large numbers and widely disseminated. Propaganda was set up in villages to spread awareness about the prevention of Kovid 19.
The National Working Group of the Royal Government distributes leaflets to the backs of people's houses. In addition, the head of the Royal Government came out to call almost every day on social media to remind people to pay attention to health care and beware of Kovid 19.
So far, despite the easing of closure measures, sanitation and prevention measures for Kovid 19 have continued to be strengthened.
A team of volunteer doctors was mobilized to fight 19 Kovid. The national budget has been released to stockpile equipment to fight Kovid 19. Royal budget of the King and Queen Mother of Cambodia, leaders of the highest institutions of the nation and civil servants of the Armed Forces jointly donate funds to the Royal Government to the Commission for the Prevention of Kovid 19 to operate against Kovid 19.
Is this not an action, not a Royal Government action to fight and prevent Kovid 19? Are not these actions and measures that led to the small number of Kovid 19 cases in Cambodia?
This statement is not a criticism, it just wants to reflect the advertising and technical nature of foreign radio broadcasters.
On the other hand, we can not blame the media. His reporters have no choice, even though he is a Khmer-speaking Cambodian living in the United States, and the radio is sponsored and funded by the United States. By the way they drew it.
Fortunately, the rich media in Cambodia today is not as small as it was in the 1960s or 1970s. Therefore, these foreign radios can no longer cause rainstorms to deceive the ears and eyes of the Cambodian people.
By: Phnom Penh Governor told more than 100 families to build houses in violation of the drainage canal must be removed by themselves before the authorities take action
(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, this morning, July 08, 2020, inspected the five drainage pumping stations, the five drainage canals and the Boeung Ha canal in Sangkat Stung Meanchey 3, Khan Meanchey and Khan Dangkor. It was found that some people have built houses in violation of the canal.
Mr. Khuong Sreng instructed the relevant officials of the local authority to clearly identify the public land of the state and the land belonging to the people, while the above canal was violated by some villagers on the canal with the filling of the canal. Take ownership, too.
In addition, the Governor of Phnom Penh affirmed that it is the position of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration to establish a working group with the participation of the Cadastral Office of the Khan, Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh to spray the location and make instructions. People who violate the above canal to dismantle.
Mr. Khuong Sreng stated that the drainage canal is very important for the general population, for people living in rural areas engaged in farming. For people in Phnom Penh, drainage canals are also very important because they can relieve the flooding of people living in the city very well.
According to the local authority, the five drainage canals are 50 meters wide, leaving more than 100 families on each side, including 35 families in Russey 1 village, Stung Meanchey 3 commune, and 76 Russey 2 villages. Family. They built illegal houses on the canal.
It should be noted that the five sewage pumping stations are located at three intersections, three districts: Meanchey, Por Senchey and Dangkor. The canal plays an important role in relieving flooding from many areas in these three districts.
