The inclusion of the Sambor Prei Kuk temple site as a World Heritage Site is a great honor for the entire Cambodian nation, as this unique cultural heritage has become one of the greatest potentials in contributing to national economic development through the sector. Tourism.
Mr. Sok Lou also claimed that all these reasons require the young people who are the successors of bamboo to be grateful to the ancestors who have worked hard to build such a rich cultural heritage for the next generation and together to maintain.
He also said that during the three years of the Sambor Prei Kuk temple site as a World Heritage Site, he observed that Kampong Thom province has attracted a significant increase in the number of national and international tourists, including visitors. They want to see this wonderful heritage.
At the same time, Mr. Prak Sovannara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, confirmed that the inclusion of Sambor Prei Kuk Temple as a World Heritage Site is very important and very proud for Kampong Thom to attract national and international tourists to visit.
