(Phnom Penh): As of now, the payment of allowances to poor and vulnerable people during the period of Kovid-19 has reached 2 million people, equivalent to 500,000 families, according to Mr. Sam Heng Boros, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs. Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation on July 08, 2020.
Mr. Sam Heng Boros made the statement at a press conference on measures to support, restore and promote economic growth and cash support programs for poor and vulnerable families during the Kovid-19 period, chaired by Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance. Objects organized by the Ministry of Economy and Finance this morning, July 08, 2020.
Mr. Sam Heng Boros also said that the first round will be implemented from June 24, 2020 to July 24, 2020, so the remaining people are invited to open before the deadline. For those who have already opened, please go to open the second round from July 25 to August 24, 2020, which is the second month of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Responding to some quarters about the recklessness of the Royal Government, Mr. Sam Heng Boros said that what the Royal Government is trying to do so far is to continue to think and the Ministry of Planning continues to receive applications from people who meet. Difficulties during Kovid-19, and it is estimated that 3-4 thousand more families will enter the program in the second round.
(Phnom Penh): According to Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Secretary of State at the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Cambodia's poverty rate has recovered due to the effects of the Kovid 19 crisis.
Speaking at a conference on measures to support, rehabilitate and promote economic growth and the Royal Government of Cambodia's cash subsidy program for poor and vulnerable families this morning, July 8, 2020, the senior official stated, "We can not deny that "There is Kovid and there is no increase in the poor, but how can he not die of starvation, it is difficult for him to live for economic opportunities and jobs, he can recover."
The poverty rate of the Cambodian people before the 19 19 outbreak of Kovid was estimated below 11%, but now in the face of this devastating epidemic, the rate will rise again.
