(Phnom Penh): The Asian Development Bank (ADB) on July 8 approved a $ 250 million loan to help the Royal Government of Cambodia respond to the Coronavirus (COVID-19) epidemic by strengthening the immune system. Health in the country increases social assistance to the poor and vulnerable, as well as provides economic support for businesses, including small and medium enterprises.
According to a press release from the Asian Development Bank (ADB) received by Fresh News on July 8, 2020, this support will help the Royal Government of Cambodia to reduce the negative impact of this epidemic on health, society and economy. .
"Cambodia is particularly vulnerable to the negative effects of COVID-19 due to its open economy, narrow economic base and large mobile population," the statement said.
The ADB expects the Cambodian economy to contract at around 5.5% by 2020 due to a decline in tourism, lower exports of clothing, footwear and travel accessories, and a slowdown in construction activity. The risk of a recession could plunge another 1.3 million people into poverty.
These include support for the health system to prevent the escalation of COVID-19 cases, and for workers and enterprises, including a $ 150 million capital injection to support banks lending to small and medium-sized businesses.
The CPRO was initiated through ADB assistance, which was extended to $ 20 billion on April 13 for developing countries in response to epidemics.
The program includes a participatory framework of supported countries to ensure that governments and ADBs continue policy discussions on the implementation and monitoring of Cambodia's response to COVID-19. The framework also includes consultations with the private sector and civil society organizations.
The program also links ADB's current support activities for public financial management reform to strengthen governance and transparency, as well as increase policy and budgeting, expenditure monitoring and auditing.
The CARE program was developed in coordination with development partners and complements ADB's current support to supply temperature monitoring equipment for international checkpoints and to ensure regular updates to the Ministry of Health website, which displays monitoring reports. COVID-19 and other relevant information daily.
