National Bank of Cambodia Introduces Three Measures to Support Kovid Affected Banking 19
This is according to the report of the meeting to review the work results of the first half of the year and the work direction of the second half of 2020 of the National Bank of Cambodia, which was held on July 7, 2020 with the participation of Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia. Of Cambodia.
Mr. Chea Chanto said that as risks to the economy have increased, risk monitoring in the banking sector has been strengthened in addition to risk and future outlook. Three measures in support of the banking sector for the effects of Kovid 19 include:
He said the global economy was being severely affected by the 19 epidemic of Kovid, and that the Cambodian economy was also adversely affected, especially in tourism, manufacturing and construction. The Royal Government, under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has set out effective measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
At the same time, support measures for affected sectors and vulnerable populations have been put in place, which have reduced the impact and maintained the sustainability of businesses and people's livelihoods.
He said the balance of payments was estimated to be in surplus as financial account inflows could still offset the widening current account deficit caused by declining tourism earnings and remittances from foreign workers. International reserves maintain a high level, which can guarantee the import of goods and services for the next 10 months, higher than the minimum level for developing countries should be (3 months).
Mr. Chea Chanto said that for the implementation of monetary policy, the National Bank of Cambodia has reduced the reserve requirement ratio on deposits and non-resident loans to 7%, which can provide additional liquidity to banking and financial institutions.
Meanwhile, the network of operations and financial services has been continuously developed, with the number of offices and branches of banking and financial institutions nationwide increasing to 2,465, and ATMs with 3,081 customer accounts. Increased to 8.2 million accounts and credit accounts to 3.2 million.
He said that with the advancement of financial technology, the payment system has been modernized to be more efficient, secure and affordable. Bakong system and retaliation system have been put into preliminary operation and are scheduled to be officially launched soon.
Meanwhile, QR code standards are being developed with the aim of facilitating cross-border payments between payment service providers and implementing payment connectivity schemes with countries in the region.
The National Bank of Cambodia continues to manage cash flow efficiently and safely to meet the needs of people across the country. The use of the riel increased significantly in 2019 and the beginning of 2020, reflected by a 36.4% increase in currency in circulation and an increase in the credit ratio in riel to 13% of total loans.
