Kampong Chhnang Agricultural Community Market sells chemical-free agricultural products and does not increase prices during the 19th season.
(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Ngin Hun, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kampong Chhnang Province, confirmed that the Agricultural Community Market in Kampong Chhnang City did not have a price increase during the Kovid 19 season, which is on the rise, and the supply of vegetables, fish and meat. Enough is not lacking.
Speaking to Fresh News Agency in Kampong Chhnang province this morning, July 8, 2020, Mr. Ngin Hun continued that along with the agricultural community market in Kampong Chhnang city, there was no increase in price when the 19 Kovid explosion occurred, there were a small number of vendors Took the opportunity to sell goods at exorbitant prices, but was stopped in time.
"In Kampong Chhnang City, under the initiative of establishing the Community Agricultural Market by Mr. Chhour Chandoeun, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, located in Tuol Kralanh Village, Sangkat Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Chhnang City, all agricultural products have no price increase, no chemicals, trusted by "People, consumers."
The establishment of this market has also helped the livelihood of the community to sell, and people benefit from buying organic vegetables that are bought to eat healthy because there is no use of chemical fertilizers, people also eat The health benefits of growers also make money, and the market for agricultural products runs normally every day without any hindrance.
The director of the department urged farmers in all farming communities to grow vegetables, raise chickens, ducks, pigs, cows twice as much to supply the market and not to use chemicals or fertilizers. If the provincial agriculture department finds that any agricultural community is stealing chemicals, the department will stop that community immediately, because today people are trusting the agricultural community market by rushing to buy in large numbers.
Please note that this agricultural community market has 48 communities throughout the province, in which part of the farmers' crops to supply the community market in the province and the other part has a contract to sell to Phnom Penh. The Deputy Prime Minister of Cambodia thanked all development partners for providing financial assistance to the Royal Government to prevent Kovid-19.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, thanked all development partners for providing financial assistance to the Royal Government of Cambodia to prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease and rehabilitation. And boost economic growth after Kovid-19.
This thanks was made on the occasion that Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Chairman of the Public Financial Management Reform Steering Committee, chaired a meeting of the Public Financial Management Reform Steering Committee meeting with development partners on July 7, 2020 at Office of the Ministry of Economy.
The meeting discussed: 1: Annual Progress Report 2019 of the implementation of the Public Financial Management Reform Program, Phase 3 and 2: Response to the comments of development partners on the Annual Progress Report 2019 of the implementation of the program Public Financial Management Form Phase III.
Organized by video, the meeting was attended by leaders and members of the Public Financial Management Reform Steering Committee, representatives of development partners (EU, World Bank, Asian Development Bank, International Monetary Fund and UNICEF) and NGO representatives as well.
1: Progress in 2019 of the implementation of the Public Financial Management Reform Program, Phase 3: Implementation of the Public Financial Management Reform in 2019, achieved good progress in all areas of the Joint Action Plan Framework, Phase 3 In that:
* The "Financial Accountability System" is being developed through the official launch of the Information Technology System for Public Financial Management (FMIS) in all General Departments of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the 25 Capital-Provincial Treasuries, 25 Departments of Economy and Finance, Capital-Province and 37 Ministries-Institutions
* "Linking budget to policy" has been changing the Cambodian budget system by strengthening and expanding the implementation of program budgets as a basis for ministries and institutions to use the budget as a tool to promote sectoral development.
As of 2019, the program budget has been implemented in all 18 ministries, institutions and provincial administrations. Other capital-provincial administrations will be implemented continuously until 2021.
* "In preparation for the next step or performance accountability", the Ministry of Economy and Finance has been preparing a new Law on Financial Management System, revised Sub-Decree No. 81 dated 16 November 1995 on the Establishment of Control Examine the finances of the state budget expenditures in the ministries, provinces, municipalities, autonomous cities of Phnom Penh and public organizations and Sub-Decree No. 82 dated 16 November 1995 on the General Regulations of Public Accounts.
* As a mechanism for supporting the implementation of a successful and sustainable public financial management reform program, CJV Trained civil servants of CJV And 1,059 ministries and institutions on economics and finance, and are conducting online training and strategic planning on capacity building and development within the framework of the fourth phase of the Public Financial Management Reform Program.
Overall, the Meeting considered that Cambodia's public financial management system is strong in preventing the economic crisis that may arise from external factors.
