(Foreign): For about a millennium, people often eat out, such as buying snacks on the street or taking a break while traveling at a street cafe.
In the West, the earliest modern restaurant models were mostly from France, along with the culinary revolution that began in Paris in the 18th century. But one of the earliest examples of real restaurant culture dates back to 600 years ago.
Trade was very busy between these northern and southern cities of the 12th century during the Song Dynasty. Restaurants in both cities are set up to serve southern food for those from the south, or to serve northern food for those from the north. This type of restaurant is considered to be the first restaurant in history.
Although the West and the East have had trade relations for centuries, there is no conclusive evidence that these early restaurant cultures in China and Japan influenced the concept of Establish a European restaurant or not.
The first French restaurants appeared in the 1760s-70s, a time when wealthy businessmen in Paris focused on eating something more special than ordinary food that ordinary people could eat, and soups. This health supplement is appealing to them.
