Senior Minister Kun Kim Asks WFP to Expand Disaster Information System
(Phnom Penh): The National Committee for Disaster Management and the World Food Program (WFP) on July 7, 2020, held a meeting and discussed the use of the "Advanced Information System Forum (PRISM)" to provide Information on disaster management.
The purpose of this meeting is to disseminate and promote the use of up-to-date information to local authorities to respond in a timely manner to disasters.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, welcomed Francesca Erdelmenn, World Food Program (WFP) Country Director for Cambodia, and her colleagues to their active efforts in the provinces and to promote the use of the PRISM system. National and sub-national institutions.
On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia and on behalf of the National Committee for Disaster Management, Senior Minister Kun Kim expressed his deep gratitude to the World Food Organization for its active contribution to Cambodia's development in all areas, including disaster management. .
The Senior Minister requested that the World Food Organization continue to call on other partner organizations to strengthen disaster management in Cambodia. The Senior Minister also requested that the World Food Program (WFP) continue to expand the "PRISM" platform to increase disaster management and timely response.
Francesca Erdelmenn, World Food Program (WFP) Country Director for Cambodia, who is nearing the end of her term in Cambodia, thanked the National Committee for Disaster Management. In particular, Senior Minister Kun Kim, who allowed her and her colleagues to pay a courtesy call to discuss the work, as well as to facilitate and provide good cooperation in various work in the past.
She informed Senior Minister Kun Kim that although she will end her term in Cambodia, she will work to help Cambodia strengthen its disaster response capacity.
Please be informed that "PRISM Breaking News Forum System" is a system for collecting information on disasters via phone / tablet as a platform to provide timely information to assist in monitoring, evaluating, updating the latest information, easy for users. And especially for decision makers. In addition, this forum is a place to integrate the flow of information of the Royal Government from relevant ministries to communicate with each other.
The "PRISM Breaking Information Forum" system was first piloted in Kampong Thom in 2016, and in 2018 the system was extended to provinces around the Tonle Sap Lake and along the Mekong River and coastal provinces.
Currently, Phnom Penh, Koh Kong, Pailin and Kep provinces have not yet launched the PRISM news platform.
