(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, requested the South Korean Ambassador to Cambodia, Mr. Park Heng Yeung, to continue to help promote the investment climate in Cambodia and attract more investors to Cambodia.
The Minister said that increasing the presence of South Korean investors in Cambodia not only contributes to the development of Cambodia and provides employment to the people of Cambodia, but also contributes to the improvement of Cambodian-South Korean relations. Also vibrant.
The request of the Minister of Commerce was made when he allowed Mr. Park Heng Yeung to pay a courtesy call and discuss some work at the Ministry of Commerce on July 7, 2020.
During the meeting, the Minister and the Ambassador stressed the importance of good relations between Cambodia and Korea, both economically, commercially and politically, which will drive the trade volume of the two countries to increase continuously to reach Announcing the start of negotiations on a Cambodia-Korea bilateral free trade agreement in the near future.
During the meeting, the Minister asked the Ambassador to help promote Cambodia's favorable investment climate to the Korean private sector to attract more investors. Especially for the processing of agricultural products, electronic components and automobiles to connect with regional and global supply chains, as well as investment in technology and e-commerce, areas where the Republic of Korea has high potential.
Please note that South Korea is a major investment and trade partner of Cambodia. Trade volume between Cambodia and South Korea has been steadily increasing, especially in recent years. In 2019, the trade volume between Cambodia and South Korea was nearly 9 million US dollars, an increase of more than 14 percent compared to 2018.
Cambodia's main exports to South Korea include: T-shirts, men's clothing, electronics, shoes, suitcases, aluminum foil, beverages, medical supplies (surgical cushions), tents and natural rubber. Imported goods from South Korea include trucks, natural mineral water blankets, blankets, electronics, bulldozers, nickel-plated sheets or sheets, processed fabrics, dyes and beauty products.
