This was stated by Mr. Em Chanmakara this morning, July 7, 2020, at the opening ceremony of the seminar on "All Forms of Discrimination against Women with Disabilities" held at the Cambodiana Hotel under the chairmanship of Ms. Ung Minister of Women's Affairs Kantha Phavi will be joined by distinguished national and international guests, as well as many people with disabilities.
Mr. Em Chanmakara added that the promotion of gender equality and women's empowerment is essential for achieving internationally agreed development goals, including the Millennium Development Goals. Women and girls with disabilities face a double standard of discrimination, putting them at higher risk of gender-based violence, sexual abuse, neglect, abuse and exploitation.
Mr. Em Chanmakara added that discrimination against people with disabilities faces great obstacles, in fact, some people with disabilities in Cambodia have not yet received a driver's license. In addition, women with disabilities also face the obstacles of long-distance travel to towns or districts, especially the lack of assistance to help them, which is the most difficult obstacle today.
In addition, Mr. Em Chanmakara also mentioned that ensuring gender equality for women with disabilities is set in the seventh strategic direction of the above strategic plan of the Royal Government of Cambodia, including:
* First: Promoting gender equality and empowerment of women and girls with disabilities
* Second: Capacity building for women and girls with disabilities on gender-based violence and economic exploitation to build confidence and reduce negative thinking about their own disability and among service providers with women and girls. Have a disability
* Third: Strengthening mechanisms to prevent and curb gender-based violence and economic exploitation of women and girls with disabilities among female co-workers.
* Fourth: Enhancing training programs by providing opportunities for women and girls with disabilities in the field of leadership to fully participate in leadership and access to functions at all levels.
* Fifth: Eliminating barriers to behavioral and relationship discrimination
* Sixth: Participation to ensure the mainstreaming of women with disabilities in the decision-making bodies of the Royal Government.
* Seventh: Providing support for networking to encourage women with disabilities to achieve full development, progress and authority.
* Eighth: Increasing awareness of age-appropriate reproductive health and access to appropriate reproductive health information to ensure free and responsible decisions on the number of children and the interval between pregnancies.
* 9th: Promoting poverty reduction programs, social protection programs and the development of progress and multidisciplinary services to ensure a focus on the needs and priorities of women, girls and the elderly with disabilities on the basis of equality.
10th: Strengthening the coordination mechanism between women and children with disabilities to ensure the effective implementation of the National Action Plan on the Prevention of Violence against Women and the Rattanak Neary Strategic Plan and the Child Protection Strategic Plan.
* Eleventh: Increasing access to financial literacy, vocational credit services to women with disabilities through changing the negative attitudes of credit agencies. Minister Mam Bunheng: Calmette Hospital is a national hospital and a High-tech model
