According to the announcement on the registration of the association signed by Mr. Bun Hon, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior on February 4, stated that the Global Real Estate Association must act in accordance with the law on associations and non-governmental organizations. Its legal documents and statutes are kept by the Ministry of Interior without discrimination on the basis of race, color, sex or religion.
Mr. Sam Sok Noeun, President of the Global Real Estate Association, said that the initiative to establish this association is to contribute with the Royal Government and other relevant partners in the development of the Cambodian economy in line with the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy for the main purposes such as promoting and promoting the sector. Real estate in Cambodia. Disseminate courses to raise awareness of the real estate sector to the members of the association.
Organizing stakeholders operating in the real estate sector to share information, provide knowledge, experience, consulting, study visits, workshops and outreach forums. Promote operational cooperation between local and foreign real estate investors or related partners in the real estate sector to develop Cambodia and protect the rights and legitimate interests of association members. Mr. Sam Sok Noeun added.
The president of the association added that the goal of the association is to share experiences and knowledge by disseminating awareness about the real estate sector and finding markets for association members. The main mission of the association is to establish and promote increased cooperation with local and foreign real estate investors to contribute to the development of Cambodia.
