"It's time to stop interfering in other people's affairs, but there seems to be no cure for such bad habits," Kwon said. "Frankly, we do not feel like sitting face to face with the United States." Minister of Women's Affairs: Cambodia has achieved many positive results in all areas of promoting gender equality
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs, on July 7, 2020, stated that Cambodia has achieved many positive results in all areas from the promotion of gender equality and empowerment of women. And girls.
This statement was made on the occasion of Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi presiding over the opening ceremony of the seminar on the elimination of all forms of discrimination against women with disabilities held at the Cambodiana Hotel this morning, July 7, 2020. .
Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi stated that in relation to the promotion of gender equality and empowerment of women and girls in the world, Cambodia has achieved many positive results in all areas, especially:
* Investing in daughters and sons to get an education and technical skills, and increasing the number of female students in both secondary and tertiary education. * Active participation of women in the economy. * Promoting maternal and child health and reducing the transmission of HIV.
In addition, the Minister of Women's Affairs emphasized that in terms of women's participation in public and political sectors in the ASEAN region, Cambodia ranks fifth among the countries with the highest number of women in parliament.
At the same time, Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi also requested the stakeholders to continue to deal with high responsibility so that women and girls with disabilities can get the expected results, including:
Em Chanmakara, Secretary-General of the General Secretariat of the Disability Action Council, said that the promotion of gender equality and women's empowerment was necessary for the achievement of internationally agreed development goals, including development goals. Millennium.
Mr. Em Chanmakara added that women and girls with disabilities face double discrimination, which puts them at higher risk of gender-based violence, sexual abuse, neglect, abuse and exploitation.
He said that, of course, the Royal Government of Cambodia is in the process of strengthening leadership, planning and coordination of important roles to ensure sustainable community-based rehabilitation, including the protection of People with disabilities as well.
By setting international norms and standards, the international community recognizes the need for a gender perspective and empowering women with disabilities to achieve equal rights and development for human rights and development for all, including people. Have a disability.
Mr. Em Chanmakara continued that discrimination against people with disabilities faces great obstacles, in fact, some people with disabilities in Cambodia have not yet received their identity cards, driver's licenses.
At the same time, Mr. Em Chanmakara pointed out that besides, women with disabilities also face obstacles of long distance travel to towns or centers, especially without assistance to help them, which is the most difficult obstacle today. . Svay Rieng Provincial Administration Shows the Progress and Progress of the Province through a Press Conference Organized by the Government Spokesperson's Unit (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): This morning, July 7, 2020, the Svay Rieng Provincial Administration presented its progress and progress through a press conference organized by the Spokesperson Unit of the Royal Government under the theme "Progress and Continuation of Svay Rieng Provincial Administration.
The press conference was held at the Office of the Council of Ministers, coordinated and chaired by Mr. Phay Siphan, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit, while the Svay Rieng Provincial Administrative Delegation led by Mr. Hou Vatanak, Councilor and Mr. Ros Pharith, Deputy Governor.
Through this press conference, Mr. Ros Pharith presented the achievements and progress of the province as follows:
* As of now, there are 963 school buildings in the province, equal to 4,124 classrooms, schools of all levels, including 342 public kindergartens, of which 6 separate kindergartens, 172 community kindergartens, 262 primary schools There are 54 secondary schools, 20 high schools, 1 pedagogical and vocational school, and 1 university.
Water Resources and Irrigation: Svay Rieng Province has three main water sources that have the potential to serve and irrigate three places: Kampong Trach River in Romeas Hek District, Vai Ko River in Svay Rieng City and Cambodia-Vietnam Canal. There are still some canals.
The province has repaired, restored and constructed dams, reservoirs, pumping stations, canals and sub-canals to irrigate people's agricultural crops, including 35 small and large irrigation systems, 48 main canals and sub-canals with a length of 611 km. 295 km of Cheung Kep canal, 15 dams, 4 pumping stations, which can irrigate 85,600 hectares, equivalent to 46% of the plan.
Meanwhile, with the guidance, guidance and support of the Royal Government, relevant ministries and institutions and current development partners, Svay Rieng province has been rehabilitating and building more irrigation systems, including:
The second phase of the Vaiko Irrigation Project in Svay Chrum District includes two main canals, a length of 23.5 km, a reservoir, and a number of small and large art structures capable of irrigating more than 10,000 hectares.
The project to rehabilitate the Mekichok canal through Romeas Hek district, Romduol district, Svay Teap district, Chantrea district, Kampong Ror district and Bavet city, which has so far achieved 53 kilometers, which has the potential to irrigate about 50,000 hectares of arable land.
The province is constructing a 2,300-meter-long Vaiko delta dam in Prey Chhlak commune, Svay Rieng city, which is a project of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology to achieve 60%. This dam has the benefit of preventing floods from flooding people's houses, farms and crops, in addition to providing water for the production of clean water for people to use in Svay Rieng, especially for the improvement of the beauty of the province. More beautiful and attractive.
* Health Sector: Throughout the province, there are 1 provincial referral hospital, 5 district referral hospitals, including Chi Phu Referral Hospital, Svay Teap Referral Hospital, Svay Chrum Referral Hospital, Romeas Hek Referral Hospital, Samaki Romduol Referral Hospital and health offices. There are 4 ODs with 44 health centers and 2 health posts.
* Rural development: Rural development is also an important priority sector, which is growing remarkably, as evidenced by the results of the rehabilitation and reconstruction of roads in both urban and rural areas. Gradually transformed from dirt roads, red gravel roads to paved and concrete roads, now there are 764 rural roads of all kinds in the province, a total length of 2,714 km.
At the same time, improving the use of clean water and latrines in rural areas has increased at a high rate, as evidenced by the achievement of stoppage of open defecation (ODF) in two districts, Svay Teap and Rumduol district and is continuing to achieve 100% goal in other districts in the future. 85% of households have access to clean water and 96% have access to latrines.
* Private sector of employment and investment: Svay Rieng province has 11 special economic zones in operation, 08 locations in total, a total of 216 companies, factories, enterprises, private institutions, banks, microfinance institutions, of which 113 factories have created jobs. More than 80,000 people (more than 70,000 factory workers) contribute to improving people's lives and reducing poverty.
Trade: Implement the policy as well as the Royal Government's National Strategic Development Plan 2019-2023 to promote the trade sector. So far, Svay Rieng has 20 markets, of which 11 are state markets and There are 9 private investment markets and 1 fish market in Bavet city.
* Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs: Systematic land registration: implemented in 250 villages, 33 villages, 8 communes, 8 districts, 254,750 land ownership certificates. Separate land registration issued 177,735 land ownership certificates.
Mining and Energy Sector: Svay Rieng Province has 3 main sources of electricity: Vietnam from Phnom Penh and its own production to supply and distribute to about 80,995 households, equivalent to 54% of the total 149,891 households and Efforts are being made to expand the electricity network in line with the Royal Government's goal by 2020 to have electricity to all villages.
* Tourism: Svay Rieng province has 3 tourist resorts, including Prey Bassac natural resort located in Bassac commune, Svay Chrum district, about 8 km from the provincial town and Chea Hor, an ancient temple in the village. Prey Kdei, Koki commune, Romeas Hek district, is about 58 kilometers from the provincial town, as well as tourist attractions organized by the provincial administration, including the banks of the Vaiko River and Svay Rieng Sankranti.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng considers critics of traffic law enforcement as just an excuse and seems to want more people to die (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Committee Road Traffic Safety (NCC) considers critics of traffic restrictions to be merely making excuses for talking nonsense and working vaguely and seemingly wanting more people to die.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng said this on the occasion that Samdech presided over the meeting to review the results of road safety work for the first half of 2020 on the morning of July 7, 2020 at the Ministry of Interior.
"Currently, the Royal Government is paying attention to 19 cases of Kovid, and so far there are 141 Kovid 19 patients in Cambodia and no one has died from the disease," he said. No, but looking back at traffic accidents, there are deaths every day. "So critics of traffic restrictions are just excuses and work vaguely, as if they want more people to die."
"It has been said that (our critics) our people are affected by Kovid 19. We put more burden on the people by enforcing traffic laws with heavy fines. "Seriously, there are others who say it is restricted to take people's money."
Samdech Tha, critics of the new traffic law is not valuing the people and must be reconsidered properly. The purpose of restricting traffic laws today is to protect the property and lives of people only if people participate in obeying all traffic laws, the authorities do not fine.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stressed that if the Royal Government eases the restrictions on road traffic laws, more people will die. That is why the Royal Government has restricted such traffic so that friendly countries can admire Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has decided to allow private educational institutions to hold lower secondary school diploma (diploma) and high school diploma (Bakdup) exams and private higher education institutions to hold final exams for two days. .
According to a letter from the Ministry of Education, obtained by Fresh News on July 7, 2020, the Ministry has previously issued instructions to private educational institutions at all levels to organize teaching and learning remotely or electronically.
The Ministry also mentioned the possibility of allowing electronic examinations according to the calendar of the respective educational institutions, ensuring acceptable quality standards. The Ministry will work with private educational institutions to ensure this quality standard.
For private educational institutions that follow the guidelines of the Ministry of Education, they can issue lower secondary school diploma and high school diploma with the recognition of the Ministry, but private educational institutions must sign themselves.
The Ministry will inspect as necessary to ensure the quality of the degree.
