(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said that in order to make it easier for people who want to transfer ownership of their vehicles, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport has cooperated with the General Department of Taxation to establish A single system to provide vehicle transfer services, this system will be launched from September 2020 onwards.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said this this morning, July 7, 2020, on the occasion of informing Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Road Safety Committee. Meeting to review the results of road safety work for the first half of 2020.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol stated that "In order to provide services to change the ownership of vehicles more easily, the Ministry of Public Works has cooperated with the General Department of Taxation to connect the system of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and the system of the General Department of Taxation. "People come to one place and provide all services."
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol further stated that from September 2020 onwards, citizens who want to exchange vehicle ownership can only go to the Ministry of Public Works and Transport or go to the General Department of Taxation to transfer vehicle ownership and send money. Wing and other systems.
