(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Municipal Police has clarified the case of criticism on Facebook regarding the activities of a group of police who locked the tires of a car in Sangkat Boeung Kak I, Khan Toul Kork, because the car was parked incorrectly. Traffic laws will affect public order.
Following the announcement, the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Information and Quick Reaction Team responded to the question on the Facebook account, which posted, Anything to play? Do not understand?
The Quick Reaction Team and the Tuol Kork Police Inspectorate would like to explain to the public that all the cars parked above the eyebrows were locked because the car owners parked illegally and affected public order: Such as:
