Today marks the 12th anniversary of the Preah Vihear Temple being inscribed on the World Heritage List! (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): July 7, 12 years ago, was a cancerous day for the Cambodian nation after the Temple of Preah Vihear was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List. The 32nd session was held in Quebec City, Canada on July 7, 2008.
In the cause of upholding national cultural heritage and defending national sovereignty, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, sent a letter to UNESCO in 2001 requesting the registration of the Temple of Preah Vihear as a World Heritage Site. The Prime Minister said that the inscription of the Temple of Preah Vihear on the World Heritage List is in line with the planned plan, which is a priority of Cambodia's foreign policy.
To celebrate this great achievement, the Royal Government of Cambodia has designated July 10 as the National Day of Remembrance for the inclusion of the Temple of Preah Vihear and Sambor Prei Kuk in the World Heritage List and recommended the celebration. Even more so.
* History of Preah Vihear temple
June 15, 1962: The Temple of Preah Vihear is ruled by the International Court of Justice (ICJ) in Cambodia to win the Cambodian-Thai dispute over the Temple of Preah Vihear.
July 7, 2008: UNESCO decides to inscribe Cambodia's Temple of Preah Vihear on the World Heritage List at its 32nd session in Quebec City, Canada.
* Prince Indrayuth
