* Brahmin Takpa Swinbandit
King Suryavarman I was a Theravada Buddhist. He still worships Iso, because in this inscription it is said that in order to temporarily limit his power, he made four penises, each of which had the same name, Suryavarmisvara, the so-called Suryavarman. You.
One penis was kept in Battambang province, Wat Ek, named Chey Kset on the western border. At the northern border is another penis, of the same name, which is kept in the temple, temporarily defining the boundaries of his authority on the northern side. There is another one left on Phnom Sorya Tri, Phnom Preah Iso, Phnom Iso Yeung in Takeo province today, that is the southern part.
And there is another penis of the same name, left in the Northeast, probably along the Mekong River, probably in Kratie, Stung Treng. These four penises were taken in all four directions in AD. 1018. This is what King Suryavarman I did for the temple of Phnom Preah Vihear.
* Purpose of building the temple of Preah Vihear
First, the deity Srey Sikkha Risvara is sometimes kept, sometimes it is written as Srak Risvara, sometimes it is written Sikkha Risvara, but it is the same name. It is a place where they are kept because this deity, who has a penis as a representative, is very powerful. It is believed that bringing fruits brings happiness to Cambodia.
* Construction features of Preah Vihear temple
From the lowlands from the road up to the temple on the highest peak, one has to walk up several stairs with a total radius of 804 meters. Before ascending from the lowlands to the temple on the top of the mountain, one has to go through 5 gates. The site of the temple on the highest peak is 525 meters high. The main temple is 35 meters by 45 meters, which is suspected to be the place to store the penis of the deity named Srey Sikhak Risvara.
Up again, a distance of 150 meters, there are always anchors along that road. On the left hand side, there are small temples, so 150 meters to the third gate, there is an inscription about the construction of the temple, in the reign of King Suryavarman I, probably your place Enter the veneration, let them perform the ritual, let them learn the Dharma there, enter through the third gate.
