(Phnom Penh): Mr. Srun Pov, President of the Cambodian Livestock Breeders Association, stated that during the 19 years of Kovid disease in Cambodia, the momentum of livestock growth has increased significantly, with the attention of Royal Government of Cambodia.
The president of this association stated that due to this excess, farmers who raise chickens have a little difficulty with less profit.
Mr. Srun Pov stated, "Looking back at raising pigs now, the price is very good, which makes farmers, companies and farms acceptable because of the reasonable price and high profits. "Currently, pig farming is increasing, with a daily supply of about 5,000 to 6,000 pigs in a short period of time."
He added that these good results came from the support of the Royal Government, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the General Department of Production and Animal Health and other stakeholders. These improvements made the local farmers very happy and continued to work hard.
"Currently, there are many farms, such as fish and ducks, which can supply the market," he said. "However, we are still affected by some factors, such as falling domestic egg prices, factors that have pushed down prices due to egg imports from Vietnam and Thailand."
Mr. Srun Pov claimed, "Confirmation of the increase in the number of livestock farmers has increased based on direct visits to the site." In fact, the association conducted a workshop in Siem Reap and found that people have brought about 6-70,000 piglets from Thailand to Cambodia, this number is not enough.
He added that in Cambodia it is not yet possible to sell and distribute piglets and piglets, so we expect to import piglets from Thailand. In the first six months of 2020, according to the association's statistics, about 7-8,000 piglets were imported from Thailand, while about 5,000 to 6,000 pigs were imported, not counting other companies such as Mong Reththy. Group as well as other companies.
Vesa is one of the most important festivals in Buddhism. It is an important time for monks and nuns to study the Dharma and Discipline consistently according to the Buddha's teachings for about three months.
The rainy season festival is to arrange a holiday somewhere or in a pagoda for three months during the rainy season and not to go away late at night unless there is a duty. Important, such as parents who are seriously ill or invited to perform dharma, etc., determined to return within 7 days.
The rainy season festival is held every year from the 1st day of the month of Assad to the 15th day of the month of Assoch. The ceremony started on the evening of the 15th day of the month of Asat, with the participation of the elders at the foot of the pagoda, the procession of candles, skirts and other paraphernalia, the procession around the temple, and then the sermon and the distribution of votive candles. Monks.
Khmer Buddhists, who have a strong belief in Buddhism, before the arrival of the Vesa date, always bring Vesa candles and other offerings to the monks to remember the Vesa without the Ben Batha ritual. That
Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, as well as their Buddhist families, have a strong belief in Buddhism. Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit and their families always bring Preah Vossa candles and gifts to the monks in various places every year while waiting for the rain for 3 months.
The ceremony of offering Preah Vossa candles and offerings was made according to the Khmer Buddhist scriptures. On that occasion, there was also a blessing to bless Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, as well as sons, daughters, grandsons, beloved granddaughters and government officials who were invited to attend.
On the occasion of Grandpa Achar, leading the program, I would also like to wish Bon Kosal to be born with a ceremony to give Preah Vossa and gifts to help the Cambodian nation meet only peace and wish the Cambodian people to meet only happiness.
It should be noted that in this ceremony, Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit presented 209 monks waiting for the rain at Wat Champouk K'aek with 100,000 Riels each, 108 Ta Chi grandmothers each received 50,000 Riels, Acha Each of the eight students received 200,000 riels, and the Pin Peat band each received 200,000 riels, and 50 students each received 50,000 riels.
In this ceremony, Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, as well as the participants, joined in the merit of more than 10,000 dollars for building achievements in the pagoda.
