Read more: The Royal Government Working Group accepts proposals for amendments to 17 articles in the Law on Associations and Non-Governmental Organizations
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government's working group has accepted the request from civil society organizations to amend 17 articles in the Law on Associations and Non-Governmental Organizations, which was accepted on July 6, 2020 in Consultation meeting on the proposal to amend the Law on Associations and Non-Governmental Organizations at the Ministry of Interior. This is according to a joint press release obtained by Fresh News.
According to the joint press release between the Royal Government and civil society organizations, based on the results of the third forum on the partnership between the Royal Government and civil society on August 29, 2019, representatives of civil society organizations About 500 requested the Royal Government to consider and consider proposals to amend the Law on Associations and Non-Governmental Organizations.
Based on this, the working group of the Royal Government to facilitate the resolution of requests and requests of civil society organizations organized a meeting to discuss and consult with representatives of civil society organizations to find out the purpose and reasons for proposing amendments to this law, starting with During November 2019 until July 6, 2020, this is the sixth and final meeting.
The working group of the Royal Government as well as the Ministry of Interior is also committed to holding further consultative meetings with representatives of civil society organizations in order to strengthen the partnership between the Royal Government and civil society organizations to strengthen and expand the democratic process in Cambodia.
Police arrested a man with a device for breaking a motorcycle, only to find out that he was skilled in stealing a motorcycle
(Phnom Penh): A suspect was arrested when the police patrol ambushed a suspect, when asked about the theft of two motorcycles in the local area.
The suspect, Run Tiya, a 32-year-old male construction worker living in a rented room in Village 5, Sangkat Phsar Doeum Thkov, Khan Chamkar Mon, had been using drugs for more than two years and confessed to stealing two motorcycles in early July 2020.
Mr. Phorn Oun, Deputy District Inspector, said that before the incident, the police station, in cooperation with the local criminal patrol to prevent various crimes in the local area, also met the suspect man and checked to find the tip and the sharp iron. (A device for breaking a motorcycle) and then brought to the interrogation station.
Police also confiscated a motorcycle found by residents and left it on the lot, and the suspect replied that his motorcycle had been stolen.
According to the inspector, two white Scoop motorcycles with license plates Phnom Penh 1HY 0792 and navy blue round motorcycles without license plates were patrolled by Phsar Doeum Thkov police on the 3rd and 3rd. 04 in July.
The suspects are currently building a case to be sent to court for legal action, while two motorcycles and search for the owner to add more burden on the suspects.
(Oddar Meanchey): Mr. Kun Kim, Member of the Standing Committee of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Oddar Meanchey Provincial Working Committee on Sunday, July 05, 2020, yesterday led the leadership and members of the Cambodian People's Party in Oddar Meanchey Province. Meeting to review the work results of the first half of the party and set the direction for the second half of 2020.
In this meeting, Oddar Meanchey Provincial Party Committee presented some reports that party members achieved in the first half. In particular, activities to help people who are struggling in life due to the epidemic of Kovid 19 and to educate people about the efforts of the Royal Government led by the Cambodian People's Party to overcome all obstacles of the nation.
The report shows that for the first six months of 2020, under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, the working group together with the party at all levels went to the grassroots to visit people at home and support people Difficult due to the effects of Covid-19 disease and natural disasters, at a cost of about 1 billion 105 million riels, 200 tons of rice, 20,000 scarves and many other materials.
During the meeting, Mr. Kun Kim praised and appreciated the efforts and active activities of all party members in solving the difficulties of the people in accordance with the direction and objectives of the party, especially the wishes of Samdech. Techo Hun Sen.
However, Mr. Kun Kim reminded the members of the mission of the Cambodian People's Party for the nation and the people is endless. Mr. Kun Kim urged all members to pay attention to maintaining security and social order and to continue to implement the policy of safe villages and communes.
In response to decentralization and co-decentralization reforms, Kun Kim told party officials, most of whom were provincial leaders, that from the provincial level to the grassroots level, efforts must be made to expand capacity and increase the sense of responsibility. Perform tasks to think of the overall work as a whole.
Mr. Kun Kim also reminded party members to strengthen internal unity within the party, remembering that unity is a strong point that has made the party successful so far.
The CPP Standing Committee member also reminded officials to eliminate all inactivity that is hostile to the aspirations of the people who own the electorate. He said that it is important to remember the five approaches "mirroring, bathing, growing, healing and surgery" of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to remind and remind the practice of serving the nation and the people effectively and Better results.
During the meeting, Mr. Kun Kim also promoted the preparation of documents on the procedure for requesting to cut the relevant land and community land, forest cover, forest land, protected area land, etc. In order to request the Royal Government to cut the gap for the relevant people.
Finally, Mr. Kun Kim urged the party working group to continue to meet with the people, promote the opening of public forums to solve their challenges and continue to find the poor and vulnerable to Kovid 19 in the second step. China issues yellow alert over rainstorms in provinces
