This afternoon, the Ministry of Planning will hold a meeting to reflect on the implementation of the procedures for identifying poor families as requested during the 19 crisis.
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of July 6, 2020, the Ministry of Planning will hold a meeting to reflect on the implementation of the procedures for identifying poor families as requested during the outbreak of Kovid 19 under the chairmanship of Dr. Kittisetha Dr. Chhay. Senior Minister, Minister of Planning. After the meeting, Senior Minister Chhay Thorn will also give an interview to the media.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Planning said the meeting would also look into irregularities in the provision of equity cards to poor families and the introduction of measures such as:
* Provide equity cards to real poor families only, without discrimination in accordance with the procedure for identifying poor families and removing equity cards from well-off families
* In case the Commune / Sangkat Council encounters any irregularity that cannot be solved, please contact the Capital / Provincial Planning Department to solve this problem. At the same time, the Ministry of Planning will be involved in resolving these irregularities and can lock up the equity cards of well-to-do families in the poor household database system.
The Ministry of Planning hopes that the local authorities, especially the commune councils, will cooperate more to achieve better results in line with the trust from the head of the Royal Government to all of us to provide the Royal Government's cash support program to poor families. During the epidemic, 19 cases of Kovid were successful.
