(Phnom Penh): Prek Leap National Institute of Agriculture has partnered with Korean investors to strengthen agricultural training in Cambodia. The partnership between the Prek Leap National Institute of Agriculture is coordinated by Hang Sothy.
Recently, Dr. Thorn Vathana, Director of Prek Leap National Institute of Agriculture, met with Korean investors to discuss and develop cooperation in this field.
The purpose of this meeting is to expand the cooperation between Cambodia and Korea and strengthen the agricultural technical capacity of Cambodian civil servants and students, especially to jointly create investment opportunities in agriculture, crop cultivation, animal husbandry and processing into semi-finished products and finished products for Meet domestic demand and exports, as well as the development of agricultural infrastructure and other priority sectors in Cambodia.
The Cambodian side is very pleased with the investment in agriculture in Cambodia and identifying Cambodia as a destination for investment in all sectors will give top priority to agriculture in Cambodia. The Korean side is excited and expresses its sincere respect for a long-term and sincere investment partnership with its partners at the Prek Leap National Institute of Agriculture.
During the meeting, Mr. Hang Sothy, Director of Hang Sothy, announced the preparation of 500 hectares of land for agricultural development in Cambodia with this project.
The two sides agreed to provide scholarships to Cambodian civil servants and agricultural students, especially the Prek Leap National Institute of Agriculture, to provide opportunities for further study of agricultural techniques, agricultural product processing, packaging and agricultural development management, as well as visits. Study and exchange experiences between Cambodian and Korean counterparts.
