More specifically, to date, the units of this Sky Villa project have sold more than 66%. The project is located along the Boulevard of the Republic of Poland in Veal Vong, Khan 7 Makara, next to the National Olympic Stadium.
Designed by renowned Taiwanese architect Chu-Yuan Lee, Sky Villa sets a new record for being the largest residential condominium project in Cambodia with unit sizes ranging from 272 square meters to 509 square meters. . Combined with a clever design, Sky Villa can be compared to a huge villa on the sky of Phnom Penh.
In addition to the above features, this condo brings the experience of living in luxury and high prestige through contemporary architectural design, accompanied by international facilities and green nature, which not only creates a fresh living environment. Not only that, but also ensures full aesthetics, well-being and comfort for the occupants.
The project has 256 luxury condominium units with a wide range of facilities and services. On the 34th and 35th floors, which are the link between the two buildings, residents can enjoy a variety of services such as a gym, massage room, swimming pool and aerial garden with beautiful city views. In addition, the building also has a Sky Villa Club, which offers a reading area, restaurants, cafes, as well as a lounge.
To provide comfort, safety and luxurious living experience, Sky Villa offers a full range of daily services such as transportation arrangements, cleaning services, laundry services, shopping services, event planning services and more. Of you live. The twin condominiums are equipped with state-of-the-art security cameras, 24-hour security and a four-story underground car park.
