Legal Awareness: Individual Guarantee
(Phnom Penh): In the day-to-day operations of all businesses, both assets and assets are mostly parallel, meaning that all types of businesses can access both assets and assets. For property, which is simply a debt, both creditors and debtors often choose one way to avoid any possible risks is to take out collateral.
To make it clearer today, Fresh News, in collaboration with the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation, has raised a topic on "Individual Guarantee" to explain and share to all citizens, students as follows: To:
Debt guarantee is provided in the Civil Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia, divided into two types: personal guarantee and property guarantee. Debt guarantee by an individual is a condition in which an individual intends to guarantee the debtor's debt voluntarily, that is, any third party is the guarantor of the debtor to repay the debt. Replace the debtor in case the debtor does not pay.
However, such a point seems to be a heavy burden on the guarantor to guarantee the obligation on the debt on behalf of the debtor, and therefore the Civil Code, Article 900, paragraph 2, paragraph 2 states: "... But the obligation of "A special contract that guarantees damage can only happen if the person in charge of the special contract that guarantees the damage has its business as a guarantee of damage or guarantee."
This means that the Civil Code provides for the protection of the guarantor, because considering the actual situation, such a guarantee is really a burden on the guarantor, therefore, the Civil Code further stipulates that the creation of such a guarantee contract can This can only be done if the underwriter has his business as collateral.
On the other hand, even if the insurer is not in business and has established a contract for the above damages, it may not be effective. In the event that a guarantee contract is established, then the guarantor has a legal obligation to guarantee the debt obligation.
In principle, the size of the guarantee obligation is already determined by the will of the guarantor and the creditors who are parties to the guarantee contract. However, if there is no prior agreement, the size of the guarantee obligation is determined by the amount of principal owed by the debtor, as well as secondary obligations such as interest, collateral, performance of the obligation or compensation for damages. Must be to a degree that can not be worse than the debtor absolutely.
This guarantee is similar to a title deed like a mortgage, but there are some differences: the mortgage, the grant by the grant, or the right to collateral, what is guaranteed is a certain value, while the guarantee is secured with property. Its in a guaranteed amount.
In sum, a personal guarantee is a form of special promise in which the guarantor is obliged to pay the debt on behalf of the debtor with the creditor in case the debtor is unable to pay the debt or is unable to perform the obligation. On its debt. But the Civil Code also stipulates some special provisions aimed at protecting the guarantor from the burden of this serious obligation.
