Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) explains the felling of an acacia tree planted by a family under a 115 kV transmission line in Dang Tong district
(Kampot): After a family living in Stok Thlok village, Totong commune, Dang Tong district, Kampot province, posted a message requesting the intervention of the head of the Royal Government, accusing Kampot provincial authorities and Electricite du Cambodge of destroying their acacia trees on July 4, 2020. Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) has come out to explain the case of cutting down acacia trees to prevent danger to the lives of people and not to affect the transmission of electricity.
Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) has confirmed that a 115-kilovolt transmission line from Chhouk district in Dang Tong district, Kampot province, was built in 2013 and April 2017 to supply the people in that area, as well as to two cement factories. K-Cement and Chip Mong factory, each with a production capacity of about 2 million tons per year to serve the national economic growth and employ thousands of young men and women.
