Minister of Agriculture monitors and evaluates the progress of freshwater aquaculture in Kampong Cham province and encourages the use of local resources to the fullest
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, accompanied by Mr. Eng Chea San, Delegation of the Royal Government of Cambodia in charge of Fisheries Administration and professional officers this morning, July 4, 2020. Monitor and evaluate the progress of freshwater aquaculture in Kampong Cham province.
Mr. Taing Im Saravy, the owner of a fish farm in Ta Ngil village, Cheala commune, Batheay district, Kampong Cham province, informed Minister Veng Sakhon that he had taken up fish farming business from 2015 until now, the farm has expanded to 6 hectares. Eight ponds Each pond is 8-10,000 square meters.
After examining the aspects and activities of fish farming in ponds, Minister Veng Sakhon praised and appreciated the efforts of the fish farming business to contribute to meet the needs of the Phnom Penh market, reduce imports, create jobs, create sources of income for families. And especially use local resources to the fullest (feed bran, baby fish feed).
Minister Veng Sakhon stated that this is a production line that is mutually beneficial (fish feed companies buy raw materials from farmers, produce feed for sale to fish farmers, fish farmers buy fish fry from Fish hatcheries catch fish for sale to companies and general customers).
This kind of active interface will support the economic and social benefits of each other is indispensable, and this is the policy of the Royal Government that sees the Cambodian aquaculture sector to grow in the future. When fish resources in natural resources are depleted due to climate change and an increase in the number of local consumers.
Currently, market demand and prices are declining slightly, but Minister Veng Sakhon encouraged them to continue to keep this business waiting for the situation to improve because this is a strong career and a sustainable source of family income and they He has a lot of experience and investment, so be patient, wait for a good opportunity to come back soon.
Taking this opportunity, he advised the Fisheries Administration and the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to contact traders in Phnom Penh and markets outside Kampong Cham to help free up fish stocks.
In good condition, it should help to plan production and apply proper techniques to ensure the sustainability of supply and lead to contract agricultural production leading to agro-industrial raising for export. Customers can contact to buy fish from the farm by calling 012 356451.
Leaving a fish farm in Batheay district, Minister Veng Sakhon and his colleagues continued to inspect Heng Martinine's turtle farm in Svay Meas village, Vihear Sour commune, Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province.
Mr. Marine reported that since 2003, there have been 50,000 turtle farms on the farm, excluding breeding partners in Stung Treng and Takeo provinces and farmers in the area.
In 2020, the price of turtles will drop to $ 7-8 per kilogram due to imports from Vietnam affecting domestic production. At this point, Mr. Marine requested the Royal Government to help prevent or reduce the amount of turtle imports. In order for local breeders to increase their breeding capacity to meet market demand and provide additional investment capital, the turtle market is popular, especially Chinese customers.
Moreover, seize the opportunity in the circumstances that we are facing the global crisis of Kovid-19 in accordance with the instructions of the Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Mr. Veng Sakhon stated that the participation of the private sector in investing in agriculture as a whole, and in particular the aquaculture sector has really contributed to job creation for local people, increase household income and reduce poverty, especially to participate. Policies and agricultural development plans in line with the "public, private, development partners and agricultural communities" approach.
Not only that, Mr. Veng Sakhon also expressed his support for the willingness to expand the area of turtle farming in the future, which will contribute to increase turtle products for the domestic market and future export destinations.
Senior Minister Kun Kim: Without the win-win policy of Techo Sen, Anlong Veng people can not celebrate religion
(Oddar Meanchey): Senior Minister Kun Kim, Chairman of the National Assistance Team for Oddar Meanchey Province, and Mr. Lim Heng, as well as Buddhist officials, brought candles, candles and other items with a total budget of 130,000 USD and more than 5 million Riels. Donate monks to remember the rain at Wat Choy Teuk Chum, called Wat Anlong Veng and 16 other pagodas throughout Anlong Veng district, Oddar Meanchey province.
Senior Minister Kun Kim and Tycoon Lim Heng also donated about $ 3,000 for the construction of Wat Choy Teuk Chum. Senior Minister Kun Kim emphasized that the bringing of Vesa candles and relics to the monks for the three-month Vesa is a demonstration of strong support for Buddhism, the national religion.
The senior minister continued that according to the beliefs in Khmer Buddhism, the offering of candles and other relics is also a good deed to dedicate merit to relatives as well as heroes and heroines who sacrificed their lives. In the cause of the motherland in the past.
On the occasion of bringing candles and relics to monks in pagodas throughout Anlong Veng district, Senior Minister Kun Kim also had a conversation with his grandparents, bringing greetings and memories of Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to monks and grandparents throughout Anlong Veng district.
Anlong Veng district, Oddar Meanchey province, was the last sanctuary of Khmer Rouge leaders and soldiers. This territory was also the last territory that Khmer Rouge soldiers agreed to submit to the Royal Government of Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the end of 1998.
Senior Minister Kun Kim reminded that until 1998 in Anlong Veng district, there were no pagodas or Buddhist worship as well as other religious beliefs. Overall, Anlong Veng district was the last territory to receive the right to worship Buddhism after the genocidal regime of Pol Pot was overthrown on January 7, 1979.
The Senior Minister told the grandparents who attended the ceremony that without the successful launch and implementation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's win-win policy, it is clear that the people of Anlong Veng could not worship God. Buddhism and other religious beliefs.
The senior minister said, "Samdech Techo Hun Sen is the hero of our Anlong Veng people as well as the people all over the country. Our grandparents, brothers and sisters in Anlong Veng district, can not do the festival, which is a tradition of our Khmer people, if Samdech Techo does not put out a win-win policy and implement it successfully. This is a great blessing for the people of Anlong Veng to remember forever.
