Khmer King Sends Message to Donald Trump Celebrating US Independence Day (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Khmer King His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni Sends a Message to Donald Trump President of the United States to celebrate American Independence Day.
In a message issued on July 2, the King of Cambodia said, "On the occasion of the United States Independence Day, I would like to express my sincere congratulations and wishes to the people of the United States. To be happy and prosperous, as well as the well-being of His Excellency himself.
He emphasized that the congratulatory message was an expression of appreciation for the harmonious friendship and cooperation established between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the United States, which has progressed for many years. This year.
Please note that July 4, 2020 is the 244th anniversary of the declaration of independence from the United States from the British colony. July 4, 1776 - A group of 13 representatives of the American colonies meet to declare their secession from the United Kingdom.
That incident pushed the United States to gain independence and become a new country. Since then, every year on July 4, celebrations, mostly through fireworks, parades, barbecues, gatherings and baseball games, have been held.
Others also celebrate this special day by creating public and private events that celebrate the history, government, and traditions of the American people.
