(Foreign): Below are some pictures of the international situation selected for Friday, July 3, 2020.
(Phnom Penh): The training of about 100 rescue workers from 6 units under the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) ended on July 3, 2020 after studying both theoretical and practical training. 5 days at the 9th Special Parachute Brigade Headquarters.
The Closing Ceremony of the Training of Trainers on Incident Control System for Search and Rescue Operations was presided over by General Ith Sarath, Commander-in-Chief of the Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chief of the Disaster Management Secretariat of the Ministry of National Defense and Mr. Hang. Samoeun, Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management.
The ceremony was also attended by senior officers of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and brigade commanders, as well as other senior officials of the National Committee for Disaster Management.
The rescue team is trained by six units, including: 70th Brigade, Special Parachute Brigade, National Gendarmerie, General Command Engineering Corps, 1st Brigade and Infantry Command Water, too.
The five-day training focused on the basics of disaster management, disaster management mechanisms and their roles and responsibilities, disaster response coordination skills, the basics of incident control systems, and estimation. Incidents, incident control systems and material resources in operational control systems and incident resource management.
Mr. Phay Sok Koma, Advisor to the National Committee for Disaster Management and a trainer, said at the closing ceremony today that the past five days of training, in addition to theoretical study, also has practical application on The field, too.
Mr. Phay Sok Koma emphasized that all the participants paid high attention to this study until they got good results. He claimed that about 95% of the trainees got good grades and 5% got good grades.
At the end of the course, General Ith Sarath gave a lot of advice and recommendations to the graduates to strengthen their work ethic.
General Ith Sarath praised the training. He said the training was short, but it was an important driver in strengthening the capacity of the rescue team.
"All the young people who went through the training, it was 5 days and it was really short, but I believe that according to the report that was reported yesterday, according to the actual activities, the young people at the end "Ability to return to training their units to become proficient in finding exploration activities in rescue operations that may occur at any time."
At the same time, General Ith Sarath also reminded all the participants in the rescue team to adhere to the spirit of their duties and responsibilities as rescuers. Especially during the rescue operation, the rescue of the victims must be the main focus and the operation should be carried out quickly with the utmost patience and determination.
The Deputy Commander-in-Chief and Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces stated, "As a savior, we must put the lives of the victims first." In order to be successful in the operation, we must have patience and a strong spirit, and we must operate quickly to help the victims in time. "If we have the skills, the equipment, but we do not operate quickly, we can not help the victims in time."
At the closing ceremony, General Ith Sarath also thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, for donating equipment and materials to support rescue operations worth a total of 70 Ten thousand US dollars.
General Ith Sarath also thanked Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, for his diligent efforts in organizing the rescue team training. Mr. Ith Sarath proposed to organize more such training to strengthen the capacity of the rescue team to respond to disasters, both natural and man-made.
Mr. Ith Sarath also instructed the participants to take the knowledge and skills learned to train the team in his unit and to maintain the equipment and equipment well when something happens can be used. Timely.
Saving the life of the victim from another accident is the most necessary and important thing for the heart of the rescuer. They do not care how difficult the rescue operation is, their goal is to save the lives of the victims from the dead. Therefore, for the first training course in Cambodia, this is very valuable for them.
Participants claim that this training helps them to be more capable and make their rescue operations more efficient.
At the closing ceremony, all participants also took the oath of office. They have sworn allegiance to the motherland and the people dare to make all kinds of sacrifices to fulfill the task of defending the independence, sovereignty and territorial integrity of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Absolutely support and protect the Royal Government with Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Minister for all terms and forever.
They are committed to their physical, mental, intellectual and spiritual devotion, always ready to strictly abide by all the rules in search and rescue of people when there is a risk.
They also swore that if they had a crooked heart, they would ask for the right object and the right to protect the territory of the Kingdom of Cambodia by imposing the death penalty so that we would not escape. But if they are loyal to the nation, the motherland and the people, let the gods and goddesses in the world help nurture and protect us to be victorious, win all the gold everywhere and at all times, without interruption.
Please note that at the closing ceremony of the training course on rescue operations this afternoon, there was also a presentation of rescue exercises to the presidency. The exercise is a rescue operation in the event of a building collapse.
The exercise featured the simultaneous deployment of rescue teams, accompanied by ambulances, fire trucks and other equipment. Arriving at the scene, the rescue team opened the headquarters to show the composition of the participants. Rescuers then began searching for the victim by using a pacemaker and hearing aids.
After experts found that the victim was still alive, rescuers who cut through the rubble of the collapsed building began to operate in unison until the rescue was successfully rescued from the rubble. Summary of important news events for July 3, 2020
