History of traffic lights
The world's first hand-operated traffic signal was installed in London in December 1868. In some European countries (such as the United Kingdom), red and yellow are shown together, indicating that the sign is about to turn green. The yellow indicator is a warning sign. Flashing operation lights are used during safe traffic hours, such as at night and during the day.
Although it is said to be successful in traffic management, the operation was short-lived. An incident occurred on January 2, 1869, which resulted in the collapse of a gas lamp and the injury to a police officer who was operating. During the first two decades of the twentieth century, traffic signs in London, as well as throughout the United States, with each state having its own device design by country.
