General Knowledge: In fact, Hitler won the Lightning War at the beginning of World War II by a special drug.
Obviously, not only did Germany use aphrodisiacs, but even the armies of Japan, the United States, and the United Kingdom used the same type of amphetamine during World War II, but Germany was the most active user before and before. They were once on the battlefield, especially in the early stages of the war.
While other drugs were banned, methamphetamine was hailed and promoted as an amazing drug when it appeared on the market in the late 1930s because it was in line with the Nazi ideology of individualism. Strong, both mentally and physically.
Between April and July 1940, the German army used a total of more than 35 million pills of pervitin. Germany's Lightning War strategy relied specifically on speed through relentless aggression using tanks and infantry day and night.
In April 1940, through the Lightning War strategy, Germany gained control of Denmark and Norway. A month later, German troops moved on to the Netherlands, Belgium, and finally to France, a great power that was conquered by the Germans in just a few weeks.
In the face of growing concerns about the possibility of addiction and the negative effects of overuse, the German military began to reduce the distribution of pervitin in the late 1940s, and its use declined sharply. 1941 and 1942. However, it was still used by German troops during World War II.
