Thus, the allegation that MFI debt leads to migration is unfounded and unacceptable, and also reflects that the interviewer does not yet understand what legal and financial services are legal. To become an unofficial, unlicensed financial service with high interest rates and no consumer protection mechanism.
The statement added that the two villagers had confirmed that they had indeed participated in LICADHO's video interviews, and that the information they had provided to the association had been verified with Village chiefs and microfinance institutions as well.
In addition to the above irregularities, through direct surveys and interviews with local authorities as well as the general population in the above commune villages, they agreed that the loans provided by official financial institutions are It is indispensable to contribute to the improvement of his business and daily life, as well as the development of his commune, which is in stark contrast to LICADHO's report.
Since mid-2019, LICADHO has often published microfinance-related studies that did not reflect the overall picture, focusing only on the negative aspects, and this study could not be re-verified. Based on this reason and based on our own findings, the Cambodian Microfinance Association is skeptical of LICADHO's integrity and true intentions of previous studies related to the microfinance sector.
Especially in the context of Kovid 19, these reports have disrupted the entire microfinance sector, which has been busy engaging with the Royal Government in promoting, preventing and protecting clients from the spread of Kovid 19, as well as assisting affected clients. Affected by various means, such as the restructuring of loans to more than 220,000 customers in the amount of more than 1.1 billion US dollars.
As the only professional association representing the microfinance sector, the Cambodian Microfinance Association maintains and adheres to its vision by helping all Cambodians access rich and up-to-date official financial services. Time through a sustainable financial system. The association welcomes and is willing to participate in the study as well as any interventions that are truly willing to help the people of Cambodia.
