(Ratanakkiri): The Northeastern region has just achieved a new national infrastructure achievement: a 230 kV transmission line connecting the Sesan hydropower plant to Ratanakkiri province for a distance of 102 km and a 230/22 kV substation with a power of 50 MW.
This brand new national infrastructure achievement is a new source of supply to Ratanakkiri province as a whole and parts of Mondulkiri province, which in the past relied almost entirely on electricity imports from Vietnam via a 35 kV transmission line over a distance. 100 km, which causes frequent disturbances.
From now on, Ratanakkiri will have an even better supply, which will attract investors in agriculture, industry, tourism, a province with rich natural resources potential.
At the same time, EDC is also building a 230 kV transmission line and substation from Kratie to Mondulkiri, which is scheduled to be operational by the end of 2020.
