Royal Government approves final master plan for new Phnom Penh International Airport construction project worth $ 1.5 billion
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia on July 3, 2020, approved the final master plan of the construction project of the new Phnom Penh International Airport, the first phase, which is planned to spend 1,500 million US dollars, not including land value.
The signing ceremony was held in the presence of General Dr. Mao Havnall, Minister in Charge of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation, and Duke Pung Kheav Se, President of the Cambodia Airport Construction Company (CAIC), which has been awarded the right to build the new Phnom Penh Airport.
General Dr. Mao Havanal said that today is the proud day with the support of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, to allow the company to sign the final master plan for the construction of the new Phnom Penh International Airport.
According to Duke Pung Kheavse, the construction work for the first phase is expected to cost 1,500 million US dollars, not including the value of the land, which will be completed in 2023 to receive 13 million tourists. People per year.
Duke Pung Kheav Se added that the second phase, which will be completed in 2030, will receive 30 million tourists a year and the third phase, which will end in 2050, will receive 50 million tourists a year.
Cambodia Airport Construction Company (CAIC) is a joint venture jointly established by OCIC and the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation of Cambodia in 2018 under the guidance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to build the new Phnom Penh Airport, 20 km away. From Phnom Penh, with a total area of 2,600 hectares, the construction project has three phases.
Construction of the 108-meter-high air control tower, which the company has completed 5%, is scheduled for completion by the end of 2022.
Duke Pung Kheav Se's company holds 90% of the shares with an investment of US $ 1.5 billion, including US $ 1.1 billion in foreign bank loans and US $ 280 million in OCIC and US $ 280 million. Registered capital. Cambodian Permanent Representative to the UN High Commissioner for Human Rights on Non-Discrimination Measures
