Rangoon: The death toll in a landslide at a mine in northern Myanmar has risen to 168 as authorities expect the death toll to rise further, authorities say. This was released by CNA on Friday afternoon, July 3, 2020.
Myanmar rescuers posted a message on social media that the disaster occurred after heavy rains in Kachin State, which borders China, rescuers found 168 bodies while the search continued. Authorities have blamed mining companies for ignoring local authorities' warnings banning mining during heavy rains.
