Royal Government Approves Draft Law on Management, Use and Management of State Property (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia through a Cabinet meeting chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the morning of the 3rd In July 2020, the "Draft Law on the Management, Use and Management of State Property" was fully approved.
According to Mr. Phay Siphan, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit, the draft law on the management, use and management of state assets was initiated in November 2014 by the Ministry of Economy and Finance. Stuff. The draft law on the management, use and disposal of state property is prepared in accordance with the law in force, divided into 12 chapters and 90 articles.
This draft law will be a key legal tool contributing to the strengthening of good governance, which can facilitate the performance of the leadership and professional officers of ministries, state institutions, aimed at increasing efficiency and effectiveness and accountability in controlling the use and Manage the management of state property in accordance with the sub-national practice and the reality of Cambodia.
Upon entry into force, this law shall apply to all types of state property, governing, utilizing and disposing of state property under the sovereignty and / or jurisdiction of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The management, protection, use, conservation and development of natural resources of the Kingdom of Cambodia shall comply with the laws and regulations. The management, use and management of state assets of the National Bank of Cambodia shall fall within the scope of the law on the organization and functioning of the National Bank of Cambodia.
