(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to release a national budget of about 25 million US dollars per month to support the poor and vulnerable people during the fight against Kovid 19, about 560,000 families.
To receive this allowance, poor and vulnerable families must have a valid equity card based on poverty level: poor level 1 (poor) or poor level 2 (poor) and go to verify the list of cash aid programs. Poor families during the fight against Kovid 19 at a commune hall.
What are the conditions to be considered poor and receive this equity card?
