(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has repeatedly warned that corrupt civil servants who conspire to take state land or people's land and seek tricks to harm the people will be severely punished and will lead to Dismissed from the party immediately.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's serious warning was made during the meeting of the Council of Ministers this morning, July 3, 2020. In this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen raised the land dispute in Koas Kralor district, Battambang province between Song Thorn and the people.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that this land dispute was a conspiracy between the officials and Mr. Song Thorn, conspiring to take state land and falsely claiming that the land was the legal land of the tycoon and cutting it off for the people. .
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in order to resolve this land dispute, he ordered the Ministry of Justice, Samdech's lawyers and the Anti-Corruption Unit to investigate this matter. In this morning's meeting, Samdech Techo ordered Senior Minister Om Yentieng, head of the Anti-Corruption Unit, to prepare relevant documents on the dispute and submit them to the Council of Ministers.
Please note that the land dispute in Koas Kralor district between Duke Song Thorn and the people has become an event that is very moving and interesting among the Cambodian people. This land dispute led to Samdech Techo Hun Sen deciding to terminate the position of Koas Kralor District Governor Mr. Mao Sochan.
