Mr. Sok Touch apologizes to Senior Minister Cham Prasidh for using exaggerated words in the introduction of new words
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, on June 30, 2020, in a press conference on "Progress of the National Council for the Khmer Language of the Royal Academy of Cambodia" reacted with a number of ministries and institutions that created new words without Pass or not discuss with the Royal Academy of Cambodia and the National Council for the Khmer Language.
According to Dr. Sok Touch, the issuance of new words without discussion leads to awkwardness or public suspicion. During the conference, Mr. Sok Touch mentioned the name of Senior Minister Cham Prasidh, Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, that he never discussed or passed with the National Council for the Khmer Language when creating new words.
Mr. Touch's reaction came after some members of the public were skeptical of the word "innovation", a new term for Senior Minister Cham Prasidh's ministry.
Mr. Sok Touch's remarks led to a backlash from Senior Minister Cham Prasidh, who explained that the word "innovation" was not a new term coined by the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation. Used for a long time.
After receiving a reaction from Senior Minister Cham Prasidh, Mr. Sok Touch apologized to the Senior Minister for his mistakes and misunderstandings.
