(Phnom Penh): Through a press conference organized by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government, Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, this morning, July 2, 2020, presented what is the strategic plan to continue to deal with landslides. In the geography of Kampong Cham and the arrangement of infrastructure along the river to attract tourists.
Mr. Un Chanda claimed that in the past, the riverside in Kampong Cham City suffered a severe landslide that required the most attention. Therefore, on behalf of the provincial administration, think immediately about the measures taken in 2020 to prevent further landslides.
According to Mr. Un Chanda, the provincial administration has discussed with the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology to prepare concrete on the river bank. In addition to repairing the bank, the province also inspected the aesthetics of the garden, because when the bank collapsed, the condition of the floor prepared as a garden was also damaged.
The provincial governor emphasized that the beautification of the river infrastructure has been included in the 2021 development plan. It also includes the installation of electrical equipment and other decorations, including the return of three thousand elephant statues.
In addition, the provincial administration will prepare more AC rubber roads to improve the aesthetics of Kampong Cham city and make it easier for people, as well as to make the sewer system bigger so that there are no road blockages. This is according to Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Kampong Cham Province.
