Cambodian Diplomatic Institute joins hands with Asia Foundation to train young diplomats
(Phnom Penh): The Institute of Diplomacy and International Relations of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia and the Asia Foundation signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) on Cooperation and Capacity Building on Diplomacy and International Relations on the second day. July 2020
The Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) was chaired by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs, to strengthen and enhance cooperation in the field of international relations and diplomacy to support the Royal Government of Cambodia's efforts to promote relations between Cambodia and the international community. .
This cooperation will also establish a public library and support the Institute in transforming this library into a specialized resource for international relations for Cambodia, co-organizing public lectures, participating in and supporting research and policy making in the field of international relations and / Or capacity development as well as organizing relevant seminars and conferences.
Both institutions hope that this MOU will enable them to contribute to the Royal Government of Cambodia in its commitment to promoting international relations with other countries.
(Phnom Penh): ACLEDA Bank on July 2, 2020, issued a statement dismissing and considering the report of the civil society institutions of the Cambodian Federation of Trade Unions, the Center for Labor Alliances and the Cambodian League for the Promotion and Defense of Human Rights (LICADHO) as useless writing. Professional research, baseless, comprehensive and provocative and intended to damage the reputation of banking and financial institutions.
According to a statement obtained by Fresh News today, "This statement aims to inform the public and explain to civil society institutions, the Cambodian Confederation of Trade Unions, the Center for Labor Alliances and the Cambodian League for the Promotion and Defense of Human Rights (LICADHO). Claiming to be human rights defenders, but in reality these civil society institutions are trying to suppress the rights, freedoms, honor and dignity of the people.
In particular, the right to life, liberty and security of person enshrined in the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia by misleading people who are misusing financial services and causing social unrest in order to gain access to them. Benefit from donors and taxpayers all over the world who volunteer to donate.
These civil society institutions always deliberately try to take advantage of the achievements that the private sector has built and actively participate in the development with the Royal Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Through the publications of many World Bank until 2019, more than two decades ago, Cambodia is a highly developed country in line with the strategic plan of the Royal Government, providing a wide range of opportunities for enterprises in all sectors, especially employment opportunities. Abundance in both domestic and foreign employment for the people of choice is not a migration as mentioned.
ACLEDA Bank confirms that it, as well as the banking and financial institutions in the Kingdom of Cambodia, are licensed under the Law on Banking and Financial Institutions and other relevant laws, including the application of a number of international principles, which are not applicable. Made for various reasons contrary to the law.
Institutions claiming to be human rights defenders and legal aid should find out more, as banking and financial institutions adhere to clear laws and principles to protect clients' rights, efficiency, and long-term client growth. .
In addition, the Cambodian Credit Bureau plays an important role in providing accurate data on the debt level of each client. Lending is not for the purpose of foreclosure.
To alleviate the burden on business owners affected by the Kovid 19 virus, the head of the Royal Government, especially the National Bank of Cambodia, has already considered the goal of protecting all stakeholders by setting out a number of measures to facilitate and solve people's problems.
Banking and financial institutions are fully involved and always take care of their customers. These vague institutions should stop all actions that damage the reputation of the banking and financial institutions that are the backbone of the national economy.
At the same time, ACLEDA Bank would like to call on the competent authorities to take legal action against any person or group that incites, shakes, promotes the impact on national economic stability, and loses the trust and safety of depositors in the sector. Banking and finance as a whole.
