(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health requires testing of 19 Kovid on all passengers arriving in Cambodia with the aim of preventing the transmission of Kovid 19 from abroad to uninfected people. This is in our country.
There are a number of main reasons why the Ministry requires this:
1: Test results from different countries may have different levels of accuracy. This means that a negative test result 72 hours before boarding is a measure to prevent and reduce contamination on the plane and during travel.
2: When traveling on airplanes and other transit points, passengers may also be exposed to Kovid 19 virus infection.
3: Post-flight testing to Cambodia is conducted to assist in determining whether each passenger must implement any of the following three measures:
A: If a passenger is tested positive, he or she will be sent to a hospital for treatment.
B: If one of the passengers on the plane is tested positive, all the other passengers on the same plane will be sent to the Intermediate Commission or Hotel organized by the Inter-Ministerial Commission to fight. And Kovid 19 to monitor health for 14 days.
