(Kampong Cham): Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Em Kosal this morning, July 2, 2020, shared his work experience on implementing the policy of safe villages and communes in Kampong Cham province, which achieved good results for 5 consecutive years. Each.
Through a press conference organized by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government on "Progress and Continuing Work of the Kampong Cham Provincial Administration", Major General Em Kosal stated that in order to implement the policy of safe villages and communes successfully, the leadership is divided into Different steps.
* First: Implementation mechanism at Kampong Cham Provincial Police: Divide the Deputy Commissioner to strengthen and lead the work in the 10 district police inspectorates throughout Kampong Cham province.
* Second: Implementation mechanism at district-municipal police inspectorates: Divide deputy inspectors to strengthen and lead police, administrative posts, communes, sangkats and people's defense forces as additional assistants.
According to the General Commissioner, in addition to the above two mechanisms, educational outreach measures also require regular implementation at the local level, so that the people have a better understanding in accordance with the plan. In addition, it is necessary to strengthen the people's defense movement, which is an effective support force at the grassroots level.
Lt. Gen. Em Kosal emphasized that in order to carry out all these tasks successfully, clear planning is required and after planning, a meeting must be held to disseminate the assignment of tasks and finally implement the set plan. In particular, in implementing this plan, attention must be paid to monitoring and improving the challenges encountered at the grassroots level.
