Recently, in Svay Chrum commune, Mesang district, Prey Veng province, there was a case where the Svay Chrum commune council withdrew between 20,000 and 40,000 riels from the people, without stating the exact reason, just saying, “Withdraw the service fee. "
The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen also warned to take action without exception if any irregularities were found in the implementation of the cash subsidy program for the poor and vulnerable people due to Kovid 19 disease, especially conspiracy against relatives. Themselves to receive allowances.
This year's wage talks are still the same every year, despite the employers' request for a one-year moratorium (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Although the world and Cambodia are facing the Kovid-19 crisis, but for the process to negotiate to increase wages The minimum wage for workers in the textile, garment and footwear sector for 2021 will still be normal, with each party reaching its own internal consultation this July.
Heng Sour, a spokesman for the Ministry of Labor, confirmed to Fresh News on July 2 that there was no delay in the process of discussing wages for workers for 2021, which is still in the calendar process in the Ministry's announcement. .
Recently, the employers asked the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to suspend the wage increase for workers for 2021 for one year to make up for some of the losses caused by the Kovid-19 crisis. However, this proposal was opposed by the Ministry of Labor and the employees.
Ath Thorn, president of the Coalition of Cambodian Garment Workers' Democratic Union and also a representative of the unions, told Fresh News that the employers' request to suspend workers' wages was unreasonable because of the talks. It is for 2021, not during this crisis.
According to the announcement of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, the discussion on the minimum wage for 2021 must follow the following calendar:
* Set July 2020 as the beginning of the internal minimum wage discussions of each party.
Set August 2020 as the start of bilateral and tripartite minimum wage discussions.
* Schedule September 2020 a meeting of the National Minimum Wage Council to achieve the minimum wage in the textile, garment and footwear sector for 2021.
The Royal Government of Cambodia has introduced a policy to increase the wages of workers in the garment and footwear sector every year. So far, the minimum wage for workers in Cambodia in 2020 is $ 190 per month.
