(Koh Kong): Pursuant to the order of the General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud, the Koh Kong Provincial Branch of the CPP in cooperation with provincial trade officials tested and found one stall of Borax. Soybean foam product weighs 1.3 kg and is on display at Dang Tong Market, Khemarak Phoumin City, Koh Kong Province on July 1 yesterday.
Mr. Chea Ny, CPP Sub-Branch of Koh Kong Province, said that the inspection of food safety, especially high-risk goods such as bubble beans, dried beans that traders import from Phnom Penh to sell in the flagpole. The provincial branch of KPRP inspected and tested 8 stalls of dried bean sprouts and 2 stalls of dried bean sprouts.
Mr. Chea Ny said that for the soybean foam that was tested for 1.3 kilograms of borax, the provincial branch officials took it to be destroyed.
