Ministry of Interior Announces Transfer of Residence and Family Book
(Phnom Penh): On July 1, 2020, the Ministry of Interior issued a proclamation to transfer the authority from the police inspector of the district to the administrative police station of the commune / sangkat for review and decision to provide a secondary residence book, residence book, and a certificate. Housing, change of family members, relocation and any correction of data in the accommodation list in accordance with the legal documents.
The Ministry also transferred the authority from the Capital / Provincial Police Commissioners to the Municipal, District and Khan Police Inspectors to review and decide on the issuance of duplicate family books, family books, changes in family members and correction of data in the family list in accordance with the legal documents.
According to a 1997 government sub-decree, the family book is a reference book for identifying family members of Cambodian nationality and the family ties of each family, including spouses and adopted children. Every family that is a Cambodian citizen living in the territory of the Kingdom of Cambodia must have a family book.
Foreigners do not have the right to use this family book. Any person who is not a Cambodian citizen and falsifies in any form in order to possess a family book or any competent authority who performs this duty contrary to the provisions of the sub-decree on this family book shall be punished in accordance with the law in force.
Residence book According to the 1997 sub-decree, the residence book is a book used by the police to collect information about the number of people living in each house. This book is not intended to confirm the kinship or Khmer nationality of the persons listed in this book.
The sub-decree states that every person who is the primary responsible person of each house, whether that person is the landlord or the tenant, is obliged to write in the residence book the name of everyone who lives permanently with him.
Both books are also important identification documents to be used as evidence in other necessary documents.
