(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chin Malin, Vice Chairman and Spokesperson of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, stated that no country can end human rights issues perfectly, while Cambodia currently has many legal mechanisms related to human rights. People and racism, etc.
Mr. Chin Malin made this remark after a working meeting between Mr. Keo Remy, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, and Mr. Pradeep Wage, Representative of the Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights in Cambodia. Monitor the implementation of the UPR Recommendations and the establishment of the National Human Rights Institution on the afternoon of July 1, 2020 at the headquarters of the Cambodian Human Rights Commission.
Responding to a reporter's question, Jean Malin said: "Because this human rights issue, no country is perfect and perfect, there are always shortcomings, and this human rights is how to make people live. "Better and according to the needs of people who are constantly demanding."
Mr. Jean Malin said that Cambodia had recently sent a delegation to Geneva, Switzerland to defend Cambodia's human rights report on racism, which had been submitted to the United Nations in a timely manner. In addition, the Cambodian Human Rights Committee also sent a delegation to defend other reports, as well as to accept some of the recommendations of the United Nations for further implementation.
"In general, in Cambodia, we have accomplished a lot of work related to this racism, including the legal mechanism, we have our national legal mechanism, the legal framework, the policy framework and the actual implementation mechanism related to racism, as if there were none," he said. In Cambodia, all nations live together in harmony. ”
On behalf of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, chaired by Mr. Keo Remy, and on behalf of the Cambodian government, Mr. Jean Malin added that this human rights work is Cambodia working relentlessly, even though human rights in Cambodia are now better. However, efforts must be made to make it even better, so all good recommendations received are Cambodia must strive to implement.
