Some rice is lacking irrigation water! Mr. Thong Khon led the intervention team to pump water into farmers' rice fields in Baray and Tang Kork districts
(Kampong Thom): While some rice fields of farmers are lacking irrigation water in recent days, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group in Kampong Thom Province led the intervention team to pump water to save rice. Farmers in Baray and Taing Kork districts responded immediately to this situation.
In fact, on July 1, 2020, Mr. Thong Khon, together with the relevant working group, inspected the water shortage situation of the people in both districts while many water pumps were busy to intervene.
Mr. Hak Mong Huot, Governor of Taing Kork District, confirmed that the rice fields of the people in Taing Kork District were affected by about 2,000 hectares, of which Sralao Commune was the most affected, about 350 hectares. As for the other fields, there is still some hope, because for several days in a row, it has rained, which makes the rice viable.
In response to the recommendation of the Royal Government and at the request of Mr. Thong Khon, General Hing Bun Heang, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the Bodyguard Command, also assigned Samdech Techo Hun Sen's rescue intervention force led by Lt. Gen. Hun Phan. Deputy Commander of the Bodyguard Command pumps water to help people who are experiencing severe water shortages in two districts from June 27-29, 2020.
In intervening to pump water into the rice fields of the two local people, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's intervention team brought 30 water pumps and two machines from the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology.
At the same time, the people also applauded the activities of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Special Intervention Force, which cooperated to help their rice fields in a timely manner.
The new National Security Law, which has six chapters and 66 articles, went into effect Tuesday night, and there are more severe penalties for violators than expected. Here are the five main points in this law:
1: Maximum sentence of life imprisonment
The four types of crimes stipulated in the new national security law include: separatism, subversion against the government, terrorism and conspiracy with foreigners, as well as internal forces undermining national security. Under the new law, masterminds and perpetrators can face up to life in prison or up to 10 years in prison, or more for the four types of crimes.
2: China's jurisdiction over serious crimes
Under the new National Security Law, China has full jurisdiction to intervene, from arrests to trials in complex cases involving foreign interference, serious cases, and those that undermine national security. Facing serious and tangible threats. At this point, the law states that "Chinese and Hong Kong national security agencies may request that the case be forwarded to mainland China."
3: Confidential hearing, no jury
4: New National Security Agency
The Hong Kong Ministry of Justice is also required by law to establish its own prosecutor's office in charge of national security crime cases, chaired by Carrie Lam. The law will give police the power to gather evidence, including the installation of communications and intelligence equipment on suspects. Police can also request software and services from suppliers to remove information and assist in investigations.
