According to Colonel Sin Narak, Mongkul Borei District Police Inspector, the victim was Ron Pheara, alias Barang, a 21-year-old male from Seur Village, Seur Commune, Mongkul Borei District, Banteay Meanchey Province.
Mr. Soeung Sothea continued that at about one o'clock in the morning, he heard something like the mountain behind the house collapsed, as he often heard the rocks fall until 5 am on June 30 when he went to urinate. The victim was found dead at the foot of the mountain.
Mongkul Borei District Police Inspector confirmed that Ron Phara's background was that he was an active smoker and drug dealer, and that he had also been imprisoned and at the Phnom Bak New Life Center (drug rehabilitation education). This is also the perpetrator of the past, as well as the destruction of many parents' property.
With the help of the provincial technical and scientific police and the Mongkul Borei district doctors, local authorities examined and autopsied the body and concluded that the man had indeed died from jumping off a mountain. At present, the body has been handed over to the family for a traditional ceremony. Senior officials of the Ministry of Planning continue to chair meetings to monitor, support and promote the identification of poor households
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Leang Phaly, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Planning and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group on Sandan District, Kampong Thom Province, continued to chair the meeting on monitoring, supporting and promoting the identification of poor families during the outbreak of Kovid 19. According to the Royal Government, it has been implemented at present.
A meeting to review the results of the work on "Monitoring, supporting and promoting the identification of poor families during the epidemic of Kovid 19" of the working group of the Royal Government in Sandan district, Kampong Thom province, was held this morning, July 1, 2013. 2020 at Sandan District Hall, with the participation of Sandan District Governor and representatives of commune members in Sandan District, Kampong Thom Province, along with many other members.
Mr. Leng Phaly, Chairman of Sandan District Local Government Working Group, said, "Sandan District Local Government Working Group has provided 18,305,000 Riels (Eighteen Million Thirty Five Thousand Riels). To help 30 poor families in Tamring commune, Sandan district, Kampong Thom province.
