(Phnom Penh): Neak Oknha Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Chair of the 13 Private Sector Working Group of the Royal Government Private Sector Forum, chaired a meeting on "Progress and Impact Situations During the Kovid-19 Outbreak. On the private sector in Cambodia.
This meeting was held at the General Department of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce this morning, July 1, 2020.
The meeting was attended by Oknha Siv Thai, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Coordinator of the 13 Private Sector Working Group, and Oknha Lim Heng, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Coordinator of the Working Group, including the Co-Chairs of each working group. Government Forum, Private Sector, Co-Chair of the General Department of Taxation-Private Sector Partnership and Co-Chair of the Customs-Private Sector Partnership Mechanism.
The purpose of this meeting is to acknowledge and reflect on the progress of the entry-level situation during the Kovid-19 epidemic on the private sector and to continue to have a significant impact on all sectors, including:
1: Working Group (a) "Agro-industry": Late harvest due to labor shortage and high import of high-value animal feed in the livestock sector, the tycoon requested a local feed mill to avoid Imports of animal feed.
4. Working Group (e) "Banking and Finance Services": The new Cash Clearing Law calls on the government to facilitate the use of the $ 3,000 deposit service through the banking system.
5: Working Group (g) "Transport and Infrastructure": Request the Government to coordinate the reopening of border crossings in accordance with the Cambodia-Vietnam bilateral agreement.
6. Working Group (s) "Rice-Rice": Request the Royal Government to establish a rice DNA laboratory and internationally recognized local rice disease laboratory and to have a local feed mill. Request the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture to delay the collection of loans for up to 12 months.
7. Working group (D) "Education" proposes to reopen all private schools, including gymnasiums, in accordance with the safety standards of the Ministry of Health in August or September.
As a result of the meeting, Duke Kith Meng told the private sector not to worry about the "EBA" issue, as he believed that the government could solve the problem and that the government would soon adopt a law on gambling. Accept challenges and suggestions related to all areas to submit to management.
(Kampong Speu): Mr. Kao Thach, Director General of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture explained in detail about the problem of raising and eating red tilapia to Cambodian farmers, noting that some people are afraid to eat and raise fish. This is due to the understanding that eating red tilapia will cause cancer, etc., but in fact, the fish is being evaluated on the world market.
Mr. Kao Thach's explanation was made on the morning of July 1, 2020, and participated in the dissemination program on "Access to credit for farmers, animal husbandry, aquaculture, vegetable growing, fruits and agricultural processing enterprises" in Kampong Speu province.
Mr. Kao Thach said that some people do not dare to eat red tilapia, believing that eating this type of fish will cause cancer, but according to fish scientists at the AIT Institute, this red tilapia does not. It causes many diseases, but on the contrary, this type of fish is high in vitamins.
He added that this is an economic crisis that makes people not dare to eat, farmers do not dare to raise because there is no demand. The countries that raise the most red tilapia are: China, Indonesia, Malaysia, Singapore and so on.
