(Phnom Penh): A video of a group of police officers in Sangkat Kbal Koh, Khan Chbar Ampov arresting a young man for distributing and using drugs and was shared on Facebook until the Phnom Penh Police Commissioner criticized the operation. The three-star general came out to explain the incident and issued a warning letter and a fine to the police officers who overreacted during the operation.
On June 30, in Kbal Koh commune, three or four police officers on a motorcycle arrested a drug-related suspect, handcuffed him on the back of a motorcycle, and used violence on his knees, ankles and feet. The video was posted by people near the operation site, causing a lot of criticism.
