The meeting of the Economic and Financial Policy Committee on the results of the negotiations on the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement was held on the morning of June 30, 2020 at the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
He also highlighted the commitment of the Cambodian Subcommittee on Negotiations to the mandate as well as the guidelines of the Economic and Financial Policy Committee at its meeting in February 2020 as a basis for negotiating the agreement.
The Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement is Cambodia's first important bilateral free trade agreement. Once in force, the agreement will play an important role in diversifying export markets and boosting exports of Cambodian products, especially agricultural and agro-industrial products, to China's major markets by agreeing to The opening of this additional commodity market.
In addition, the agreement will accelerate the process of Cambodia's economic integration into the region and the world by strengthening Cambodia's participation in regional and global production chains, as well as transforming Cambodia into a potential country. Attract investment as a production base for export to Chinese market.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the Meeting, expressed his gratitude and appreciation to the leaders of the relevant ministries and institutions, especially the Cambodian Negotiation Team, for their efforts and active participation in the negotiation of the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement. Negotiations ended on schedule as planned.
