Through his Facebook page, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng noted that based on the above data, it is clear that the people are more aware and more involved in obeying traffic laws as the country develops, there is an increase in vehicles. Despite the increase in traffic and the number of drivers, the number of accidents has decreased.
As the Chairman of the National Road Safety Committee, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng thanked all the compatriots, especially the road users, for their strict compliance with the road traffic law and thanked the competent forces. Like all relevant officials who performed their duties well.
"Hello, dear compatriots! Today is July 1, the end of the middle of 2020, and today I would like to inform my compatriots about the positive results of traffic problems for the first half of 2020, the number of accidents has decreased. Notably, compared to last year and before the enforcement of road traffic laws.
According to the above data, it is clear that our people are more aware and respect the traffic law as our country grows, the number of vehicles traveling and the number of drivers increase. There is a decrease.
As the Chairman of the National Committee for Road Safety, I would like to thank all the compatriots, especially the road users, for their continued compliance with the Road Traffic Law and thank the competent forces. As well as all relevant officials who have performed their duties well.
We would like to thank all the media, NGOs and local authorities at all levels for their participation in disseminating and educating the people about this road traffic law. I would also like to express my deep gratitude to my compatriots who sent messages and comments, especially on my own Facebook page, which are all messages and comments, content to build and improve.
I would like to encourage my compatriots to continue to contribute constructively and improve in order to continue to better implement the road traffic law, which means that the accident rate will be lower and the death toll will be higher. Less public order, more orderly, better suited to Cambodia and the Cambodian people as a civilized nation.
At the same time, I would like to remind the competent forces as well as all relevant officials who have participated in the performance of their duties must continue to adhere to professional ethics and discipline in the performance of their duties must be reduced. "Or eliminate any negative phenomena to serve the interests of our nation and our people."
Japan continues to provide more than $ 3 million grant to develop human resources in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Government of Japan has continued to provide more than 3 million US dollars in grants to the Royal Government of Cambodia for the development of the country's human resources. This is according to a joint press release between the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) and the Ministry of Economy and Finance released on June 1, 2020.
The two sides successfully signed a grant agreement for the Human Resource Development Scholarship (JDS) project worth 348 million yen (approximately 3.23 million US dollars) on June 29, 2020. .
The project aims to address all development challenges in Cambodia by supporting young government officials who are expected to become leaders in Cambodia by obtaining a master's or doctoral degree from a higher education institution in Japan. Officials supported by the JDS project can use the experience study and human resource network through the project to develop and implement socio-economic development plans in Cambodia.
