It should be noted that the construction project of the new administration building of the Ministry of National Defense has organized a Krong Pali ceremony to demolish the old Ministry building on May 27, 2018. The engineering department started the dismantling process in one month and was completed by the end of June 2018.
The groundbreaking ceremony for the construction site will be held on June 30, 2018 under the presidency of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, which is planned to last for 36 months and will be completed on June 30, 2021. Due to the Kovid 19 crisis, construction was requested to extend the contract for four months, so the construction was postponed until October 30, 2021.
Avocado growers in Ratanakkiri share tips for high yields
(Rattanakiri): Mr. Van Sophea, the owner of an avocado plantation located in Thmor Da village, Sangkat Boeung Kanseng, Banlung city, Ratanakkiri province, who has planted 400 avocado trees on an area of about 4 hectares, told the key to planting this avocado. To get high yield.
The owner of the avocado plantation said that planting avocados by choosing good varieties to plant like this will soon get the yield, with one tree between 4 to 5 years old can harvest more than 100 Kg per plant.
Mr. Van Sophea said that the avocado crop is currently in high demand and can be sold both wholesale and retail at a reasonable price, between 10,000 riel to 12,000 riel per kilogram. At the same time, he requested people who have a lot of vacant land in Ratanakkiri to grow avocados because of the high yield, easy maintenance and market.
According to a report by the Ratanakkiri Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the total area cultivated by avocados is now more than 50 hectares throughout Ratanakkiri province, and among the nine districts of the province where avocados are cultivated the most. They have Banlung and Bor Keo districts.
