(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Kratie Province, Mr. Vathorn, this morning, June 30, 2020, presented the recent progress and progress of the Kratie Provincial Administration through a press conference organized by the Government Spokesperson's Unit on "Progress and direction of the work of the Kratie provincial administration."
Expansion of Agriculture and Trade: Kratie Province has 47,714 hectares of agricultural land in dry season rice and wet rice in 2019, equivalent to 101% of the plan of 47,000 hectares, with a total rice yield of 151,141 Tons supply enough demand in the province and the rest of the rice is exported every year.
In addition, the province has invested in the construction of 3 agricultural processing factories, including: 2 cassava flour factories, 1 sugar factory. The province has 1 special economic zone on an area of 818 hectares located in Snuol district, invested by UBE Snuol Company from the People's Republic of China with the permission of the Royal Government, currently in the process of building 9 factories and development projects. Next.
Irrigated 23,897 hectares throughout the province, equivalent to 50.84% of the plan of 47,000 hectares, including dry and wet rice. Farmers' communities use water 66 communities, 2 hydrological stations and 8 rainwater filter basins. The province built 2,476 meters of riverbank from 2006 to 2020.
* Tourism: Tourism is one of the main priority sectors of the province, especially in Kratie province, there are Mekong River dolphins, there are old buildings from the French colonial period and a land full of long history. Therefore, the province has been paying attention to promote the development of 19 tourist resorts, including 5 cultural and historical sites, 13 natural resorts and 1 natural cultural resort.
The province has worked to strengthen the five ecotourism communities, including: Koh Trong ecosystem, Koh Pdao, Koh Dambang, Chuot Ta Chhor Krahorm Kor and Koh Sam Thip ecotourism community, especially the conservation and development of the Mekong River dolphin tourism area, which currently has animals. About 80 dolphins are attracting more and more national and international tourists to visit and enjoy every year.
* Land Dispute Resolution: As a result, 54 cases of land dispute settlement within the Cadastral Commission mechanism and 98 cases outside the Cadastral Commission mechanism have received a total of 148 complaints, of which 83 cases have been resolved, 81 cases are being resolved and 08 cases have been withdrawn. And rejected the complaint after the investigation of 9 cases different from the authorities and 48 cases are being resolved.
Cambodia Celebrates World Day Against Deteriorating Land Quality and Drought 2020
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, this morning, June 30, 2020, celebrated the "World Day Against Deterioration and Drought 2020" in Kampot village, commune. Quick, Rovieng district, Preah Vihear province.
The event was also attended by leaders of the Ministry, provincial governors, sub-national authorities, representatives of development partners, national and international organizations, government officials at all levels, grandchildren, students and more than 200 people.
The provincial governor, through Minister Veng Sakhon, called on the private sector to study the feasibility of investing in agriculture in Preah Vihear province, which has the potential to expand production productivity for domestic supply and export.
Minister Veng Sakhon praised and highly appreciated the responsible efforts of Preah Vihear Provincial Administration and stakeholders in cooperation with the Department of International Cooperation to organize this important event smoothly in order to join the fight against Deterioration of soil quality and drought 2020 under the theme "Sustainable production and consumption of food, animal feed and fiber".
Minister Veng Sakhon stated that the World Day Against Deforestation or Decreased Soil Quality has been celebrated annually from 1995 onwards in order to increase human interest in the root causes of landslides. Soil quality and drought, as well as other consequences affecting the life of the planet and the livelihoods of farmers in rural areas who depend on agriculture.
On October 15, 1994, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has the obligation to join and cooperate with the world in implementing the activities set out in the Convention. This is to combat or prevent deforestation or soil degradation fully and consistently for the primary purpose of preserving the environment, biodiversity and natural resources.
In fact, the Ministry organizes this ceremony every year and in 2019 celebrated this day in the forest community of Neak Ta Thmor Puon, Prey Yav village, Sre Knong commune, Chum Kiri district, Kampot province, under the theme "Let there be progress in the future".
To join in the celebration of this celebration and to raise the awareness of the compatriots to pay more attention and attention on the above topic, Minister Veng Sakhon gave additional recommendations in addition to the recommendations made last year. Past inclusion related to:
* Responsible use of agricultural land and water, smart adaptation to climate change * Measures to reduce soil degradation, unsustainable land use and ecosystem degradation * Contribute to the prevention of degradation Land Intensive farming is responsible for sustainable land management to improve livelihoods * Participate in planting trees, planting crops to improve and maintain soil quality, etc.
