Cambodian MPs Concerned Over Drug Use in Growing Areas
(Phnom Penh): Cambodian lawmakers have expressed concern over the growing use of drugs in the region.
Mr. Hou Srey, Member of the IPA-Cambodia National Assembly and Deputy Chairman of the National Assembly's Investment, Agriculture, Rural Development, Environment and Water Resources Planning Committee, led the Cambodian parliamentary delegation to the meeting, which was hosted by the Vietnamese National Assembly.
The National Assembly of Cambodia, like many other members, has expressed concern over the growing trend of drug use and trafficking, especially the emergence of the use of synthetic drugs (ATS) and the increase in the number of synthetic drug production facilities.
The Cambodian National Assembly delegation added that some drug addicts are still unwilling to seek treatment and rehabilitation services, which can be caused by shame and fear, discrimination or lack of awareness about treatment and rehabilitation, as well as integration programs. . Drug trafficking and use in ASEAN continues to occur in places such as tenants' homes, entertainment services and some complex areas that are difficult to crack down on.
The meeting recognized that the suppression of drug trafficking is a common problem and suggested that in order to prevent and suppress global crime, a comprehensive and multidisciplinary action plan for promoting drug prevention to relevant institutions has been strengthened. A better understanding of the dangers of drugs among the population.
The meeting was committed to raising the member states' awareness of the dangers of drugs to vulnerable workers, such as migrant workers, mercenaries and truck drivers.
In 1893, at the end of the monarchy, the Kingdom of Hawaii was invaded by Britain and the United States. After the complete overthrow of the Indigenous Empire, Hawaii became an independent republic from 1894 until August 12, 1898. Hawaii was declared the 50th state of the United States by Washington on August 21, 1959.
* First European presence
Historical records show that the first Chinese, originally from Guangdong, arrived in Hawaii in 1778 with James Cook.
Despite these claims, Cook is generally recognized as the first European to dock in Hawaii. Arriving in Hawaii for the second time, James Cook encountered many problems until 1779, when he was about to return to the United Kingdom, where James Cook and four sailors were killed. Throw it there.
After Cook's visit and the publication of several books related to his travels, Hawaii attracted many more Europeans, such as explorers, traders, and fishermen, who noted that the island was The port is easy to supply commercial products and also a source of raw materials.
* Overthrow of the monarchy and the establishment of a republic
On January 17, 1893, the throne of Queen Lily Oukalani was completely overthrown by John El-Stevens, Chargé d'Affaires of the United States in Hawaii and replaced by a caretaker government. After the overthrow, Sanford Bidolale, a Hawaiian, became president of the new republic when the Provisional Government ended on July 4, 1894.
However, the coup d'état to oust Queen Lily and the overthrow of the monarchy in Hawaii was widely blamed by the US government. The United States has backed Queen Lily O'Keefe to restore the throne, but has been blocked by the Provisional Government of Hawaii, forcing hundreds of years of plans to restore the "Khammehameha" dynasty on the isolated archipelago. There is hope forever.
