Russia: Opposition Accuses Amendments to Constitution Amend Putin for Life
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Opposition groups in Russia have strongly condemned President Vladimir Putin's constitutional referendum, calling it "ridiculous." This was released by CNA on Monday, June 29, 2020.
According to opposition parties, the referendum on the constitutional amendment, which began last week and will end on Wednesday, July 1, will pave the way for Putin to stay in power for life. But while condemning and calling on the Russian people not to participate in the referendum or opposition vote, the opposition did nothing more.
Putin, now 67, proposed amendments to the constitution in January with the support of parliament and the Supreme Court. If successful, the amendment would allow Putin to run for two more terms, one for six years or more after his presidential term expires in 2024.
