Ministry of Transport launches road safety education campaign in 4 provinces
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) has launched an education campaign on road safety in four other provinces, including Mondulkiri, Ratanakkiri, Stung Treng and Preah Vihear.
The opening of the education campaign was presided over by Ms. Mon Manvi, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and Secretary General of the NCDD Secretariat. Recently.
The purpose of this educational campaign is to raise awareness among all road users, especially motorcycle users, to pay attention and respect the law on road traffic in order to prevent and reduce road accidents. Low.
In this campaign, there is a program to talk with the people, as well as to ask and answer questions about road traffic safety to get a helmet and to explain to young people to learn to use the education program on road traffic law. Cambodia Driving Rules), a convenient program for citizens to learn about road traffic laws and to test their abilities.
It should be noted that the four traffic safety education campaigns were attended by a total of 460 people, each of whom received a helmet, as well as a book on road traffic law, a book on what motorcyclists need to know, and a leaflet to help them. On traffic safety.
The campaign also provides guidance to participants on the Covid-19 disease prevention campaign by keeping gaps, wearing protective masks, health care and personal hygiene in accordance with the guidelines of the Ministry of Health to contribute to the Royal Government in preventing disease. Covid-19 as well.
