Thai authorities detain 13 Cambodian workers crossing the border into Thailand illegally
(Banteay Meanchey): A total of 13 Cambodian workers were detained by Thai police in Thai territory after they smuggled across the border.
According to a report by Fresh News Agency on the morning of June 29, 2020, the arrest was made on June 28, 2020, yesterday, with all 13 workers crossing the border in search of work. Made in Thailand, while the country is preventing the spread of Kovid 19, Thai sheriffs in Sa Kaeo province arrested.
All Cambodian workers admitted that they had crossed the border in a corridor in Ban Lem commune, Pong Nam Ron district, Chanthaburi province, and paid 3,000 baht per car to go to work in Samut Prakan province.
Currently, all Cambodian workers have been handed over by Thai police to professional officers to be interrogated in order to build a case for legal referrals related to illegal entry to work or stay in Thailand.
