The tomb of the king was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List in 1987. According to historians, Emperor Qin Shi was born in 259 BC and died in 210 BC.
Above the stupa is a replica of a natural forest, with peaks made of pearls, statues of cranes and cranes made of gold and silver. The roof of the stupa is designed as a replica of the sky, with the sun, moon and stars made of diamonds, glittering gems, as well as mechanical keys to attack any intruder. .
The stupa is full of statues of soldiers and horses made of clay, the size of a real statue, arranged in a procession around the cemetery in the same tactical way of war. In addition, there are diamonds, sapphires, gems, precious stones, skeletons of servants and skeletons of animals that are sacrificed. This huge stupa took at least 39 years to build and cost up to 720,000 workers.
The brutal story that is recorded is that at the funeral of Emperor Qin Xi, Prince Qin Xue, the second son, brought more than 10,000 concubines from Xianyang Palace to be buried alive to follow. Serve Emperor Qin Xi in the afterlife. The carpenter was also tricked into burying more than 3,000 people alive in a shrine to destroy evidence.
Although built in the late 3rd century BC, these statues were only discovered in 1974. In 1974, farmers in the Lintong area of Chang'an City, Shaanxi Province, China dug a well there and found the statues.
* About the death of the emperor:
Wanting to enjoy the immortality of the emperor, King Qin Xi ordered the scholars to seek the medicine of immortality, but as we all know, no human being can have immortality, as the saying goes. The phrase "change is immutable." At the end of the reign of King Qin Xi, he went to explore the forest in an area called Yun Mang to pray to the spirits of various dynasties.
Because he did his duty alone all day and night, he gradually became weaker and weaker at the age of only 49 years old. The king's only expectation was a life-long medicine to be able to continue his life in power, but no one could combine this medicine, and other medicines could not help him recover. Finally, this powerful emperor died on the streets.
