Murder! A village chief in Samaki Meanchey district, Kampong Chhnang province, had sex and then brutally burned a woman and was handcuffed by the military
(Kampong Chhnang): A suspect with the role of Kraing Kantrol village chief was arrested by the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Gendarmerie after being found to be involved in a case in which a woman died on the night of June 21, 2020 in A farm hut in Kraing Kantrol village, Peam commune, Samaki Meanchey district, Kampong Chhnang province.
Lieutenant General Hang Socheat, Deputy Commander of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Gendarmerie Command, told Fresh News on the evening of June 28, 2020 that the suspect arrested by the Gendarmerie was named Nhep Sokhom. 67 years old, chief of Kraing Kantrol village.
He said that under the order of Brigadier General Sak Sarang, Commander of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Gendarmerie, and under the coordination of the procedure from the representative of the Prosecutor General of the Gendarmerie, investigated the procedure and arrested the village chief, Mr. Nhep Sokhom. Taken for questioning on June 27, 2020.
It was not until June 28, 2020 that the suspect confessed that he, the suspect, and the victim had been in a relationship for five years. On the same day, there was an engagement ceremony in the village, and the woman also came to participate in the engagement ceremony.
After the engagement ceremony, the victim rode a motorbike to Sre Ni Cham Cham and called the suspect and met at about 12:37 noon on June 21, 2020 after meeting the suspect. And the victim was reconciled as usual, this time they had sex at a water buffalo pond about 30 meters from the hut where the woman's body was cremated.
The suspect is currently being investigated by the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Military Police and sent to court for further proceedings.
It should be reminded that: On the night of June 21, 2020, a woman was found dead in a hut guarding a plantation at Senni point in Kraing Kantrol village, Peam commune, Samaki Meanchey district, Kampong Chhnang province. A fire broke out in the upper part of the house without knowing the exact reason why the victim, Chea Thorn, 56 years old, lived in the commune where the incident took place, and her husband was blind on both sides.
