Today marks the 69th birthday of the Cambodian People's Party
Currently, the Cambodian People's Party has Samdech Techo Hun Sen as President, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Honorary President and accompanied by two Vice Presidents, Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum and Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, as well as members from all walks of life. Armed forces, traders, workers, laborers, a total of more than 6 million people.
Every year, the Cambodian People's Party always celebrates the birthday of Yang Maholarik. But this year, the major political party, which has the overwhelming support of the Cambodian people, did not celebrate its birthday to help curb the spread of Kovid 19.
It should be noted that the Cambodian People's Party, originally known as the Khmer Revolutionary People's Party, was founded on June 28, 1951, with its origins in the Cambodian people's resistance movement against the colonialists for national independence.
Since its inception, the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) has always adhered to its goals and ideals: standing by the people, connecting with the people, overcoming all obstacles, and daring to make unremitting sacrifices for Cambodia's independence, peace, freedom, democracy, neutrality and progress. Society.
The party that has built great achievements and merits for the nation and the people of Cambodia is the only political force that has stood up and mobilized all patriotic forces to form the United Front for National Salvation of Cambodia to inspire and lead the movement. People all over the country overthrew the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
The Cambodian People's Party is an important reference for building and developing the nation from the past, present and future. In the 41 years since the overthrow of the Pol Pot regime, in its role as the country's leading party, the Cambodian People's Party has achieved many historic achievements for the nation:
1. The Cambodian People's Party led the national liberation struggle from the genocidal regime on January 7, 1979 and prevented the return of this vicious regime, preventing the revival of the nation. .
2. The Cambodian People's Party has brought back the people the rights, freedoms, democracy, honor and dignity of the people who were completely lost during the Democratic Kampuchea regime.
3. The Cambodian People's Party has led the restoration and reconstruction of the socio-economy from zero, reviving and stabilizing all sectors step by step, which has laid the basic precedent for the restoration and development to date.
4: The Cambodian People's Party has been the core force in the process of national unification until the Paris Agreement on the political solution to the Cambodian problem of October 23, 1991 and is an indispensable support force in the successful implementation. Of this Agreement.
1. The Cambodian People's Party (CPP) has vigorously defended all achievements of the society, especially the Constitution, which is a noble achievement of the Paris Agreement, preventing the return of genocidal regimes, preventing acts of social unrest. Stabilized politics, security, social order and sustainability of all state institutions.
2. The Cambodian People's Party protects the legal property of the people, protects the career of civil servants and protects all investment contracts during the Cambodian state.
5. The Cambodian People's Party (CPP) has led the recovery and development of the economy for sustainable growth, achieving an average high growth rate of 9.4% from 1993-2008, ensuring poverty reduction and improving the well-being of the economy. Population and sustainability of natural resources and the environment, and have taken effective measures to address the impact of the international financial crisis.
6. The Cambodian People's Party has resolved border issues with neighboring countries peacefully, defending sovereignty, territorial integrity and national cultural heritage in the face of external aggression attempts.
* Major principles of the CPP political program:
The Cambodian People's Party strives to mobilize the entire Khmer nation, both at home and abroad, regardless of political affiliation, past beliefs, religions, national origins and social status. Strengthen political stability, security and public order to ensure the process of national development.
The Cambodian People's Party adheres to the policy of multi-party liberal democracy, strives to strengthen and expand democracy at the national, sub-national and local levels in line with the proposals of socio-economic development. Build Cambodia as a strong rule of law with an adequate legal system, comprehensive legal education, effective law enforcement and social justice. Prevent violations of the law, impunity, violence and all forms of discrimination.
The Cambodian People's Party respects all rights and freedoms of the people, promotes freedom of the press and expression, guarantees equality before the law for all people, and strengthens equity in accessing state, economic, social, cultural, educational, health and public services. Other. Strengthen cooperation between the state and civil society based on the rule of law.
The CPP continues to promote the implementation of in-depth and comprehensive state reforms, such as the reform of the armed forces, the reform of the law and the judiciary, and the reform of public financial management to ensure good governance at all levels. Promote the active participation of the people in the development process of the country in all fields.
The Cambodian People's Party adheres to the market economy system, strives to promote high and sustainable economic development, linked to equitable distribution of resources and sustainable management of the environment and natural resources. Promote the development of the private sector by considering the private sector as the engine of economic growth. Increase employment and expand employment for the people, strive to reduce the poverty rate by more than 1% per year.
The Cambodian People's Party strives to achieve the goal of "Education for All", linking education and training with development proposals. Promote the provision of effective, equitable and sustainable health services to the people. Strengthen the expansion of social services for the vulnerable to improve living conditions and create conditions for them to be connected with the currents of development.
Promote the role of the youth as a core force and a real force to continue the turn of society in the future. Increase education, training and vocational training in the job market, improve the moral education and health care of young people. Strive to include the needs of young people in development plans at all levels. Implement a step-by-step policy of rejuvenation in providing responsibilities at all levels.
* Policies for women
Nearly 700 Veterans, Retirees, the Disabled and Families of Victims in Prey Veng Province Receive Support for the 69th Anniversary of the Party
At the party headquarters of the nine communes, there were 674 veterans, retirees, the disabled and the families of the victims throughout Pearang district, focusing on five main topics:
1: Reasons for not organizing the celebration of the 69th anniversary of the founding of the Cambodian People's Party with Kovid-19 disease, based on the instructions of the Central Committee (C85) to participate in the prevention and control of the spread of the disease This.
2. The Cambodian People's Party is still grateful for the merits of the veterans, the Armed Forces, the retired civil servants, the disabled and the families of the victims who participated in the boycott for the benefit of the nation and the people in the past.
3. The problem of Kovid-19 is still a serious challenge of our world. Let all our people pay attention and listen to the guidance of the Royal Government and the guidelines of the Ministry of Health to know how to clean. Maintain a safe gap and live clean to help prevent this deadly disease.
4. All people must strive to increase animal husbandry to improve living standards while the country is fighting Kovid-19.
5. The working group of the local party in Pearang district must monitor the living conditions of the people and not allow any people who are in need of hunger while the Kovid-19 disease is spreading.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen made this statement in a message congratulating the 69th anniversary of the founding of the Cambodian People's Party on June 28, 2020.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated in his message, "I hope that with the active participation of all the people, we will be successful in the battle against Kovid-19."
Samdech Techo also called on party committees at all levels, party members and compatriots throughout the country to strictly implement the guidelines of the Royal Government and the Ministry of Health on measures to avoid infection. Kovid-19 to individuals and communities, as well as to maintain a normal life, production and employment of the people.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also stated that this year, as the national situation is facing major new difficulties caused by the global Kovid-19 epidemic in all countries, the Standing Committee of the Central Committee has decided to suspend the celebration. The party will mark its birthday this year to focus on efforts to address the aftermath of Kovid 19.
