Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng pays tribute to the body of Mr. Chak Leng, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, as well as the leaders of civil servants and the National Police of the Ministry of Interior, on Sunday morning, June 28, 2015. This year 2020, we pay our respects to the late Mr. Chak Leng, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, at the mortuary in Sangkat Chaktomuk, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh.
On this auspicious occasion, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, laid a wreath, incense and smiles to pay his respects to the body of Mr. Chak Leng and signed a condolence message to Ms. Khieu Hong and her group. Family.
In the condolence message, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, on behalf of his wife, as well as the leaders of civil servants and the National Police of the Ministry of Interior, expressed their deep sorrow and sadness over the death of Mr. Chak Leng. Former Secretary of State of the Council of Ministers and former Chief of Police of the Ministry of Interior, who is Khieu Hong's husband.
The Deputy Prime Minister continued that the death of Mr. Chak Leng was not only the loss of his beloved husband, father and grandfather, but also the loss of a senior official who had been actively involved with The Royal Government in the cause of serving the motherland, as well as sacrificing physical, intellectual, mental, tireless, participating in many social activities and humanitarian work to improve the lives of the people.
On behalf of the leaders, civil servants and the National Police of the Ministry of Interior, and on behalf of the Prince and his wife, expressed their condolences to her and her family, and wished the soul of Mr. Chak Leng a happy birthday. In death, do not be greedy.
In this sad atmosphere, Samdech Krala Hom, Deputy Prime Minister, also had a personal meeting and condolences with Ms. Khieu Hong and the descendants of Mr. Chak Leng and handed over the funeral rites. Ms. Khieu Hong as well. Joint Police Seize 30 Pieces of Wood Near Lum Village Corridor Station in O'Yadao District, Ratanakkiri Province
(Ratanakkiri): At 6:15 am on June 28, 2020, the joint police raided 30 pieces of mixed wood near the corridor of Lum village in Pak Nhay commune, O'Yadao district, Ratanakkiri province, which was intended for export. To Vietnam.
Joint forces include: National Gendarmerie, Provincial Economic Police, O'Yadao National Park rangers, Border Guard 623, O'Yadao District Police and O'Yadao District Local Armed Forces.
Brigadier General Nou Dara, Deputy Commissioner for Economic Crimes Planning, told Fresh News that the operation was directed by Provincial Governor Thong Savun and coordinated by Ratanakkiri Provincial Prosecutor Ngin Pech.
The Deputy General Commissioner continued that before reaching the crackdown on the above timber transportation, his force cooperated with the relevant law enforcement forces to search for the traders until the actual crackdown. They fled on a motorcycle after the force arrived, leaving only one motorcycle as evidence. However, the number of cubic meters above is not yet known because it has not been measured.
At present, 30 pieces of mixed wood exhibits and a motorbike have been kept at O'Yadao Forestry Administration Sangkat to find the owner of the tree and punish him according to the law.
