Ministry decides to study 38 road projects in Siem Reap in hopes of promoting the economy, beauty and tourism like Sihanoukville
(Siem Reap): The Royal Government of Cambodia, as well as the Ministry of Public Works and Transport of Siem Reap Province, have decided to study 38 infrastructure projects for the main road in Siem Reap with a total length of nearly 100 km to improve the public-transport sector. Travel of people, especially to support tourism in the province.
The decision on this important project that people always look forward to was made at a meeting at Siem Reap Provincial Hall chaired by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport and Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap Province on the 27th. June 2020.
The meeting was held to review and study 38 main road projects with a total length of 98.34 km, including two lanes with a length of 44 km and four lanes with a length of 54 km. The 12 communes of Siem Reap city and part of Bakong district are under the infrastructure development project in Siem Reap city.
These 38 Siem Reap Main Road Infrastructure Development Projects were studied in order to contribute to the economic development, the aesthetics of Siem Reap to be suitable as a cultural and historical tourism city, and to connect Siem Reap to the suburbs and Facilitate the travel of people and tourists in Siem Reap.
According to the Governor of Tea Seiha Province, Siem Reap is a province of tourism, culture and history, and the infrastructure of many roads needs to be repaired and improved. The heart of the province for the birth of the economy, tourism and beauty of the province.
He mentioned the work of repairing and improving 10 roads by Siem Reap Provincial Administration, including Ta Och Road, Neak Tep Road, Khnong Chunlong Road, Tong Seng Road, Atizan Road, Kork Srit Road, Sopitel Road, Provincial Tax Road, Kesor Kol Road and Svay Meas Road.
At the same time, the Senior Minister said that it is time to study the road infrastructure in Siem Reap to prepare a master plan to renovate Sihanoukville to be a suitable tourist city to enhance the country's image on the international stage through visitors. International tourism, and the Royal Government is studying to find sources of funding to implement the infrastructure project on the 38 main roads.
