(Prey Veng): Residents in Svay Chrum commune, Mesang district, Prey Veng province, claim that the Svay Chrum commune council withdrew between 20,000 and 40,000 riel from the government subsidy without confirmation. For no apparent reason, just "deduct fees". This withdrawal is different from the policy of the Royal Government.
Choeun Savoeun goes to pay for the family of his son who is working in Thailand. His three-member son received a subsidy from the government of about 176,000 riels.
Mr. Choeun Savoeun claimed that when he took the end of the sheet to verify the payment from Wing Specialized Bank, Svay Chrum commune council officials demanded between 20,000 and 40,000 riel from the villagers.
Mr. Choeun Savoeun claimed that after paying the money, the council officials handed over the verification card to open the money at Wing.
Another resident also claimed that Mrs. Channhong, a resident of Prey Chamkar village, Svay Chrum commune, Mesang district, told Fresh News that her family of five members received a subsidy from the Royal Government 22 40,000 Riels. She was also demanded 20,000 riel by commune officials before giving the end of the sheet to verify payment at Wing Specialized Bank.
Despite such deductions, Channhong did not express her condolences. She also expressed her happiness for the Royal Government's financial support now because it helped solve the difficulties in her life.
The commune chief added that in principle, the Royal Government does not require the deduction of money from the people, and he has already instructed his commune officials. The commune chief claims that he will go to inquire about this case.
Mr. Lahn Sareth said that in Svay Chrum commune, there are more than 600 families who have received subsidies from the Royal Government, and more than 300 families have come to get verification cards from Wing Bank.
