Montenegro (Declaration of Independence, June 3, 2006) Montenegro and Serbia were united as one nation after the fall of the Yugoslav Federation in 1991. In 2003, it became a union state of Serbia and Montenegro. By 2006, the Union State had split into two separate states.
In a referendum on May 21, 2006, 55.5 percent of Montenegrin's population voted in favor of declaring independence for Montenegro. As a result, Montenegro seceded and was officially recognized by the Serbian parliament. In June 2006, the United Nations welcomed Montenegro as its 192th member.
Serbia (Declaration of Independence, June 5, 2006) Two days after the declaration of independence of Montenegro, Serbia also declared itself a sovereign state, succeeding the Union of Serbia and Montenegro.
