Court finally decides to detain Seng Sovannara on charges of encroaching on dozens of hectares of state public land in Mondulkiri province
(Phnom Penh): Seng Sovannara, former Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Justice, has finally been remanded in custody on charges of encroaching on dozens of hectares of state land in Mondulkiri province, according to a spokesman for the prosecution. Phnom Penh, Kuch Kimlong told Fresh News.
Seng Sovannara's detention order was issued after a representative of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court decided to indict him in connection with a case of encroachment on dozens of hectares of public land in Mondulkiri province.
According to Mr. Kuch Kimlong, Mr. Seng Sovannara was charged with four counts of aggravated fraud, trespassing on state public property, threatening not to sue and illegal possession of a firearm. .
It should be informed that Mr. Seng Sovannara was arrested by the Internal Security Department of the General Commission of the National Police on the afternoon of June 26, 2020 yesterday when he went to clarify the case of encroachment on about 1,000 hectares of public land in Mondulkiri Province. .
It should be noted that Mr. Seng Sovannara was issued a Royal Decree by His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, terminating the position of Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Justice at the request of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on the 24th. August 2019.
He was also removed from the National Task Force to assist Mondulkiri by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior. It is noteworthy that the decision to remove Mr. Seng Sovannara from the National Assistance Team for Mondulkiri Province came after an incident involving the encroachment of about 1,000 hectares of state land in Andres Village, Or Buon Leu Commune, Koh Nhek District, Mondul Province. Kiri.
