Siem Reap Provincial Police Disseminate and Educate People on the Use of Uniforms to Avoid Mistakes
(Siem Reap): The Siem Reap Provincial Police Commissioner on June 26, 2020, educated and disseminated to the people about the proper use of uniforms in accordance with the law to avoid misleading the people.
This educational activity was conducted by Brigadier General Toch Sakal, Deputy Commissioner for Human Resource Planning, representing Major General Tith Narong, Siem Reap Provincial Police Commissioner.
On that occasion, Brigadier General Toch Sakal led a joint team of the Office of Personnel and the Office of Intervention and Sheriff to visit the people and advise on the use of people to avoid confusion with the National Police uniform in the pagoda. Kesararam is located in Sangkat Svay Dangkum, Siem Reap City.
It should be informed that this educational outreach started from a case in the past, when the joint police force organized order, then a guard took the car wheel lock at a gas station in Siem Reap city.
However, during the operation, the guards used the wrong uniform, wearing the uniform of a national police officer, which caused confusion. Later, the provincial police commission also issued an explanation and educated the people to protect.
Police Arrest Murderer in Stung Kambol, Kampong Thom Province
(Phnom Penh-Kampong Thom): The killer who stabbed his wife to death in a pool of blood on June 22 in Phnom Penh's Kambol district was arrested by the police on the night of June 26, 2020 in Po Ta village Un, Sangkat Srayov, Steung Sen City, Kampong Thom Province.
According to Fresh News, the operation was carried out by the Criminal Police Department in collaboration with the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and the Kampong Thom Provincial Police.
Preliminary information from the police confirmed that after the arrest, the assailant confessed that he stabbed his wife to death out of jealousy, and on the day of the incident, he stabbed his wife with a knife and died immediately in a pool of blood.
Authorities said that tonight, the Criminal Police Department is sending suspects to Phnom Penh to build a case for further proceedings.
