Prior to the assassination of President John F. Kennedy, US presidential cars often allowed the country's leaders to ride without much concealment. However, since then, the US presidential vehicle has been fitted with thicker shields and tighter closures to increase safety from generation to generation.
Donald Trump's "The Beast" worth $ 15 million was used for the first time during his visit to New York on September 24, 2018. Its features include a body covered with a protective layer of aluminum, ceramic and steel, 20 cm thick and 12 cm thick glass windows with 5 layers of penetration protection.
The US presidential raft typically has between 20 and nearly 50 vehicles, including multi-role vehicles, as well as cars that look like the president's car. When traveling abroad, "The Beast" and other escorts must also be airlifted for Tram's travels.
