Ministry of Information invites TV station representatives to a meeting to strengthen the correct use of the spelling of the names, roles, leadership and country names
(Phnom Penh): Seeing the comments, readings and writing of the presenters and readers of some TV stations, there is still a lack of misspellings, wrong names, wrong roles, etc. On the morning of June 26, In 2020, the Ministry of Information has invited representatives of all television stations in Cambodia to a meeting to strengthen those shortcomings.
Mr. Chum Kosal said that television is like a big school because it is watched by millions of people, so if we write misspellings or comments, misspellings, wrong names, wrong positions, especially names, leadership roles, etc. Will lead the audience, the listener also misunderstood, misspelled accordingly.
He also asked the leaders in charge of TV stations to help strengthen the teaching and guidance of the presenters, readers, news writers, to strive to strengthen the responsibility of their work to avoid. There are errors that will adversely affect the viewer.
He added that the presenter should be diligent in commenting on the new measures that the Royal Government has put in place, such as the current enforcement of traffic laws, driving to respect the law, prevention and prevention of Kovid-19 disease and so on.
In particular, some TV station representatives also mentioned the difficulties due to some presenters and writers, readers, their work knowledge is limited, some have less work experience, however, all TV station representatives will work hard to strengthen In addition to spelling, commenting, writing, reading and so on.
Finally, the presidium and all members of the meeting agreed to find common principles in writing, commenting, reading the names, roles, leadership status and country name to ask for the approval of the management for the use of a common standard.
