Kampot Governor Asks CRBC to Accelerate Construction of Urban Roads to Avoid Traffic Jams
(Kampot): Mr. Chiao Tai, Governor of Kampot Province, requested the CRBC Road Construction Company to expedite the construction of National Road No. 3 in Kampot City as soon as possible, seeing that the construction of National Road No. 3 from the point from Kampot City Railway to the fire. The traffic light at Samaki Market in Kampot is slow, causing congestion, making it difficult to travel and affecting the livelihood of the people living next to the road.
Mr. Chiao Tai made this request this morning, June 26, 2020, on the occasion that he led a team to inspect the construction site of National Road 3 from the railway in Kampot to the traffic light of Samaki Ti Market. Including Kampot province.
Mr. Chiao Tai said that the project to build National Road No. 3 from the traffic light at the intersection of Samaki Market, Kampot town to the railway is a 1,100-meter-long, 12.8-meter-thick, two-fiber-reinforced concrete road project. 4 Water to plant trees on both sides of the road, prepare corolla on both sides of the road, 2 meters long.
After a month of construction, the CRBC contractor seems to be struggling to find a way to speed up construction, leaving this busy road congested at the construction site almost every day. Eating of people living next to the road is also difficult.
At the same time, the provincial governor also proposed to the company three points, including:
* First: Please stop using hand-rolled cement, use long-hand cement, and during the day, prepare to install the steel wire in the evening, pour concrete until night * Second: Set a day to build a length of 100 meters on one size Side of the road or complete the construction of one side of the road in 10 days * 3: Please install a new drainage system along this concrete road.
