Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan recommends seven points to implement the anti-drug campaign plan more effectively
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan, Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, made seven recommendations to participate in the fight against drugs, especially the implementation of anti-drug campaign plans, as well as the implementation of village-commune-sangkat policies. It is safer for the Royal Government to operate more efficiently.
The recommendation of the President of the National Authority for Combating Drugs was made this morning, June 26, 2020, on the occasion that he presided over the burning of nearly 500 kilograms of drugs during the celebration. Celebrate the International Day Against Drug Abuse on June 26, 2020.
The seven recommendations of Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan are as follows:
First, pay close attention to personal hygiene, family, community and workplace in accordance with the guidelines of the Ministry of Health and the World Health Organization, and also do not neglect the drug.
Second: Civil servants of all types of law enforcement forces must take care and take care of themselves to participate in the fight against Kovid-19 by preventing themselves from becoming infected and preventing the spread of the disease into the workplace, especially the treatment area. And rehabilitation of drug addicts and prisons.
Third, all Capital-Provincial Drug Control Committees must continue to pay attention to the effective implementation of Regulation No. 01 on the strengthening of anti-drug measures and the policy of "safe villages, communes", village and commune strategic policies. / Sangkat Sar No Drug as well as other plans and measures of the Royal Government.
Fourth, all relevant ministries, institutions, units and sub-national authorities must support and inspire all local social components to participate in the movement to treat and rehabilitate drug addicts in the community successfully. Reassuring families and drug users is the task that leads to successful rehabilitation treatment.
Successful rehabilitation treatment leads to a successful reduction of local and community drug demand and a reduction in drug supply and marketing. In the circumstances of the Kovid-19 crisis, it is recommended that all treatment and rehabilitation centers for drug addicts, both public and private, must strictly and strictly follow the guidelines of the Ministry of Health to prevent infections and outbreaks. The Kovid-19 is in its constituency and in the community.
Sixth, as we will see soon, many drugs will be burned, which is a message to drug criminals to see the strong will of the Royal Government of Cambodia to crack down on drugs. Not only will drug seizures be eradicated, but our law enforcement officers will continue to seek the resources of those criminals to seize and sever the mechanisms that serve illegal activities in society.
