Health minister calls on people to continue implementing measures to prevent Kovid-19 virus as the disease reaches nearly 10 million worldwide
(Phnom Penh): Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, on the evening of June 25, 2020, once again reminded and called on all people to continue to implement measures to prevent the transmission of Kovid-19 virus. Tightened to prevent Kovid-19 disease, which can lead to death.
According to a report by the World Health Organization on June 24, 2020, the number of cases of Kovid-19 has risen to nearly 10 million and the death toll has risen to nearly half a million.
Secretary of State O Vandin, spokeswoman for the Ministry of Health, told Fresh News this evening that the death toll was largely due to the severity of the Kovid-19 virus in the respiratory tract of patients. This causes the patient to have difficulty breathing, shortness of breath, seeking help to breathe and leading to inability to breathe on their own and suffocation and death.
