As of March 2020, the United States will provide about $ 11 million in grant funding for Cambodia's emergency response to Kovid 19.
(Phnom Penh): Since March 2020, the United States has provided approximately $ 11 million in grant funding to support the Royal Government of Cambodia's Emergency Response Plan for Kovid-19. This is according to the joint declaration on the signing of the amendment agreement on development cooperation financing for 2019, which was received by Fresh News on the night of June 25.
According to the statement, the funding will be used to alleviate both the immediate medical response to Kovi 5-19 in the Cambodian health system and the effects of infectious diseases, with a focus on economic recovery. By environment and equity.
In addition, the United States Government provides support to civil society organizations that focus on human rights, anti-trafficking, and accountability and transparency in Cambodia. These efforts complement our work with the Royal Government in supporting sustainable and environmental development in Cambodia.
From 1994 to the present, the US government has provided more than $ 1 billion in support to Cambodia. This is according to the press release.
The following is the report of the Ministry of Health: Farmers and local officials in Banteay Meanchey province ask for donations to build a community concrete bridge in Thmar Puok district
(Banteay Meanchey): Farmers and local officials called for donations of funds and resources to continue the construction of a community concrete bridge at the dry nest spot of Ta Son Dam near Anlong Laok of Thmor Puok River in Treas Village, Kork Kathin Commune, Thmor Puok District, Banteay Meanchey Province.
They made this request when officials, including Ms. Vounum Sophorn, Member of Parliament for Banteay Meanchey, Mr. Ly Sary, Deputy Governor of Banteay Meanchey, Mr. Diep Chhuon, Governor of Thmor Puok District, and officials visited the site and visited the workers and Mr. Nong Bun Chi, Kork Kathin commune chief, who was building the concrete bridge on June 24, 2020.
They requested the competent authorities, philanthropists, especially dignitaries, leaders to contribute to provide financial support for the construction of this bridge.
The above officials encouraged and supported this project of the community and on that occasion raised some money to support the purchase of food for the group of craftsmen and people involved in the construction.
Mr. Ven Sam Oun, Superintendent of Yi Saren Construction Company, and Mr. Khon Tha, construction site, said that the bridge was built on the 4.5 km long Tason Dam, which runs from Kork Kathin Village, Treas Village to Phnom Preah, which people use for construction. Transportation and transportation of rice, cassava.
In that, Venerable Bun Boeun Kong at Wat Pali Ley USA donated $ 400. Other than that, it is a fundraiser from the people in the community. He said the bridge needed about $ 10,000 to complete. That is, it still lacks a lot. And now construction is in full swing ahead of the heavy rains that can no longer be done.
