According to the announcement of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, which was published by Fresh News on June 25, 2020, the allowance will be paid in KHR and depends on the number of days of suspension. Employment contracts include:
In order to avoid the difficulty of reimbursing the Royal Government in the event that factories apply for employment before the end of the contract period, the allowance will be divided into two parts for those who have suspended the contract. Work from 21 days to 1 month and will be divided into 8 times for those who are suspended, also promised work for 2 months, each time equal to the budget of 81,000 Riels ($ 20).
The Ministry would like to remind you that Wing Specialized Bank will return this subsidy to the Royal Government if you fail to pay this allowance within 10 days after receiving the phone message from Wing Specialized Bank. To pay this allowance, you need to bring your Cambodian ID card and the phone number that received the message to the nearest Wing agent.
Please note that you are not required to pay a service fee to Wing agents when paying this allowance.
Two men who cheated to transport steel and were arrested by the depot owner were allowed to return home by the prosecutor's office
(Kandal): Deputy Prosecutor So Sovitya of Kandal Provincial Court has ordered Sieb Dina and Koy Kosal to return home after they were tricked into taking a car to transport steel to an unidentified person who called. The phone was already handcuffed by the depot owner to the authorities.
According to the report of the Kandal Provincial Police, the metal was handed over to the victim for use, and the vehicle as a means of action and two mobile phones related to the crime were kept at the district police inspectorate for further investigation.
The owner of the phone number said to let the car go, I crossed the ferry to Svay Chrum commune, and then Sieb Dina drove out of the truck. Arriving in Bak Kheng commune, Chroy Changva district, Hang Norak Theara stopped Sieb Dina from driving a steel truck back to Prek Takov commune.
At that time, the owner of the depot also complained to the Prek Takov police to arrest the two men, while the owner of the phone number 096 3 703 236 hung up the phone and could not be found to pay the bill.
According to relatives, if both of them were involved in the crime, they would not return at the call of the depot owner, they would have found a place to hide to hide the metal, so please the provincial governor And the commissioner helped bring justice to both of them.
