Thirteen suspects were arrested by the Phnom Penh Military Police in connection with drug cases
(Phnom Penh): The specialized officers of the Office of Drug Crime Investigation of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie, in cooperation with some local military forces, on June 24, 2020, arrested 13 suspects in 5 different cases in a row. Like the early rains involved drug trafficking and illegal use.
The four drug cases include:
Case 3: At 18:40 on June 24, 2020, the Chroy Changvar District Military Patrol Force arrested 4 suspects in connection with a case of illegal drug use at National Road 6A in Chambok Village. Meas, Sangkat Bak Kheng, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh.
Case 4: At 14:30 on June 24, 2020, the Prek Pnov Military Patrol Force ambushed and arrested 2 suspects in connection with a case of illegal drug use at the national road. No. 5 in front of Sokimex Gas Station, Po Mongkul Village, Sangkat Prek Pnov, Khan Prek Pnov, Phnom Penh.
The two suspects: First name: Khieu Visal, male, 19 years old, occupation: construction worker, living in Taeng Kansomak village, Kampong Trabek district, Prey Veng province, second name: Rith Daro, male, 23 years old, occupation: construction worker, living in Kampong Thom village, Kirivon commune, Santuk district. Kampong Thom Province.
Case 5: At 2:50 AM on June 25, 2020, the Chamkar Mon District Military Patrol Force arrested a suspect in connection with a case of illegal drug use at a water pumping station. Street 271, Sangkat Phsar Doeum Thkov, Khan Chamkarmon.
The suspect is named Diep Veasna, male, 26 years old, living in a rented house with no number, Lum Road, Tuol Rokar Village, Sangkat Chak Angre Krom, Khan Meanchey.
The 13 suspects are currently being interrogated by the Phnom Penh Office for the Suppression of Drug Offenses and are building a case to be sent to court for legal proceedings.
10 New Houses Donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to 10 Veterans Families in Leuk Dek District, Kandal Province
(Kandal): Mr. Chap Chanvithya, Governor of Leuk Dek District and Honorary President of the Cambodian Veterans Association of Leuk Dek District, Kandal Province, on June 25, 2020, led a working group to visit and hand over 10 new houses as a gift. Precious words of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association to 10 families of Cambodian Veterans in Leuk Dek District, Kandal Province.
Mr. Chap Chanvithya said that the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has always taken care of all people and veterans are also among those who need to take care of support, while the gift of this house really reflects To see the noble merits of Samdech Techo who took care to help veterans.
The district governor added, "Our country is rich, happy, prosperous, prosperous, known for its progress, and especially the value of peace, nothing can come at the expense of our territorial integrity."
